window.STUDY_SUPPLEMENT = {"notes":{"01":[{"zh":"制片方法怎么选","en":"Choosing a preparation","bodyZh":"石蜡切片适合观察常规组织结构。冷冻切片有利于保留部分脂质和酶活性。观察血细胞用涂片，观察疏松结缔组织纤维可用铺片，观察骨单位的矿化结构可用骨磨片。","bodyEn":"Use paraffin sections for routine architecture, frozen sections for selected lipids or enzyme activity, smears for blood cells, spreads for loose connective tissue, and ground sections for mineralized bone.","pages":"5–6"},{"zh":"检测对象决定方法","en":"Choosing a staining or detection method","bodyZh":"PAS 标记多种富含糖的结构，Feulgen 反应显示 DNA。免疫组织化学用抗体定位蛋白抗原，原位杂交用互补探针定位核酸序列。用酶组织化学观察组织中的酶活性。","bodyEn":"PAS demonstrates carbohydrate-rich structures. The Feulgen reaction demonstrates DNA. Immunohistochemistry detects antigens with antibodies, in situ hybridization detects nucleic acid sequences, and enzyme histochemistry demonstrates enzyme activity.","pages":"7–18"},{"zh":"观察方法、分辨率与切面","en":"Resolution and section orientation","bodyZh":"TEM 观察内部超微结构，SEM 看表面立体形态。分辨率决定能否分开相邻结构；单纯放大不会增加细节。同一根管纵切像通道，横切像圆环，复核题图时先找腔和边界。","bodyEn":"TEM shows internal ultrastructure and SEM shows surface topography. Resolution is the ability to distinguish nearby points. Identify the lumen and boundaries before interpreting a longitudinal or transverse profile.","pages":"7–12、21–22"}],"02":[{"zh":"浆液性、黏液性和混合性腺泡","en":"Serous, mucous, and mixed acini","bodyZh":"浆液性细胞基底嗜碱，核较圆，顶端可见分泌颗粒。黏液性细胞胞质较淡，核扁并偏基底。混合腺泡可见浆半月；肌上皮细胞位于腺上皮与基膜之间，收缩帮助排出分泌物。","bodyEn":"Serous cells have basal basophilia, round nuclei, and apical secretory granules. Mucous cells are pale with flattened basal nuclei. Mixed acini may show serous demilunes. Myoepithelial cells contract to aid secretion.","pages":"28–32"},{"zh":"微绒毛、动纤毛与静纤毛","en":"Microvilli, motile cilia, and stereocilia","bodyZh":"微绒毛靠肌动蛋白芯支持，形成纹状缘或刷状缘；动纤毛有典型 9+2 微管轴丝和基体；附睾静纤毛是长微绒毛。光镜先比长短和整齐度，电镜再看内部骨架。","bodyEn":"Microvilli contain actin and form a striated or brush border. Motile cilia contain a typical 9+2 axoneme and arise from basal bodies. Epididymal stereocilia are elongated microvilli.","pages":"32–35"},{"zh":"连接与基膜的位置关系","en":"Junctions and basement membrane","bodyZh":"紧密连接封闭细胞间通路，黏着带连肌动蛋白，桥粒连中间丝，缝隙连接传递小分子和离子。半桥粒把上皮细胞固定于基板。基板富含 IV 型胶原和层粘连蛋白，VII 型胶原参与锚定。","bodyEn":"Tight junctions seal, adherens junctions link actin, desmosomes link intermediate filaments, and gap junctions permit intercellular communication. Hemidesmosomes anchor epithelium to the basal lamina.","pages":"34–37"}],"03":[{"zh":"巨噬细胞和肥大细胞的过程题","en":"Macrophage and mast cell mechanisms","bodyZh":"巨噬细胞识别并摄取颗粒，吞噬体与溶酶体融合后消化。Ⅰ型超敏反应中，肥大细胞先结合特异性 IgE，再暴露时抗原交联 IgE，引起脱颗粒。","bodyEn":"Macrophages digest ingested material after phagosome–lysosome fusion. Re-exposure to antigen can cross-link receptor-bound IgE and trigger mast cell degranulation.","pages":"40–45"},{"zh":"按分泌物归类细胞","en":"Group cells by what they secrete","bodyZh":"成纤维细胞合成纤维与基质，浆细胞分泌抗体，肥大细胞释放炎症介质。白色脂肪细胞还分泌瘦素、脂联素等信号分子。看到浆细胞先找偏心核、车轮状染色质和核旁浅染区。","bodyEn":"Fibroblasts produce extracellular matrix, plasma cells secrete antibodies, and mast cells release inflammatory mediators. White adipocytes also release adipokines. Look for an eccentric clock-face nucleus and a pale Golgi region in plasma cells.","pages":"40–45、51"},{"zh":"三种纤维的形态与染色","en":"Recognizing the three fiber types","bodyZh":"胶原纤维粗、成束、HE 嗜酸。弹性纤维较细、可分支，特殊弹性染色更清楚。网状纤维由 III 型胶原构成，银染呈细网。第 4 版写胶原原纤维周期约 67 nm，课件部分材料写约 64 nm，答题按题源。","bodyEn":"Collagen fibers form thick eosinophilic bundles. Elastic fibers branch and are clearer with elastic stains. Reticular fibers contain type III collagen and form silver-stained networks. Use the stated reference for numerical conventions.","pages":"46–50"}],"04":[{"zh":"软骨单位与关节软骨","en":"Chondron and articular cartilage","bodyZh":"软骨单位包括软骨细胞及其细胞周基质。看透明软骨先找陷窝、同源细胞群及较深染的领地基质。关节软骨可分表层、移行层、深层和钙化层，潮标位于深层未钙化区与钙化区之间。","bodyEn":"A chondron comprises a chondrocyte and its pericellular matrix. In hyaline cartilage, find lacunae, isogenous groups, and territorial matrix. The tidemark separates uncalcified from calcified articular cartilage.","pages":"53–56"},{"zh":"五类骨相关细胞","en":"Five bone-associated cell categories","bodyZh":"人卫第 4 版单列骨被覆细胞。成骨细胞沿骨表面排成一列，分泌类骨质；成熟骨细胞位于陷窝；破骨细胞为贴骨表面的多核大细胞，常位于吸收陷窝。RANKL 促进破骨细胞形成，OPG 能结合 RANKL。","bodyEn":"The fourth edition also lists bone-lining cells. Osteoblasts form osteoid at bone surfaces, osteocytes occupy lacunae, and multinucleated osteoclasts resorb bone at resorption bays. RANKL supports osteoclast differentiation and OPG acts as a decoy receptor.","pages":"58–61"},{"zh":"软骨内成骨的空间顺序","en":"Endochondral ossification in section","bodyZh":"沿骺端向骨干端依次找静止、增殖、成熟与肥大、钙化及成骨区域。先根据柱状排列和陷窝大小定位，再核对深处过渡性骨小梁。骨领最初在骨干周围由膜内成骨形成。","bodyEn":"From epiphysis toward diaphysis, follow resting, proliferating, maturing and hypertrophic, calcified, and ossification zones. Cell columns and enlarging lacunae are landmarks. The bony collar initially forms by intramembranous ossification.","pages":"64–68"}],"05":[{"zh":"红肌纤维、白肌纤维和中间型","en":"Red, white, and intermediate fibers","bodyZh":"红纤维肌红蛋白和线粒体较多，偏慢缩、氧化供能，耐疲劳；白纤维偏快缩、糖酵解供能，较易疲劳；另有中间型。遇到现代 I、IIA、IIX 型命名时注意分类依据。","bodyEn":"Red fibers have abundant myoglobin and mitochondria and are typically slow, oxidative, and fatigue-resistant. White fibers are typically fast and more glycolytic. Intermediate fibers are also described.","pages":"87–88"},{"zh":"从肌节到钙调节","en":"Sarcomere and calcium control","bodyZh":"肌节是两条 Z 线之间。收缩时 I 带和 H 带缩小，A 带长度基本稳定。骨骼肌三联体含一个横小管和两个终池。Ca²⁺结合肌钙蛋白 C，ATP 与肌球蛋白结合使其和肌动蛋白解离。","bodyEn":"A sarcomere extends from Z line to Z line. During shortening, the I band and H zone narrow while the A band stays essentially constant. A triad contains a T tubule and two terminal cisternae.","pages":"83–89"},{"zh":"心肌与平滑肌的高倍线索","en":"Cardiac and smooth muscle landmarks","bodyZh":"心肌多见中央核、分支与闰盘，二联体是一个横小管与一个终池。平滑肌无横纹，靠密体锚定肌丝，膜小凹参与信号和钙调节；心肌间质纤维位于细胞外，闰盘连接相邻心肌细胞。","bodyEn":"Cardiac muscle shows central nuclei, branching, and intercalated discs. A diad has one T tubule and one terminal cisterna. Smooth muscle lacks striations and anchors filaments at dense bodies.","pages":"89–93"}],"06":[{"zh":"血涂片按核形和颗粒判读","en":"Identify leukocytes by nuclei and granules","bodyZh":"中性粒细胞看分叶核，嗜酸性粒细胞看常见双叶核与粗红颗粒，嗜碱性粒细胞看深紫颗粒。单核细胞较大、核常肾形或折叠，淋巴细胞常圆核深染、胞质窄。带状核中性粒细胞可先看颗粒和成熟阶段。","bodyEn":"Use nuclear shape and granules together. Neutrophils often have segmented nuclei, eosinophils coarse red granules and bilobed nuclei, and basophils dark granules. Monocytes have indented nuclei, and small lymphocytes have scant cytoplasm.","pages":"70–75"},{"zh":"红细胞膜骨架与血小板颗粒","en":"Erythrocyte skeleton and platelet granules","bodyZh":"血影主要保留红细胞膜及膜骨架，spectrin 参与维持形状。血小板 α 颗粒富含蛋白，致密颗粒储存 ADP、Ca²⁺等小分子；开放小管系统与细胞表面相通，致密小管系统参与储钙。","bodyEn":"Spectrin supports erythrocyte shape. Platelet alpha granules contain proteins, dense granules store small molecules such as ADP and calcium, and the dense tubular system stores calcium.","pages":"72、75–76"},{"zh":"骨髓–血屏障与造血谱系","en":"Marrow–blood barrier and lineages","bodyZh":"先分造血索和骨髓血窦。教材强调新生血细胞可经窦内皮临时穿胞孔入血。造血干细胞兼有长期自我更新和多系分化潜能，祖细胞则逐渐定向。巨核细胞常有单个高度分叶的多倍体核。","bodyEn":"Distinguish hematopoietic cords from marrow sinusoids. New blood cells can cross temporary transcellular pores in sinusoidal endothelium. HSCs self-renew and generate multiple lineages. Megakaryocytes have a multilobed polyploid nucleus.","pages":"77–82"}],"07":[{"zh":"轴丘、突触前膜和突触后膜","en":"Axon hillock and synaptic polarity","bodyZh":"尼氏体位于胞体和树突，轴丘缺乏尼氏体。识别典型化学突触时先找含成簇小泡的突触前终末，再找突触间隙和突触后致密物。核仁在核内，尼氏体在胞质。","bodyEn":"Nissl substance lies in the soma and dendrites and is absent from the axon hillock. Identify a chemical synapse by presynaptic vesicles, a synaptic cleft, and postsynaptic density.","pages":"96–102"},{"zh":"髓鞘、胶质与被膜","en":"Myelin, glia, and nerve sheaths","bodyZh":"少突胶质细胞可为多个中枢轴突节段形成髓鞘，一个施万细胞形成一段周围髓鞘。髓鞘节段之间为朗飞结；施万细胞髓鞘内可见施密特–兰特曼切迹。神经束膜有紧密连接，分隔单个神经束。","bodyEn":"Oligodendrocytes myelinate multiple CNS internodes. Each Schwann cell myelinates one PNS internode. Nodes interrupt myelin, and Schmidt–Lanterman clefts occur within PNS myelin. Perineurium encloses nerve fascicles.","pages":"102–110"},{"zh":"神经肌接头与血脑屏障填图","en":"Neuromuscular junction and BBB labeling","bodyZh":"神经肌接头沿轴突终末、间隙、终板皱褶定位；终板有烟碱型乙酰胆碱受体。血脑屏障关键在内皮紧密连接，周细胞、基膜和星形胶质足突参与维持；血–脑脊液屏障的紧密连接位于脉络丛上皮。","bodyEn":"Locate the motor terminal, synaptic cleft, and junctional folds. In the BBB, endothelial tight junctions are the physical seal, supported by pericytes, basal lamina, and astrocyte endfeet.","pages":"113–115、125–126"}],"08":[{"zh":"动静脉和三类毛细血管","en":"Vessel walls and capillary types","bodyZh":"动静脉比较壁厚、腔形和哪层占优势。连续型内皮完整，常靠小泡转运；有孔型可见窗孔；血窦腔较宽，可有内皮间隙，基膜特征随器官而异。窗孔属于单个内皮细胞，可与细胞之间的间隙区分。","bodyEn":"Compare the relative wall thickness, lumen, and dominant tunic. Continuous capillaries have uninterrupted endothelium, fenestrated capillaries have endothelial pores, and sinusoidal profiles vary by organ.","pages":"129–137"},{"zh":"微循环三条路线","en":"Three routes through the microcirculation","bodyZh":"迂回通路经过真毛细血管网，主要用于物质交换。直捷通路经过通血毛细血管，利于血液快速通过。动静脉吻合可绕过毛细血管网，皮肤内有助于体温调节。","bodyEn":"The exchange route passes through true capillaries. The thoroughfare route allows more direct flow. An arteriovenous anastomosis bypasses the capillary bed and can aid thermoregulation.","pages":"137–139"},{"zh":"浦肯野纤维、心瓣膜和淋巴管","en":"Purkinje fibers, valves, and lymphatics","bodyZh":"浦肯野纤维常位于心内膜下，细胞大而浅染、糖原多、肌原纤维偏周边。心瓣膜以结缔组织为核心，表面覆内皮。毛细淋巴管盲端起始，内皮有重叠瓣样边缘。","bodyEn":"Subendocardial Purkinje cells are large and pale with abundant glycogen and peripheral myofibrils. Heart valves have a connective tissue core covered by endothelium. Initial lymphatics begin blindly.","pages":"140–142"}],"09":[{"zh":"滤泡反应与抗原识别","en":"Follicular responses and antigen recognition","bodyZh":"普通树突状细胞把加工后的肽呈递给 T 细胞；滤泡树突状细胞保留天然抗原供 B 细胞识别。生发中心暗区富含增殖的中心母细胞，明区发生抗原依赖的选择。","bodyEn":"Conventional dendritic cells present processed peptides to T cells. Follicular dendritic cells retain native antigen for B cells. Centroblasts proliferate in the dark zone, and selection occurs in the light zone.","pages":"143–147"},{"zh":"胸腺皮质的血–胸腺屏障","en":"The cortical blood–thymus barrier","bodyZh":"由血侧向外复述五层：连续毛细血管内皮、内皮基膜、血管周围结缔组织、上皮性网状细胞基膜、上皮性网状细胞层。胸腺小体在髓质，胸腺皮质看密集胸腺细胞。","bodyEn":"From the lumen outward: continuous endothelium, endothelial basal lamina, perivascular connective tissue, epithelial reticular cell basal lamina, and epithelial reticular cells. Hassall corpuscles are medullary.","pages":"148–149"},{"zh":"淋巴结与脾的流向","en":"Flow through lymph node and spleen","bodyZh":"淋巴结从输入淋巴管进入被膜下窦，经过小梁周窦和髓窦，从门部输出。脾以中央小动脉定位白髓，周围淋巴鞘为 T 区，滤泡为 B 区；红髓由脾索和脾血窦组成，参与血液过滤。","bodyEn":"Lymph enters a node via afferent vessels and passes through subcapsular, trabecular, and medullary sinuses. In the spleen, locate the central arteriole, the T-cell PALS, B-cell follicles, and the red pulp cords and sinusoids.","pages":"150–155"},{"zh":"扁桃体与淋巴结的区分","en":"Tonsil versus lymph node in section","bodyZh":"腭扁桃体表面的复层扁平上皮向内折成隐窝，隐窝旁可见滤泡。淋巴结先找结缔组织被膜、被膜下窦与皮髓分区。题干问到不同类型扁桃体时，分别核对上皮和隐窝。","bodyEn":"Palatine tonsil has stratified squamous epithelium, crypts, and adjacent lymphoid follicles. A lymph node shows a capsule, subcapsular sinus, and cortical–medullary organization.","pages":"155–156"}]},"definitions":[{"chapter":"01","term":"Histology","zhTerm":"组织学","zh":"研究细胞、组织和器官微细结构及其与功能关系的科学。","en":"Histology is the study of the microscopic structure of cells, tissues and organs and its relationship to function."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Basophilia","zhTerm":"嗜碱性","zh":"组织成分对碱性染色体系的亲和性，通常呈蓝色或紫蓝色；核酸和核糖体丰富的结构常具有此性质。","en":"Basophilia is the affinity of tissue components for basic dyes, usually producing blue or purple staining. It is typical of structures rich in DNA or RNA."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Acidophilia / eosinophilia","zhTerm":"嗜酸性","zh":"组织成分对酸性染料的亲和性，在H&E中常表现为伊红染成粉红色或红色。","en":"Acidophilia is the affinity of tissue components for acidic dyes. In H&E staining, eosin stains many protein-rich structures pink or red."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Euchromatin","zhTerm":"常染色质","zh":"相对疏松、浅染的染色质，通常与较活跃的转录有关。","en":"Euchromatin is relatively dispersed, lightly staining chromatin that is generally associated with active transcription."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Heterochromatin","zhTerm":"异染色质","zh":"较凝集、深染、通常转录较不活跃的染色质。","en":"Heterochromatin is condensed, dark-staining chromatin that is generally less transcriptionally active."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Epithelium","zhTerm":"上皮","zh":"由紧密排列的细胞和少量细胞外基质构成的组织，覆盖体表、衬器官腔面或形成腺体。","en":"Epithelium is tissue composed of closely packed cells with little extracellular matrix. It covers surfaces, lines cavities and forms glands."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Endothelium","zhTerm":"内皮","zh":"衬于心血管和淋巴管腔面的单层扁平上皮。","en":"Endothelium is the simple squamous epithelium lining the heart and the lumens of blood and lymphatic vessels."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Mesothelium","zhTerm":"间皮","zh":"覆盖胸膜、心包膜、腹膜等浆膜表面的单层扁平上皮，有利于脏器滑动。","en":"Mesothelium is the simple squamous epithelium covering serosal surfaces such as the pleura, pericardium and peritoneum. It facilitates movement of the viscera."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Microvillus","zhTerm":"微绒毛","zh":"细胞游离面短而细、含肌动蛋白微丝的胞质突起，增大吸收表面积。","en":"A microvillus is a short apical cytoplasmic projection supported by actin filaments. Microvilli increase the surface area for absorption."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Motile cilium","zhTerm":"运动纤毛","zh":"细胞表面较长、可运动的突起，典型轴丝含9+2微管排列，通过摆动推动表面液体或黏液。","en":"A motile cilium is a long cell-surface projection with a typical 9+2 microtubular axoneme. Coordinated beating moves fluid or mucus along the surface."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Tight junction","zhTerm":"紧密连接","zh":"相邻细胞之间靠近顶端的带状封闭连接，限制细胞旁通路，并参与维持细胞极性。","en":"A tight junction is a belt-like junction near the apical region of adjacent cells. It restricts paracellular passage and helps maintain epithelial polarity."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Gap junction","zhTerm":"缝隙连接","zh":"相邻细胞通过连接子对接形成的通道性连接，可直接交换离子和小分子。每个连接子由六个连接蛋白亚基组成。","en":"A gap junction is a communicating junction in which paired connexons form channels between adjacent cells, allowing ions and small molecules to pass directly. Each connexon consists of six connexin subunits."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Junctional complex","zhTerm":"连接复合体","zh":"同一细胞侧面两种或以上细胞连接组合而成的结构。","en":"A junctional complex is an association of two or more types of intercellular junctions along the lateral surface of epithelial cells."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Basement membrane","zhTerm":"基膜","zh":"位于上皮基底面与下方结缔组织之间的特化细胞外薄层，课程按基板和网板组成理解，具有支持、附着及选择性通透作用。","en":"A basement membrane is a specialized extracellular layer at the basal surface of epithelium. It comprises a basal lamina and a reticular lamina and provides support, attachment and selective permeability."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Basal plasma membrane infoldings","zhTerm":"基底部质膜内褶","zh":"细胞基底部质膜向胞质内形成的褶皱，褶间常有线粒体，可增加膜表面积并支持离子和水运输。","en":"Basal plasma membrane infoldings are invaginations of the basal cell membrane, often associated with mitochondria. They increase membrane surface area for ion and water transport."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Glandular epithelium","zhTerm":"腺上皮","zh":"以合成和分泌物质为主要特征的上皮组织，是腺体的主要组成部分。","en":"Glandular epithelium is epithelium specialized for the synthesis and secretion of substances. It forms the secretory component of glands."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Mesenchyme","zhTerm":"间充质","zh":"由未充分分化的间充质细胞及丰富胶状细胞外基质构成的胚胎性结缔组织。","en":"Mesenchyme is embryonic connective tissue composed of undifferentiated mesenchymal cells in an abundant extracellular ground substance."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Molecular sieve","zhTerm":"分子筛","zh":"基质中由透明质酸与蛋白聚糖聚集体等形成的水合网络，允许物质扩散并限制某些大颗粒通过。","en":"The molecular sieve is a hydrated network of hyaluronan and proteoglycan aggregates in the ground substance. It permits diffusion and restricts the passage of some large particles."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Fibroblast","zhTerm":"成纤维细胞","zh":"固有结缔组织的重要常驻细胞，合成细胞外基质的纤维及基质成分。","en":"A fibroblast is a principal resident cell of connective tissue that synthesizes fibers and ground substance of the extracellular matrix."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Macrophage","zhTerm":"巨噬细胞","zh":"具有吞噬清除能力的细胞，去除微生物、细胞碎片和衰老细胞，并参与抗原呈递及免疫调节。","en":"A macrophage is a phagocytic cell that removes microorganisms and cellular debris and participates in antigen presentation and immune regulation."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Plasma cell","zhTerm":"浆细胞","zh":"由活化B淋巴细胞分化、分泌抗体的细胞，典型有偏心车轮状核、嗜碱性胞质及核旁浅染区。","en":"A plasma cell is an antibody-secreting cell derived from an activated B lymphocyte. It has an eccentric nucleus, basophilic cytoplasm and a pale perinuclear Golgi region."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Mast cell","zhTerm":"肥大细胞","zh":"结缔组织中富含分泌颗粒的细胞，可释放组胺等介质，参与过敏及炎症反应。","en":"A mast cell is a granule-rich connective tissue cell that releases histamine and other mediators in allergic and inflammatory reactions."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Collagenous fiber / white fiber","zhTerm":"胶原纤维／白纤维","zh":"由胶原原纤维成束形成的细胞外纤维，粗胶原束主要为Ⅰ型胶原，提供较高抗拉强度。","en":"A collagenous fiber, also called a white fiber, is a bundle of collagen fibrils that provides tensile strength to connective tissue. Coarse collagen bundles are composed mainly of type I collagen."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Elastic fiber / yellow fiber","zhTerm":"弹性纤维／黄纤维","zh":"由弹性蛋白核心和周围微原纤维构成的细胞外纤维，使组织伸展后回缩。","en":"An elastic fiber, also called a yellow fiber, contains an elastin core associated with microfibrils. It allows tissues to stretch and return toward their original shape."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Reticular fiber / argyrophilic fiber","zhTerm":"网状纤维／嗜银纤维","zh":"主要由Ⅲ型胶原形成的细分支纤维，可银染成黑色，为多种组织提供精细支持网架。","en":"A reticular fiber is a delicate, branching fiber composed mainly of type III collagen. It is argyrophilic and forms a supporting network in many tissues."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Isogenous group","zhTerm":"同源细胞群","zh":"由同一个软骨细胞分裂形成、在基质中相邻聚集的一组软骨细胞。","en":"An isogenous group is a cluster of chondrocytes formed by division of a single chondrocyte within cartilage matrix."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Osteoid","zhTerm":"类骨质","zh":"由成骨细胞新分泌、尚未发生矿化的有机骨基质。","en":"Osteoid is the newly secreted, unmineralized organic matrix of bone produced by osteoblasts."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Osteoblast","zhTerm":"成骨细胞","zh":"位于骨表面、合成类骨质的造骨细胞，活跃时呈立方形，粗面内质网和高尔基体发达。","en":"An osteoblast is a bone-forming cell on the bone surface that secretes osteoid. Active osteoblasts are cuboidal and have abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum and a prominent Golgi complex."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Osteocyte","zhTerm":"骨细胞","zh":"由成骨细胞被骨基质包埋后形成的成熟骨细胞；胞体位于骨陷窝，突起位于骨小管，参与维持骨基质。","en":"An osteocyte is a mature bone cell derived from an osteoblast enclosed in bone matrix. Its body lies in a lacuna and its processes extend through canaliculi to help maintain the matrix."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Osteoclast","zhTerm":"破骨细胞","zh":"位于骨表面吸收凹窝内的巨大多核骨吸收细胞，具有皱褶缘及丰富溶酶体，降解骨矿物和有机基质。","en":"An osteoclast is a large multinucleated cell that resorbs bone. It occupies a resorption bay and has a ruffled border and abundant lysosomes for breakdown of bone matrix."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Osteon / Haversian system","zhTerm":"骨单位／哈弗斯系统","zh":"成熟密质骨中的圆柱状结构单位，由中央管及围绕它排列的同心圆骨板组成，中央管内有血管、神经等。","en":"An osteon is a cylindrical structural unit of mature compact bone composed of a central canal and surrounding concentric lamellae. The canal contains blood vessels and nerves."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Bone lacuna","zhTerm":"骨陷窝","zh":"骨基质内容纳骨细胞胞体的小腔隙。","en":"A bone lacuna is a small cavity in bone matrix that houses the cell body of an osteocyte."},{"chapter":"04","term":"Bone canaliculi","zhTerm":"骨小管","zh":"骨基质内含骨细胞突起和组织液的微细通道，连接骨陷窝并支持细胞交流与物质交换。","en":"Bone canaliculi are tiny channels containing osteocyte processes and tissue fluid. They connect lacunae and support communication and exchange between osteocytes."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Sarcomere","zhTerm":"肌节","zh":"相邻两条Z线之间的一段肌原纤维，是横纹肌收缩的基本结构与功能单位。","en":"A sarcomere is the segment of a myofibril between adjacent Z discs and is the basic structural and functional unit of contraction in striated muscle."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Sarcoplasmic reticulum","zhTerm":"肌质网","zh":"肌细胞中特化的滑面内质网，主要储存、释放和回收钙离子，调节收缩与舒张。","en":"The sarcoplasmic reticulum is specialized smooth endoplasmic reticulum in muscle cells that stores, releases and takes up calcium ions to regulate contraction and relaxation."},{"chapter":"05","term":"T-tubule","zhTerm":"横小管／T管","zh":"肌膜向肌细胞内部凹陷形成的管道，将表面去极化传入细胞深部；其管腔与细胞外空间相通。","en":"A T-tubule is an inward extension of the sarcolemma that carries depolarization from the muscle cell surface into its interior. Its lumen is continuous with the extracellular space."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Triad","zhTerm":"三联体","zh":"一条横小管与其两侧各一个肌质网终池构成的复合结构；哺乳动物骨骼肌中通常位于A、I带交界处。","en":"A triad consists of one T-tubule flanked by two terminal cisternae of the sarcoplasmic reticulum. In mammalian skeletal muscle it is located at the A-I junction."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Diad / dyad","zhTerm":"二联体","zh":"一条横小管与一个肌质网终池相邻形成的结构，是心肌常见的膜系统组合。","en":"A diad consists of one T-tubule associated with one terminal cisterna of the sarcoplasmic reticulum and is characteristic of cardiac muscle."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Intercalated disc","zhTerm":"闰盘","zh":"相邻心肌细胞之间的连接复合体，含黏着连接、桥粒和缝隙连接，分别支持机械联系及电耦联。","en":"An intercalated disc is a junctional complex between adjacent cardiac muscle cells. Adherens junctions and desmosomes provide mechanical attachment, while gap junctions provide electrical coupling."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Red muscle fiber","zhTerm":"红肌纤维","zh":"传统分类中以氧化代谢和耐疲劳性为突出特点的骨骼肌纤维；典型慢氧化型富含肌红蛋白、线粒体和毛细血管，收缩较慢且能持续工作。","en":"A typical red, slow oxidative muscle fiber is rich in myoglobin and mitochondria, has a good capillary supply and produces sustained, relatively slow contractions with high fatigue resistance."},{"chapter":"05","term":"White muscle fiber","zhTerm":"白肌纤维","zh":"传统分类中以快速糖酵解供能为突出特点的较淡骨骼肌纤维；肌红蛋白和线粒体相对少，收缩快、能产生较强张力但较易疲劳。","en":"A typical white, fast glycolytic muscle fiber has relatively little myoglobin and fewer mitochondria. It relies mainly on glycolysis, contracts rapidly and forcefully, and fatigues relatively quickly."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Fast oxidative-glycolytic fiber","zhTerm":"快氧化糖酵解纤维／中间型肌纤维","zh":"兼有较强氧化和糖酵解能力、收缩较快的骨骼肌纤维；耐疲劳性通常介于典型慢氧化型和快糖酵解型之间，常与人体ⅡA型联系。","en":"A fast oxidative-glycolytic fiber contracts rapidly and has both oxidative and glycolytic metabolic capacity. Its fatigue resistance is generally intermediate between slow oxidative and fast glycolytic fibers."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Muscle satellite cell","zhTerm":"肌卫星细胞","zh":"位于骨骼肌纤维肌膜外、基膜内的单核前体细胞，能在损伤后活化、增殖并参与肌纤维修复。","en":"A muscle satellite cell is a mononuclear precursor located between the sarcolemma and basal lamina of a skeletal muscle fiber. It can become activated and contribute to muscle repair."},{"chapter":"05","term":"Motor unit","zhTerm":"运动单位","zh":"一个运动神经元及其支配的全部骨骼肌纤维共同组成的功能单位。","en":"A motor unit comprises one motor neuron together with all the skeletal muscle fibers innervated by that neuron."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Erythrocyte","zhTerm":"红细胞","zh":"富含血红蛋白、无核且可变形的双凹圆盘状血细胞，承担呼吸气体运输。","en":"An erythrocyte is a flexible, anucleate, biconcave blood cell rich in hemoglobin that transports respiratory gases."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Reticulocyte","zhTerm":"网织红细胞","zh":"已无核但仍保留少量核糖体RNA的未成熟红细胞，活体染色时胞质可呈蓝色颗粒或网状结构。","en":"A reticulocyte is an immature, anucleate red blood cell containing residual ribosomal RNA that appears as granules or a reticular network with supravital staining."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Neutrophil","zhTerm":"中性粒细胞","zh":"具有分叶核及细小胞质颗粒的粒细胞，可趋化进入炎症部位并吞噬细菌，参与急性化脓性炎症。","en":"A neutrophil is a granulocyte with a multilobed nucleus and fine cytoplasmic granules. It migrates to inflammatory sites and participates in bacterial phagocytosis."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Platelet","zhTerm":"血小板","zh":"骨髓巨核细胞形成的无核胞质碎片，含颗粒及骨架等结构，参与止血和凝血。","en":"A platelet is an anucleate cytoplasmic fragment derived from a megakaryocyte. It contains granules and cytoskeletal components and participates in hemostasis and coagulation."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Hemopoiesis / hematopoiesis","zhTerm":"血细胞发生／造血","zh":"由造血干细胞及其后代增殖、分化而形成血液有形成分的过程，成人主要在红骨髓进行。","en":"Hemopoiesis is the production and development of the formed elements of blood from hematopoietic stem and precursor cells, occurring mainly in red bone marrow in adults."},{"chapter":"06","term":"Hemogram / blood picture","zhTerm":"血象","zh":"对血液中红、白细胞及血小板数目、形态和比例，以及血红蛋白浓度等指标的描述。","en":"A hemogram describes the counts, morphology and proportions of blood cells and platelets, together with measurements such as hemoglobin concentration."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Neuron","zhTerm":"神经元","zh":"神经组织的基本结构和功能单位，由胞体、树突和轴突组成，能接收、整合并传递信息。","en":"A neuron is the structural and functional unit of nervous tissue. It consists of a cell body, dendrites and an axon and receives, integrates and transmits information."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Nissl bodies","zhTerm":"尼氏体","zh":"神经元胞体和树突内由粗面内质网及游离核糖体形成的嗜碱性团块，参与蛋白质合成；轴丘与轴突内不见典型尼氏体。","en":"Nissl bodies are basophilic aggregates of rough endoplasmic reticulum and free ribosomes in the neuronal cell body and dendrites. They participate in protein synthesis and are absent from the axon and axon hillock."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Synapse","zhTerm":"突触","zh":"神经元之间或神经元与效应细胞之间传递信息的特化连接。化学突触由突触前成分、突触间隙和突触后成分组成。","en":"A synapse is a specialized junction that transmits information between neurons or between a neuron and an effector cell. A chemical synapse consists of presynaptic and postsynaptic elements separated by a synaptic cleft."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Nerve fiber","zhTerm":"神经纤维","zh":"由轴突及其相关胶质包裹结构构成、负责传导神经冲动的结构，可分为有髓和无髓神经纤维。","en":"A nerve fiber consists of an axon and its associated glial coverings. It conducts nerve impulses and may be myelinated or unmyelinated."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Myelin sheath","zhTerm":"髓鞘","zh":"胶质细胞膜在轴突外反复卷绕形成的多层结构，具有电绝缘作用并有利于跳跃传导。周围由施万细胞形成，中枢由少突胶质细胞形成。","en":"The myelin sheath is a multilayered glial membrane wrapping around an axon that provides electrical insulation and supports saltatory conduction. It is formed by Schwann cells in the PNS and oligodendrocytes in the CNS."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Node of Ranvier","zhTerm":"郎飞结","zh":"有髓神经纤维相邻髓鞘节段之间的间隙，是跳跃传导过程中动作电位再生的重要部位。","en":"A node of Ranvier is a gap between adjacent myelin segments of a myelinated nerve fiber. It is a site of action potential regeneration during saltatory conduction."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Internode","zhTerm":"节间段","zh":"有髓神经纤维上两个相邻郎飞结之间的节段；周围神经中该段髓鞘由一个施万细胞形成。","en":"An internode is the segment of a myelinated nerve fiber between two adjacent nodes of Ranvier. In the PNS, its myelin is formed by one Schwann cell."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Blood-brain barrier","zhTerm":"血脑屏障","zh":"血液与中枢神经组织之间的选择性屏障，关键结构为连续毛细血管内皮及其紧密连接，相关基膜、周细胞和星形胶质细胞足突等共同支持其功能。","en":"The blood-brain barrier is a selective barrier between blood and CNS tissue. Its key structural basis is continuous capillary endothelium with tight junctions, supported by the basal lamina and associated pericytes and astrocyte end-feet."},{"chapter":"07","term":"Motor end plate","zhTerm":"运动终板","zh":"运动轴突与骨骼肌纤维接触的特化神经肌接头区域，肌膜侧有接头褶皱及乙酰胆碱受体，将神经信号传给肌纤维。","en":"A motor end plate is the specialized region of the neuromuscular junction where a motor axon contacts a skeletal muscle fiber. The postsynaptic sarcolemma has junctional folds and acetylcholine receptors for neuromuscular transmission."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Elastic artery","zhTerm":"弹性动脉","zh":"中膜富含弹性层板的大动脉，管壁在收缩期扩张、舒张期弹性回缩，有助于维持较连续的血流。","en":"An elastic artery is a large artery with numerous elastic lamellae in its tunica media. Expansion during systole and elastic recoil during diastole help maintain continuous blood flow."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Muscular artery","zhTerm":"肌性动脉","zh":"中膜以多层环行平滑肌为主、内外弹性膜较清楚的动脉，通过改变管径调节各器官血流分配。","en":"A muscular artery has a tunica media composed mainly of circular layers of smooth muscle and usually distinct elastic laminae. It regulates the distribution of blood by changing its diameter."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Capillary","zhTerm":"毛细血管","zh":"管壁主要由单层内皮及相关基膜构成的微小血管，是血液与组织之间进行物质交换的主要场所。","en":"A capillary is a small blood vessel whose wall consists mainly of a single layer of endothelial cells and an associated basal lamina. It is a major site of exchange between blood and tissues."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Fenestrated capillary","zhTerm":"有孔毛细血管","zh":"内皮细胞胞质具有窗孔而外侧基膜仍连续的毛细血管，适应较活跃的物质交换；窗孔可有薄隔膜。","en":"A fenestrated capillary has pores in its endothelial cells and a continuous basal lamina, allowing efficient exchange. Its fenestrations may be spanned by thin diaphragms."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Sinusoid","zhTerm":"血窦","zh":"管腔较宽且不规则、内皮可有较大窗孔或细胞间隙、基膜不连续或部分缺如的特殊微血管，有利于较大成分或细胞通行。","en":"A sinusoid is a specialized capillary with a wide, irregular lumen, endothelial fenestrations or gaps, and a discontinuous or incomplete basal lamina. It permits extensive exchange of large molecules or cells."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Microcirculation","zhTerm":"微循环","zh":"微动脉与微静脉之间的微血管循环，借局部血流分配和毛细血管交换为组织提供物质交换条件。","en":"Microcirculation is blood flow through the microvascular network between arterioles and venules. It regulates local perfusion and supports exchange between blood and tissues."},{"chapter":"08","term":"Purkinje fibers","zhTerm":"浦肯野纤维","zh":"心脏传导系统中的特化心肌细胞，通常位于心内膜下，细胞大、糖原丰富且胞质较淡，能快速传导兴奋以协调心室收缩。","en":"Purkinje fibers are specialized cardiac muscle cells of the conducting system, usually in the subendocardium. They are large and pale, contain abundant glycogen, and rapidly conduct impulses to coordinate ventricular contraction."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Lymphoid tissue","zhTerm":"淋巴组织","zh":"含大量淋巴细胞及其他免疫细胞、由支持网架构成的组织，参与免疫应答。多数由网状组织支持，胸腺的上皮性网架为重要例外。","en":"Lymphoid tissue contains numerous lymphocytes and other immune cells supported by a stromal framework. It participates in immune responses."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Diffuse lymphoid tissue","zhTerm":"弥散淋巴组织","zh":"淋巴细胞及其他免疫细胞较疏松分布、无清楚圆形边界的淋巴组织，可参与局部免疫反应。","en":"Diffuse lymphoid tissue is a loosely arranged accumulation of lymphocytes and other immune cells without a sharply defined boundary. It participates in local immune responses."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Secondary lymphoid follicle","zhTerm":"次级淋巴滤泡／次级淋巴小结","zh":"抗原刺激后形成、主要由B细胞构成且具有生发中心的球形淋巴细胞聚集，外围常见较深染的小淋巴细胞。","en":"A secondary lymphoid follicle is a rounded aggregation of mainly B lymphocytes with a germinal center formed after antigenic stimulation, usually surrounded by a darker mantle of small lymphocytes."},{"chapter":"09","term":"High endothelial venule","zhTerm":"高内皮微静脉","zh":"具有较高、近立方形内皮的特殊毛细血管后微静脉，允许血液中的淋巴细胞穿过管壁进入淋巴组织。","en":"A high endothelial venule is a specialized postcapillary venule with tall endothelial cells that allows circulating lymphocytes to enter lymphoid tissue."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Periarteriolar lymphoid sheath (PALS)","zhTerm":"动脉周围淋巴鞘","zh":"脾白髓中围绕中央小动脉、以T细胞为主的淋巴组织鞘，是脾的胸腺依赖区。","en":"The PALS is a T-cell-rich sheath surrounding a central arteriole in the white pulp of the spleen. It is a thymus-dependent region."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Splenic cord","zhTerm":"脾索","zh":"脾红髓内由网状组织组成、富含血细胞和巨噬细胞等的细胞索，参与血液过滤及衰老血细胞清除。","en":"A splenic cord is reticular tissue in the red pulp containing blood cells, lymphocytes and macrophages. It contributes to blood filtration and the removal of aged blood cells."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Splenic sinusoid","zhTerm":"脾血窦","zh":"脾红髓中的特殊血管通道，管腔较宽、不规则，细长杆状内皮细胞之间的间隙允许血细胞通行。","en":"A splenic sinusoid is a specialized vascular channel in the red pulp with a wide, irregular lumen. Gaps between elongated endothelial cells permit blood cells to pass."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Hassall corpuscle","zhTerm":"胸腺小体","zh":"位于胸腺髓质、由同心排列的上皮网状细胞形成的嗜酸性结构，是胸腺的重要识图标志。","en":"A Hassall corpuscle is an eosinophilic structure formed by concentric layers of epithelial reticular cells in the thymic medulla."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Blood-thymus barrier","zhTerm":"血胸腺屏障","zh":"胸腺皮质毛细血管周围的多层屏障，包括内皮及紧密连接、内皮基膜、含巨噬细胞的周血管间隙、上皮基膜和上皮网状细胞层，限制血源大分子抗原进入发育中T细胞环境。","en":"The blood-thymus barrier is a multilayered barrier around cortical capillaries that protects developing T cells from blood-borne macromolecular antigens. It includes continuous endothelium with tight junctions, its basal lamina, a macrophage-containing perivascular space, an epithelial basal lamina and epithelial reticular cells."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Lymph node","zhTerm":"淋巴结","zh":"位于淋巴管行程中的外周淋巴器官，实质分皮质和髓质，能过滤淋巴并支持T、B细胞免疫应答。","en":"A lymph node is a secondary lymphoid organ along lymphatic vessels. Its parenchyma is divided into cortex and medulla, and it filters lymph and supports T- and B-cell immune responses."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Spleen","zhTerm":"脾","zh":"位于血液循环通路中的外周淋巴器官，实质分白髓和红髓，参与血源抗原的免疫应答，并清除衰老或损伤红细胞。","en":"The spleen is a secondary lymphoid organ associated with the blood circulation. It has white and red pulp, mounts immune responses to blood-borne antigens and removes aged or damaged erythrocytes."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Thymus","zhTerm":"胸腺","zh":"提供T细胞发育、选择和成熟微环境的初级淋巴器官，由上皮网状细胞支持，分深染皮质和浅染髓质，髓质可见胸腺小体。","en":"The thymus is a primary lymphoid organ that provides a microenvironment for T-cell development, selection and maturation. It has a dark cortex and a paler medulla supported by epithelial reticular cells, with Hassall corpuscles in the medulla."},{"chapter":"09","term":"Antigen-presenting cell (APC)","zhTerm":"抗原呈递细胞","zh":"能够摄取、处理并向T细胞呈递抗原的细胞。专业APC包括树突状细胞、巨噬细胞和B细胞等。","en":"An antigen-presenting cell captures and processes antigen and presents antigenic peptides to T cells. Professional APCs include dendritic cells, macrophages and B lymphocytes."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Adherens junction","zhTerm":"黏着连接／中间连接","zh":"相邻细胞之间与肌动蛋白微丝相联系的锚定连接，帮助维持细胞层的机械稳定性与形态。","en":"An adherens junction is a cell-to-cell anchoring junction linked to actin filaments. It helps maintain the mechanical integrity and shape of a cell layer."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Desmosome","zhTerm":"桥粒","zh":"相邻细胞之间斑状的锚定连接，胞质附着板与中间丝相联系，使细胞能抵抗机械牵拉。","en":"A desmosome is a spot-like anchoring junction between adjacent cells. Its cytoplasmic plaques anchor intermediate filaments and provide strong mechanical attachment."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Hemidesmosome","zhTerm":"半桥粒","zh":"位于上皮细胞基底面的细胞—基质锚定连接，将胞内中间丝与基板联系起来，固定上皮细胞。","en":"A hemidesmosome is a cell-matrix anchoring junction at the basal surface of an epithelial cell. It links intracellular intermediate filaments to the basal lamina."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Merocrine secretion","zhTerm":"局浆分泌／胞吐分泌","zh":"分泌产物经胞吐释放，分泌细胞不伴随部分胞质脱落或整个细胞解体的分泌方式。","en":"Merocrine secretion releases secretory products by exocytosis while preserving the secreting cell and its cytoplasm."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Apocrine secretion","zhTerm":"顶浆分泌","zh":"分泌产物连同细胞顶端的一部分胞质和质膜脱离细胞的分泌方式。","en":"Apocrine secretion involves release of the product together with a portion of the apical cytoplasm and plasma membrane."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Holocrine secretion","zhTerm":"全浆分泌","zh":"整个分泌细胞解体并成为分泌物一部分的分泌方式，皮脂腺是典型例子。","en":"Holocrine secretion is a mode of secretion in which entire secretory cells disintegrate and become part of the secretion, as in sebaceous glands."},{"chapter":"03","term":"Metachromasia","zhTerm":"异染性","zh":"组织成分染色后呈现不同于染料溶液本来颜色的现象，肥大细胞颗粒用某些碱性染料染色时可表现此性质。","en":"Metachromasia is a staining phenomenon in which tissue components take on a color different from that of the dye solution. Mast-cell granules can show this property with certain basic dyes."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Serous cell","zhTerm":"浆液细胞","zh":"合成并分泌较稀薄、富含蛋白质的分泌物的外分泌腺细胞。其基底部通常富含粗面内质网而呈嗜碱性，顶端含分泌颗粒。浆液细胞与产生抗体的浆细胞是不同类型的细胞。","en":"A serous cell is an exocrine gland cell that produces a watery, protein-rich secretion. It typically contains abundant basal rough endoplasmic reticulum and apical secretory granules."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Mucous cell","zhTerm":"黏液细胞","zh":"合成并分泌黏蛋白等糖蛋白的腺细胞，分泌物与水结合形成具有润滑和保护作用的黏液。细胞顶端含较多黏原颗粒，常规H&E切片中胞质常浅染，细胞核常扁而偏向基底部。","en":"A mucous cell is a gland cell that produces mucin glycoproteins, which combine with water to form protective and lubricating mucus. It contains apical mucinogen granules and usually has pale cytoplasm and a flattened basal nucleus in routine H&E sections."},{"chapter":"02","term":"Myoepithelial cell","zhTerm":"肌上皮细胞","zh":"位于某些外分泌腺分泌部腺细胞与基膜之间、具有收缩能力的上皮细胞。其胞体扁平并具有多个突起，胞质内含收缩性微丝，收缩可帮助分泌物排入导管。","en":"A myoepithelial cell is a contractile epithelial cell located between the secretory cells and the basement membrane of certain exocrine glands. Its cytoplasmic processes contain contractile filaments, and its contraction helps expel secretion into the ducts."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Immunohistochemistry","zhTerm":"免疫组织化学","zh":"利用特异性抗原与抗体结合，在组织切片中检测并定位抗原性物质的技术。结合反应可通过荧光、酶反应产物或电子致密标记等显示；它检测的是相应抗原，不应与检测酶催化活性的酶组织化学混淆。","en":"Immunohistochemistry is a technique that detects and localizes specific antigens in tissue sections through antigen-antibody binding. The binding is visualized by suitable labels, such as fluorophores, enzyme-generated reaction products or electron-dense markers."},{"chapter":"01","term":"In situ hybridization","zhTerm":"原位杂交","zh":"在保留组织、细胞或染色体原有位置的标本中，以标记的核酸探针通过碱基互补配对识别特定DNA或RNA序列的技术。显示探针标记可获得目标核酸在标本内的分布信息。","en":"In situ hybridization is a technique that uses a labeled complementary nucleic acid probe to detect a specific DNA or RNA sequence within a tissue, cell or chromosome preparation while preserving its spatial location."},{"chapter":"01","term":"Argyrophilia / argentaffinity","zhTerm":"嗜银性／亲银性","zh":"两种银染反应特性。嗜银性指组织结构在银染时需加入外源还原剂，才能使银离子还原并显色；亲银性指组织结构本身可直接使银离子还原为黑色银颗粒，无需另加还原剂。二者不能仅按“都能染黑”视为同义词。","en":"Argyrophilia is the property of a tissue structure that requires an added reducing agent to develop metallic silver during silver staining. Argentaffinity is the ability of a tissue structure to reduce silver ions to visible metallic silver without an added reducing agent."}],"comparisons":[{"zh":"分泌什么","en":"What is secreted","rows":[["02","浆液性腺细胞","Serous gland cells","向腺腔释放富含蛋白的分泌物。观察顶端分泌颗粒。","Release protein-rich material into a gland lumen. Look for apical granules."],["03","浆细胞","Plasma cells","分泌抗体。看偏心核、车轮状染色质及核旁浅区。","Secrete antibodies. Look for an eccentric clock-face nucleus and pale Golgi region."],["03","成纤维细胞","Fibroblasts","合成细胞外基质，产物在细胞周围分布。","Produce extracellular matrix around the cells."],["08","心房肌细胞","Atrial cardiomyocytes","部分细胞含 ANP 分泌颗粒。识图仍以心肌组织定位为先。","Some cells contain ANP granules. First identify the cardiac muscle context."]]},{"zh":"屏障封在哪里","en":"Where each barrier seals","rows":[["02","上皮紧密连接","Epithelial tight junctions","位于上皮细胞近顶端的侧面，限制旁细胞通路。","Near the apical lateral border, restricting the paracellular pathway."],["07","血脑屏障","Blood–brain barrier","物理封口在脑毛细血管内皮紧密连接，周细胞与星形胶质足突支持。","The seal is at brain endothelial tight junctions, with pericyte and astrocyte support."],["09","血–胸腺屏障","Blood–thymus barrier","位于皮质，沿毛细血管内皮、两层基膜及上皮性网状细胞定位。","Cortical capillary endothelium, two basal laminae, and epithelial reticular cells are key landmarks."]]},{"zh":"怎么收缩","en":"How cells contract","rows":[["05","骨骼肌","Skeletal muscle","外周核、规则横纹。横管与两侧终池组成三联体。","Peripheral nuclei and striations. A T tubule and two terminal cisternae form a triad."],["05","心肌","Cardiac muscle","中央核、分支、闰盘。横管与一侧终池组成二联体。","Central nuclei, branching, and intercalated discs. A T tubule and one cisterna form a diad."],["05","平滑肌","Smooth muscle","梭形、中央长核、无横纹，肌丝附着于密体。","Spindle-shaped cells with central elongated nuclei, no striations, and dense bodies."]]},{"zh":"识别和防御怎么分工","en":"Recognition and defense","rows":[["03","巨噬细胞与肥大细胞","Macrophages and mast cells","巨噬细胞吞噬、消化；肥大细胞脱颗粒，释放介质。","Macrophages ingest and digest material. Mast cell degranulation releases mediators."],["06","中性粒细胞与嗜酸性粒细胞","Neutrophils and eosinophils","中性粒细胞常分叶核，吞噬细菌。嗜酸性粒细胞常双叶核、粗红颗粒，参与抗寄生虫反应。","Neutrophils often have segmented nuclei and ingest bacteria. Eosinophils often have bilobed nuclei and coarse red granules and participate in antiparasitic responses."],["09","普通树突状细胞和滤泡树突状细胞","Conventional and follicular dendritic cells","前者通过 MHC 给 T 细胞呈递肽。后者在滤泡内保留天然抗原供 B 细胞识别。","Conventional DCs present peptide–MHC to T cells. Follicular DCs retain native antigen for B cells."]]},{"zh":"形成、维持、更新","en":"Formation, maintenance, and turnover","rows":[["04","成骨细胞、骨细胞、破骨细胞","Osteoblasts, osteocytes, and osteoclasts","骨表面产基质、骨陷窝内感知负荷、骨表面吸收三个定位分别对应三类细胞。","Matrix deposition at the surface, mechanical sensing within lacunae, and resorption at the surface identify the three roles."],["06","造血干细胞和造血祖细胞","Hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells","干细胞有长期自我更新和多系分化潜能；祖细胞逐渐定向并扩增。","Stem cells have long-term self-renewal and multilineage potential. Progenitors expand as they become lineage-restricted."],["07","少突胶质细胞和施万细胞","Oligodendrocytes and Schwann cells","少突胶质细胞可包多个中枢节段，一个施万细胞包裹一个周围有髓节段。","An oligodendrocyte can myelinate several CNS internodes. One myelinating Schwann cell wraps one PNS internode."]]}],"practices":[{"id":"01_intro-q01","chapter":"01","type":"single_choice","topic":"分辨率与显微镜","stemEn":"Which method is most suitable for examining the internal ultrastructure of a mitochondrion?","stemZh":"要观察线粒体内部超微结构，最适合哪种方法？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Routine light microscopy","zh":"普通光镜"},{"key":"B","en":"Transmission electron microscopy","zh":"透射电镜"},{"key":"C","en":"Scanning electron microscopy","zh":"扫描电镜"},{"key":"D","en":"Increasing light-microscope magnification alone","zh":"仅增加光镜放大倍数"}],"answerEn":"B","answerZh":"B","explanationEn":"TEM displays thin sections and reveals internal ultrastructure, including mitochondrial membranes and cristae.","explanationZh":"TEM观察薄切片的内部超微结构，可显示线粒体膜和嵴。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Routine LM cannot resolve the details of mitochondrial membranes.","zh":"普通光镜无法分辨线粒体膜的超微细节。"},{"key":"B","en":"TEM is appropriate for internal ultrastructure.","zh":"TEM适合观察内部超微结构，为正确答案。"},{"key":"C","en":"SEM primarily shows surface topography.","zh":"SEM主要显示表面立体形态。"},{"key":"D","en":"Magnification alone does not overcome the resolving limit.","zh":"单纯放大不能突破分辨率限制。"}],"printedPages":[7,11]},{"id":"01_intro-q02","chapter":"01","type":"single_choice","topic":"胞质嗜碱性的结构基础","stemEn":"A cell exports large amounts of protein and has strongly basophilic cytoplasm. Which structure most directly accounts for this cytoplasmic basophilia?","stemZh":"一个细胞大量输出蛋白质，胞质强嗜碱性。哪种结构最直接解释这种胞质嗜碱性？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Abundant ribosomes and rough endoplasmic reticulum","zh":"丰富的核糖体和粗面内质网"},{"key":"B","en":"Large neutral lipid droplets","zh":"大型中性脂滴"},{"key":"C","en":"Extracellular collagen bundles","zh":"细胞外胶原纤维束"},{"key":"D","en":"The phospholipid bilayer alone","zh":"仅磷脂双分子层"}],"answerEn":"A","answerZh":"A","explanationEn":"Ribosomal RNA in free and RER-bound ribosomes contributes to basophilia. Abundant RER also supports synthesis of exported proteins.","explanationZh":"游离及附着核糖体中的rRNA贡献嗜碱性，丰富RER又与输出蛋白的合成相联系。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Abundant ribosomal RNA binds the hematoxylin staining system.","zh":"rRNA丰富，与苏木精染色体系结合，正确。"},{"key":"B","en":"Neutral lipids do not explain RNA-associated basophilia.","zh":"中性脂质不能解释与RNA有关的嗜碱性。"},{"key":"C","en":"Collagen is extracellular and usually eosinophilic in H&E.","zh":"胶原位于细胞外，H&E中通常嗜酸。"},{"key":"D","en":"The bilayer alone does not produce this characteristic cytoplasmic pattern.","zh":"仅有磷脂双层不能解释这种胞质染色特征。"}],"printedPages":[5,22]},{"id":"01_intro-q03","chapter":"01","type":"single_choice","topic":"常染色质与核仁","stemEn":"Which combination most strongly supports active transcription and ribosome production?","stemZh":"哪一组合最支持转录和核糖体形成活跃？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A small dark nucleus with mostly condensed chromatin","zh":"小而深染、以凝集染色质为主的核"},{"key":"B","en":"No nuclear envelope in a typical interphase cell","zh":"典型间期细胞缺少核膜"},{"key":"C","en":"Dispersed euchromatin with a prominent nucleolus","zh":"疏松常染色质及明显核仁"},{"key":"D","en":"Only a larger cell diameter","zh":"仅细胞直径更大"}],"answerEn":"C","answerZh":"C","explanationEn":"Dispersed euchromatin is generally associated with transcriptional activity; a prominent nucleolus is associated with rRNA synthesis and ribosomal subunit formation.","explanationZh":"疏松常染色质通常与转录活跃相关；明显核仁与rRNA及核糖体亚基形成相关。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Condensed heterochromatin is generally less transcriptionally active.","zh":"凝集异染色质通常转录较不活跃。"},{"key":"B","en":"Loss of the envelope is not the defining feature of active interphase transcription.","zh":"核膜消失不是间期转录活跃的判断标准。"},{"key":"C","en":"Both nuclear features support the stated functions.","zh":"两个核特征均支持题干功能，为正确答案。"},{"key":"D","en":"Cell size alone cannot establish these functions.","zh":"细胞大小单独不能确定这两项活动。"}],"printedPages":[]},{"id":"01_intro-q04","chapter":"01","type":"true_false","topic":"分辨率","stemEn":"Increasing the magnification of an already blurred light-microscope image necessarily reveals additional ultrastructural detail.","stemZh":"增加已经模糊的光镜图像的放大倍数，必然能显示更多超微结构。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Resolution determines whether adjacent structures can be distinguished. Enlarging an unresolved image does not create new detail.","explanationZh":"能否分开相邻结构取决于分辨能力；把未分辨的图像放大，不会产生新的结构细节。","printedPages":[5,7]},{"id":"01_intro-q05","chapter":"01","type":"true_false","topic":"切面与无核判断","stemEn":"A cell profile without a visible nucleus in one tissue section does not by itself prove that the cell type is anucleate.","stemZh":"在一张切片中看到某个细胞断面没有核，并不能单独证明这类细胞本来无核。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"A section may miss the nucleus. The known absence of a nucleus in a mature erythrocyte is a separate biological fact.","explanationZh":"切面可能没有经过核；成熟红细胞本来无核是另一项明确的生物学事实，二者不能混为一谈。","printedPages":[22]},{"id":"01_intro-q06","chapter":"01","type":"definition","topic":"嗜碱性","stemEn":"Define basophilia.","stemZh":"解释名词：嗜碱性（basophilia）。","answerEn":"Basophilia is the affinity of cellular or extracellular components for basic staining systems, appearing blue or purple in routine H&E staining; nucleic-acid-rich structures are typical examples.","answerZh":"嗜碱性指细胞或细胞外成分对碱性染色体系的亲和性，常规H&E中表现为蓝紫色；核酸丰富的结构是典型例子。","explanationEn":"State the staining affinity, the observed color in H&E and an appropriate structural example. Basophilia does not mean that the cell itself is alkaline.","explanationZh":"作答包含染色亲和性、H&E颜色及恰当例子；嗜碱性不是说细胞本身呈碱性。","printedPages":[5]},{"id":"01_intro-q07","chapter":"01","type":"image_label","topic":"原图结构定位","stemEn":"Identify the five structures described by locations A-E. The letters refer to the written location descriptions, not to new arrows on the original figure.","stemZh":"根据文字定位A–E，写出五个结构的英文名称。A–E仅为下方文字定位编号，不是原图自带的新箭头。","image":{"stem":"01-intro-q07","targets":[{"key":"A","whereEn":"The double boundary around the blue nuclear model on the left","whereZh":"左侧蓝色细胞核模型外围的双层边界","answerEn":"Nuclear envelope","answerZh":"核膜","explanationEn":"The envelope separates nucleoplasm from cytoplasm and contains pores.","explanationZh":"核膜将核质与胞质分隔，并含核孔。"},{"key":"B","whereEn":"The large dense blue body inside the left nuclear model","whereZh":"左侧核模型内部显著的蓝色致密团块","answerEn":"Nucleolus","answerZh":"核仁","explanationEn":"The nucleolus is inside the nucleus, not a second nucleus.","explanationZh":"核仁在核内，并非第二个细胞核。"},{"key":"C","whereEn":"The small circular openings on the outer blue surface of the left model","whereZh":"左侧模型蓝色外表面的多个小圆形开口","answerEn":"Nuclear pores","answerZh":"核孔","explanationEn":"The pores are part of the nuclear envelope and mediate nucleocytoplasmic exchange.","explanationZh":"核孔位于核膜，参与核与胞质之间的交换。"},{"key":"D","whereEn":"The small yellow dots on the cytoplasmic face of the nuclear model and adjacent membranes","whereZh":"核模型胞质侧及相邻膜上的黄色小点","answerEn":"Ribosomes","answerZh":"核糖体","explanationEn":"These are diagrammatic ribosomes on the cytoplasmic membrane surface.","explanationZh":"这是示意图中附着于膜胞质侧的核糖体。"},{"key":"E","whereEn":"The pale folded membrane cisternae continuous with the outer nuclear envelope at lower left","whereZh":"左下方与外核膜相连续的浅色折叠膜囊","answerEn":"Rough endoplasmic reticulum","answerZh":"粗面内质网","explanationEn":"RER has attached ribosomes and is continuous with the outer nuclear membrane.","explanationZh":"RER表面附着核糖体，并与外核膜连续。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Nuclear envelope; B: Nucleolus; C: Nuclear pores; D: Ribosomes; E: Rough endoplasmic reticulum","answerZh":"A：核膜；B：核仁；C：核孔；D：核糖体；E：粗面内质网","explanationEn":"Identify the location and the structural boundary before naming it. The original teaching figure contains labels, so this is guided recognition rather than a concealed-answer test.","explanationZh":"先核对位置及结构边界，再命名。所用原课件图保留原有文字标注，本题用于引导识图，不伪装成去答案的正式试卷。","printedPages":[]},{"id":"01_intro-q08","chapter":"01","type":"case","topic":"细胞器与蛋白输出","stemEn":"A tissue sample contains cells actively exporting proteins. Their cytoplasm is basophilic, TEM shows parallel membrane cisternae studded with small particles, and a pale juxtanuclear region is visible by light microscopy. Answer the following questions.","stemZh":"某组织样本内的细胞正在大量输出蛋白质。其胞质嗜碱性，TEM见平行膜囊表面附有小颗粒，光镜见核旁浅染区。回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Identify the particle-studded cisternae and explain the basophilic cytoplasm.","promptZh":"识别附有小颗粒的膜囊，并解释胞质嗜碱性。","answerEn":"They are rough endoplasmic reticulum. Abundant ribosomal RNA in attached ribosomes contributes to cytoplasmic basophilia.","answerZh":"这些是粗面内质网；附着核糖体中的rRNA丰富，贡献胞质嗜碱性。","explanationEn":"Name both the membrane organelle and the chemical basis of the staining.","explanationZh":"不能只答蛋白合成旺盛，还应写出RER与rRNA这两层依据。"},{"promptEn":"Which organelle most likely corresponds to the pale juxtanuclear region, and what does it do?","promptZh":"核旁浅染区最可能对应哪种细胞器？其主要任务是什么？","answerEn":"It most likely corresponds to the Golgi complex, which modifies, sorts and packages proteins for their destinations.","answerZh":"最可能对应高尔基复合体，负责蛋白的加工、分选及包装。","explanationEn":"A pale Golgi region is a light-microscopic clue, not direct visualization of every Golgi cisterna.","explanationZh":"核旁浅染区是光镜线索，不等于光镜直接分辨了每层高尔基扁囊。"},{"promptEn":"Trace the main route of an exported protein through these organelles.","promptZh":"描述输出蛋白通过相关细胞器的主要路径。","answerEn":"Synthesis on RER-bound ribosomes is followed by entry into the ER, transport to the Golgi complex, packaging into secretory vesicles and release by exocytosis.","answerZh":"附着于RER的核糖体合成蛋白，蛋白进入内质网，转运至高尔基复合体，包装进分泌囊泡，最后经胞吐释放。","explanationEn":"RER, Golgi and vesicles cooperate; neither mitochondria nor lysosomes replace this secretory route.","explanationZh":"RER、高尔基体与囊泡相互配合，线粒体和溶酶体不能代替这条分泌路径。"}],"answerEn":"See the three model answers below.","answerZh":"见以下三个小问的标准答案。","explanationEn":"Connect the observed structure to the stated function; do not infer an unprovided clinical diagnosis.","explanationZh":"从题目已给结构推到功能及后果，不额外推定未提供证据的疾病诊断。","printedPages":[22,28,30]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q01","chapter":"02","type":"single_choice","topic":"假复层上皮命名","stemEn":"Why is pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium classified as a simple epithelium?","stemZh":"假复层纤毛柱状上皮为什么属于单层上皮？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"All cells reach the free surface","zh":"全部细胞均到达游离面"},{"key":"B","en":"All cells contact the basement membrane","zh":"全部细胞均接触基膜"},{"key":"C","en":"All nuclei lie at the same level","zh":"所有细胞核位于同一高度"},{"key":"D","en":"Its cilia contain actin bundles","zh":"纤毛内含肌动蛋白束"}],"answerEn":"B","answerZh":"B","explanationEn":"All cells contact the basement membrane, although only some reach the free surface. Nuclei at different levels produce the false appearance of multiple layers.","explanationZh":"所有细胞均接触基膜，但只有部分到达游离面；核高低不一造成假复层外观。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Only some cells reach the free surface.","zh":"只有部分细胞达到游离面。"},{"key":"B","en":"Contact with the basement membrane is the decisive criterion.","zh":"全体细胞接触基膜是关键依据，为正确答案。"},{"key":"C","en":"The nuclei are located at different heights.","zh":"细胞核恰恰高低不一。"},{"key":"D","en":"Typical motile cilia contain microtubules, not an actin core.","zh":"典型运动纤毛骨架为微管，肌动蛋白束对应微绒毛。"}],"printedPages":[26]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q02","chapter":"02","type":"single_choice","topic":"细胞连接的功能与骨架","stemEn":"Which junction anchors an epithelial cell to the basal lamina?","stemZh":"哪一种连接把上皮细胞固定到基板？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Desmosome","zh":"桥粒"},{"key":"B","en":"Gap junction","zh":"缝隙连接"},{"key":"C","en":"Tight junction","zh":"紧密连接"},{"key":"D","en":"Hemidesmosome","zh":"半桥粒"}],"answerEn":"D","answerZh":"D","explanationEn":"Hemidesmosomes attach the basal surface of an epithelial cell to the basal lamina and connect to intermediate filaments.","explanationZh":"半桥粒位于上皮细胞基底面，将细胞固定到基板，并与中间丝联系。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Desmosomes provide mechanical adhesion between adjacent cells.","zh":"桥粒主要提供相邻细胞之间的机械联系。"},{"key":"B","en":"Gap junctions allow direct passage of ions and small molecules between cells.","zh":"缝隙连接使离子及小分子在相邻细胞间直接通过。"},{"key":"C","en":"Tight junctions regulate the paracellular route near the apical surface.","zh":"紧密连接位于近顶端侧面，调节细胞旁通路。"},{"key":"D","en":"The cell-to-matrix attachment is the defining feature of a hemidesmosome.","zh":"细胞与基板之间的附着是半桥粒的关键特征，正确。"}],"printedPages":[36,37]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q03","chapter":"02","type":"single_choice","topic":"三种分泌方式","stemEn":"Which secretion mode releases the product by exocytosis without loss of the whole cell or an apical portion of cytoplasm?","stemZh":"哪种分泌方式通过胞吐释放产物，不伴随整个细胞或顶端胞质的脱落？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Holocrine secretion","zh":"全浆分泌"},{"key":"B","en":"Merocrine secretion","zh":"局浆分泌"},{"key":"C","en":"Apocrine secretion","zh":"顶浆分泌"},{"key":"D","en":"Desquamation of the entire epithelial sheet","zh":"整片上皮脱落"}],"answerEn":"B","answerZh":"B","explanationEn":"Merocrine secretion releases vesicular contents by exocytosis. Holocrine secretion involves cell disintegration, whereas apocrine secretion involves loss of an apical portion.","explanationZh":"局浆分泌通过分泌囊泡胞吐释放内容物；全浆分泌伴细胞解体，顶浆分泌伴顶端部分胞质脱离。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"The entire secretory cell contributes to holocrine secretion.","zh":"全浆分泌中整个分泌细胞成为分泌物的一部分。"},{"key":"B","en":"Exocytosis with preservation of the cell is merocrine secretion.","zh":"保留细胞、经胞吐释放是局浆分泌，正确。"},{"key":"C","en":"Apocrine release includes a portion of apical cytoplasm.","zh":"顶浆分泌带走部分顶端胞质。"},{"key":"D","en":"Loss of an epithelial sheet is not the named physiological secretion mode.","zh":"整片上皮脱落不属于题述生理性分泌方式。"}],"printedPages":[30,31]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q04","chapter":"02","type":"true_false","topic":"复层上皮命名","stemEn":"A stratified epithelium is named mainly according to the shape of the cells in its basal layer.","stemZh":"复层上皮主要依据基底层细胞的形状命名。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Stratified epithelia are named by the shape of their superficial cells. A basal layer of cuboidal cells does not prevent the epithelium from being stratified squamous.","explanationZh":"复层上皮按最表层细胞形状命名；基底细胞为立方形，不妨碍整层上皮被命名为复层扁平上皮。","printedPages":[27]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q05","chapter":"02","type":"true_false","topic":"单腺与复腺分类","stemEn":"The terms simple and compound exocrine glands refer to whether the duct system is branched, not to whether the gland contains one or many secretory cells.","stemZh":"外分泌腺的单腺与复腺，依据导管系统是否分支区分，而不是依据分泌细胞为一个还是多个。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"A simple gland has an unbranched duct; a compound gland has branched ducts. Unicellular versus multicellular is a separate classification, so a simple gland can contain many secretory cells.","explanationZh":"单腺导管不分支，复腺导管分支；单细胞腺／多细胞腺是另一条分类轴，单腺也可含许多分泌细胞。","printedPages":[30,31]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q06","chapter":"02","type":"definition","topic":"基膜","stemEn":"Define basement membrane.","stemZh":"解释名词：基膜（basement membrane）。","answerEn":"The basement membrane is a thin extracellular layer between an epithelium and its underlying connective tissue. In the course model, it includes the basal lamina and reticular lamina and provides support, attachment and selective permeability.","answerZh":"基膜是上皮与下方结缔组织之间的细胞外薄层；课程模型将其分为基板和网板，具有支持、附着与选择性通透作用。","explanationEn":"Include its extracellular location, main layers and functions. A basal plasma-membrane infolding is part of the epithelial cell, whereas the basement membrane is outside the cell.","explanationZh":"答题包括细胞外位置、主要分层与功能。质膜内褶属于细胞自身质膜，基膜则位于细胞外，不能互换。","printedPages":[35,36]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q07","chapter":"02","type":"image_label","topic":"原图结构定位","stemEn":"Identify the five structures described by locations A-E. The letters refer to the written location descriptions, not to new arrows on the original figure.","stemZh":"根据文字定位A–E，写出五个结构的英文名称。A–E仅为下方文字定位编号，不是原图自带的新箭头。","image":{"stem":"02-epithelium-q07","targets":[{"key":"A","whereEn":"The uppermost belt-like contact on the lateral surfaces immediately below the microvilli","whereZh":"紧邻微绒毛下方、侧面最上端的带状连接","answerEn":"Tight junction / Zonula occludens","answerZh":"紧密连接／闭锁小带","explanationEn":"Its position and sealing pattern distinguish it from the anchoring junctions below.","explanationZh":"近顶端的位置及封闭细胞间隙的模式使其区别于下方机械连接。"},{"key":"B","whereEn":"The lateral belt just below A, associated with the green filament bundle","whereZh":"A下方、与绿色丝束相联系的侧面带状连接","answerEn":"Adherens junction / Zonula adherens","answerZh":"黏着连接／中间连接","explanationEn":"The green filaments represent actin; this junction mechanically links adjacent cells.","explanationZh":"绿色丝表示肌动蛋白；此连接提供细胞之间的机械联系。"},{"key":"C","whereEn":"The spot-like lateral junctions with dense plaques from which orange filaments extend","whereZh":"侧面斑状连接，致密附着板向胞质发出橙色丝","answerEn":"Desmosome / Macula adherens","answerZh":"桥粒","explanationEn":"The orange intermediate filaments are attached to desmosomal plaques.","explanationZh":"橙色中间丝附着于桥粒的胞质侧附着板。"},{"key":"D","whereEn":"The small channel-containing patch halfway down the left lateral surface","whereZh":"左侧面中下部带多个小通道的斑片","answerEn":"Gap junction","answerZh":"缝隙连接","explanationEn":"Paired channels allow ions and small molecules to move directly between neighboring cells.","explanationZh":"对接的通道允许离子和小分子在相邻细胞间直接通过。"},{"key":"E","whereEn":"The anchoring structure on the bottom surface where orange filaments meet the purple basal layer","whereZh":"底部橙色丝与紫色基板相接的基底附着结构","answerEn":"Hemidesmosome","answerZh":"半桥粒","explanationEn":"This is a cell-to-matrix attachment, not an additional cell-to-cell desmosome.","explanationZh":"这是细胞与基质的附着，而不是另一种细胞间桥粒。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Tight junction / Zonula occludens; B: Adherens junction / Zonula adherens; C: Desmosome / Macula adherens; D: Gap junction; E: Hemidesmosome","answerZh":"A：紧密连接／闭锁小带；B：黏着连接／中间连接；C：桥粒；D：缝隙连接；E：半桥粒","explanationEn":"Identify the location and the structural boundary before naming it. The original teaching figure contains labels, so this is guided recognition rather than a concealed-answer test.","explanationZh":"先核对位置及结构边界，再命名。所用原课件图保留原有文字标注，本题用于引导识图，不伪装成去答案的正式试卷。","printedPages":[32,34,35,36,37]},{"id":"02_epithelium-q08","chapter":"02","type":"case","topic":"呼吸道上皮与黏液清除","stemEn":"A patient has recurrent retention of airway mucus. A sample shows tall epithelial cells with nuclei at different levels, pale mucus-producing cells and reduced movement of the long apical projections. Answer the following questions.","stemZh":"某患者反复出现气道黏液潴留。标本见高柱状细胞、核位置高低不一、浅染产黏液细胞，长的顶端突起运动减弱。回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Identify the epithelial type and explain why it is not truly stratified.","promptZh":"识别上皮类型，并解释它为什么并非真正复层。","answerEn":"It is pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium. All cells contact the basement membrane, although not all reach the free surface.","answerZh":"是假复层纤毛柱状上皮。所有细胞接触基膜，但并非全部达到游离面。","explanationEn":"Different nuclear heights create the apparent layers.","explanationZh":"核高低不一造成表观多层，不能仅按核排数命名。"},{"promptEn":"Identify the long apical projections and contrast their main skeleton and function with those of microvilli.","promptZh":"识别长的顶端突起，并与微绒毛比较主要骨架及功能。","answerEn":"The projections are motile cilia, which have a microtubular axoneme, typically 9+2, and move mucus. Microvilli contain actin bundles and increase surface area for absorption.","answerZh":"这些是运动纤毛，典型轴丝为9+2微管，负责推动黏液；微绒毛含肌动蛋白束，主要增加吸收面积。","explanationEn":"Projection length, movement and skeleton must agree; microvilli do not replace ciliary clearance.","explanationZh":"长度、运动与骨架三者应一致；微绒毛不能代替纤毛清除黏液。"},{"promptEn":"Which cells produce the mucus, and how can impaired ciliary movement lead to mucus retention?","promptZh":"什么细胞产生黏液？纤毛运动减弱怎样造成黏液潴留？","answerEn":"Goblet cells secrete mucus, which traps particles. Ciliated cells move this mucus along the surface; impaired movement reduces clearance and allows mucus and trapped material to accumulate.","answerZh":"杯状细胞分泌黏液并捕获颗粒；纤毛细胞推动黏液沿表面移动，纤毛运动受损使清除减少，黏液和被捕获物积聚。","explanationEn":"Secretion and transport are performed by cooperating cell types. The findings alone do not establish a specific genetic disorder.","explanationZh":"分泌和运输由不同细胞协作完成；这些描述不足以直接确诊某个遗传病。"}],"answerEn":"See the three model answers below.","answerZh":"见以下三个小问的标准答案。","explanationEn":"Connect the observed structure to the stated function; do not infer an unprovided clinical diagnosis.","explanationZh":"从题目已给结构推到功能及后果，不额外推定未提供证据的疾病诊断。","printedPages":[26,33]},{"id":"03_connective-q01","chapter":"03","type":"single_choice","topic":"三类纤维","stemEn":"Which description best identifies reticular fibers?","stemZh":"哪项最符合网状纤维？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Thick type I collagen bundles providing tensile strength","zh":"粗大的Ⅰ型胶原束，提供抗拉强度"},{"key":"B","en":"An elastin core surrounded by microfibrils","zh":"弹性蛋白核心，周围有微原纤维"},{"key":"C","en":"A delicate argyrophilic network rich in type III collagen","zh":"富含Ⅲ型胶原的精细嗜银性网络"},{"key":"D","en":"Intracellular filaments forming the ciliary axoneme","zh":"形成纤毛轴丝的细胞内丝状结构"}],"answerEn":"C","answerZh":"C","explanationEn":"Reticular fibers form a fine supporting network and are rich in type III collagen; silver staining makes them conspicuous.","explanationZh":"网状纤维以Ⅲ型胶原为主，形成精细支架；银染使其清楚显示。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"This is the usual description of thick collagen bundles.","zh":"这描述粗胶原纤维束。"},{"key":"B","en":"This describes elastic fibers.","zh":"这描述弹性纤维。"},{"key":"C","en":"Fine network, type III collagen and argyrophilia agree.","zh":"细网、Ⅲ型胶原和嗜银性三条线索一致，为正确答案。"},{"key":"D","en":"The axoneme is a microtubular intracellular structure.","zh":"轴丝是细胞内微管结构，不属于细胞外结缔纤维。"}],"printedPages":[46,47]},{"id":"03_connective-q02","chapter":"03","type":"single_choice","topic":"浆细胞结构功能","stemEn":"A connective-tissue cell has an eccentric nucleus with coarse peripheral chromatin, basophilic cytoplasm and a pale perinuclear region. What is its principal specialized function?","stemZh":"结缔组织内某细胞核偏心、粗染色质沿核周分布、胞质嗜碱且核旁浅染。其主要特化功能是什么？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Production of antibodies","zh":"产生抗体"},{"key":"B","en":"Storage of histamine-rich granules","zh":"储存富含组胺的颗粒"},{"key":"C","en":"Synthesis of most extracellular collagen bundles","zh":"合成大部分细胞外胶原束"},{"key":"D","en":"Storage of a single large neutral-lipid droplet","zh":"储存单个大型中性脂滴"}],"answerEn":"A","answerZh":"A","explanationEn":"The combined features identify a plasma cell. Its abundant RER and Golgi complex support immunoglobulin synthesis and secretion.","explanationZh":"这些特征共同支持浆细胞；丰富RER与Golgi适应免疫球蛋白的合成、分泌。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Plasma cells synthesize and secrete immunoglobulins.","zh":"浆细胞合成并分泌免疫球蛋白，正确。"},{"key":"B","en":"Histamine-rich granules suggest mast cells.","zh":"组胺颗粒主要联系肥大细胞。"},{"key":"C","en":"Fibroblasts are the principal ECM-producing cells in connective tissue proper.","zh":"固有结缔组织中ECM的主要生产者为成纤维细胞。"},{"key":"D","en":"A single large lipid droplet is characteristic of a white adipocyte.","zh":"单个大脂滴是白色脂肪细胞特征。"}],"printedPages":[40,41,42]},{"id":"03_connective-q03","chapter":"03","type":"single_choice","topic":"基质分子筛","stemEn":"Which statement best explains the molecular sieve of connective-tissue ground substance?","stemZh":"哪一项最准确解释结缔组织基质的分子筛？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"It is an impermeable wall that blocks every bacterium","zh":"它是阻挡所有细菌的完全不透性墙"},{"key":"B","en":"It consists exclusively of tightly packed collagen bundles","zh":"它仅由紧密堆积的胶原束组成"},{"key":"C","en":"It is the same structure as a nuclear pore","zh":"它与核孔为同一结构"},{"key":"D","en":"A hydrated hyaluronan-proteoglycan network permits diffusion while restricting some large particles","zh":"水合的透明质酸－蛋白聚糖网络允许扩散，同时限制部分大颗粒"}],"answerEn":"D","answerZh":"D","explanationEn":"GAGs and proteoglycans bind water to form a hydrated gel. This provides an exchange medium and selectively limits passage; it is not an absolute seal.","explanationZh":"GAG与蛋白聚糖结合水形成凝胶，提供交换介质并选择性限制通过，但不构成绝对密封。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Restriction is selective, not an absolute block of all microbes.","zh":"这种限制具有选择性，并非绝对挡住所有微生物。"},{"key":"B","en":"Collagen bundles are fibers; the molecular sieve concerns the hydrated ground substance.","zh":"胶原束属于纤维；分子筛重点是水合基质网络。"},{"key":"C","en":"A nuclear pore lies in the nuclear envelope, not in the extracellular ground substance.","zh":"核孔位于核膜，不在细胞外基质中。"},{"key":"D","en":"This combines the correct composition, hydration and functions.","zh":"这一选项同时符合组成、水合状态和功能，正确。"}],"printedPages":[48,49]},{"id":"03_connective-q04","chapter":"03","type":"true_false","topic":"肝素与硫酸乙酰肝素","stemEn":"Heparin in mast-cell granules and heparan sulfate in extracellular matrix are interchangeable names for the same material.","stemZh":"肥大细胞颗粒内的肝素与ECM中的硫酸乙酰肝素是同一种物质的可互换名称。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Heparin and heparan sulfate are related but distinct GAGs. Heparin is associated here with mast-cell granules and anticoagulant activity; heparan sulfate is an ECM-associated GAG.","explanationZh":"两者相关但不同。此处heparin指肥大细胞颗粒中具有抗凝作用的肝素；heparan sulfate为ECM相关GAG，不应因英文相近而混用。","printedPages":[44,48]},{"id":"03_connective-q05","chapter":"03","type":"true_false","topic":"白脂肪与棕脂肪","stemEn":"Brown adipocytes typically contain multiple lipid droplets and numerous mitochondria, whereas white adipocytes usually have one large lipid droplet.","stemZh":"棕色脂肪细胞通常有多个脂滴和丰富线粒体，而白色脂肪细胞通常有单个大脂滴。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"Multilocular lipid storage and abundant mitochondria support the thermogenic role of brown adipose tissue; unilocular white adipocytes mainly store energy.","explanationZh":"棕色脂肪多房脂滴及丰富线粒体与产热功能相适应；单房白色脂肪细胞主要储能。","printedPages":[45,46,51]},{"id":"03_connective-q06","chapter":"03","type":"definition","topic":"分子筛","stemEn":"Define molecular sieve.","stemZh":"解释名词：分子筛（molecular sieve）。","answerEn":"The molecular sieve is a hydrated network of hyaluronan and proteoglycans in connective-tissue ground substance that permits diffusion of substances while restricting the passage of some large particles.","answerZh":"分子筛是结缔组织基质中由透明质酸和蛋白聚糖组成的水合网络，允许物质扩散，并限制部分大颗粒通过。","explanationEn":"Include the location in ground substance, the hydrated molecular network and its selective rather than absolute barrier function.","explanationZh":"定义应包含基质中的位置、水合分子网络及选择性限制功能，不写成绝对不通透。","printedPages":[48,49]},{"id":"03_connective-q07","chapter":"03","type":"image_label","topic":"原图结构定位","stemEn":"Identify the five structures described by locations A-E. The letters refer to the written location descriptions, not to new arrows on the original figure.","stemZh":"根据文字定位A–E，写出五个结构的英文名称。A–E仅为下方文字定位编号，不是原图自带的新箭头。","image":{"stem":"03-connective-q07","targets":[{"key":"A","whereEn":"In the upper-right panel, the elongated purple cell at the lower edge indicated by the Fibroblast leader","whereZh":"右上小图下缘、原图Fibroblast引线指向的紫色梭形细胞","answerEn":"Fibroblast","answerZh":"成纤维细胞","explanationEn":"This stellate or spindle-shaped resident cell is distinct from the surrounding extracellular fibers.","explanationZh":"梭形或有突起的常驻细胞与周围细胞外纤维不是同一级结构。"},{"key":"B","whereEn":"In the upper-right panel, the irregular brown cell containing several dark bodies near the Macrophage leader","whereZh":"右上小图Macrophage引线附近、不规则且含多个深色小体的棕色细胞","answerEn":"Macrophage","answerZh":"巨噬细胞","explanationEn":"Its irregular contour and phagocytic contents agree with a phagocytic cell.","explanationZh":"不规则轮廓与吞噬内容物共同支持吞噬细胞。"},{"key":"C","whereEn":"At the bottom of the lower-left block diagram, the small blue cell indicated by the Plasma cell leader","whereZh":"左下立体块图最下缘、原图Plasma cell引线指向的小蓝色细胞","answerEn":"Plasma cell","answerZh":"浆细胞","explanationEn":"Use the actual leader line; do not label a nearby large fiber bundle as a cell.","explanationZh":"沿原图引线准确定位，不能把附近大纤维束当成细胞。"},{"key":"D","whereEn":"In the lower-left block diagram, the thick blue-green, cross-banded bundles indicated by Collagen fibers","whereZh":"左下立体块图中原图Collagen fibers引线所指的粗蓝绿色有横纹束","answerEn":"Collagen fibers","answerZh":"胶原纤维","explanationEn":"The diagram encodes collagen as thick bundles; this blue-green is not the expected H&E color.","explanationZh":"图中用粗束编码胶原，蓝绿色是示意图配色，不能套作H&E真实染色。"},{"key":"E","whereEn":"In the upper-right panel, the thin dark branching strands indicated by Elastic fiber","whereZh":"右上小图原图Elastic fiber引线所指的细深色分支线","answerEn":"Elastic fibers","answerZh":"弹性纤维","explanationEn":"The thin branching fibers must be distinguished from the thick pink collagen bundles.","explanationZh":"细且分支的弹性纤维应与粗粉红胶原束区分。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Fibroblast; B: Macrophage; C: Plasma cell; D: Collagen fibers; E: Elastic fibers","answerZh":"A：成纤维细胞；B：巨噬细胞；C：浆细胞；D：胶原纤维；E：弹性纤维","explanationEn":"Identify the location and the structural boundary before naming it. The original teaching figure contains labels, so this is guided recognition rather than a concealed-answer test.","explanationZh":"先核对位置及结构边界，再命名。所用原课件图保留原有文字标注，本题用于引导识图，不伪装成去答案的正式试卷。","printedPages":[39,40,47]},{"id":"03_connective-q08","chapter":"03","type":"case","topic":"炎症水肿与伤口修复","stemEn":"A superficial skin wound becomes red and swollen. Microscopy shows granule-rich cells near small vessels and, during later repair, increased spindle-shaped cells with pale nuclei. New collagen accumulates in the wound. Answer the following questions.","stemZh":"某浅表皮肤伤口出现红肿。显微镜见小血管旁颗粒丰富的细胞；随后修复阶段出现更多核较浅的梭形细胞，伤口内新生胶原增多。回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Which granule-rich cell is most closely associated with rapid local histamine release, and how does histamine contribute to swelling?","promptZh":"哪种颗粒丰富的细胞最直接联系局部快速释放组胺？组胺怎样促进肿胀？","answerEn":"Mast cells release histamine. Increased vascular permeability allows more fluid to enter the interstitial tissue, contributing to edema.","answerZh":"肥大细胞释放组胺，增加血管通透性，使更多液体进入组织间隙，促成水肿。","explanationEn":"Use vessel-adjacent location, granules and histamine together. Granules alone would not identify every cell as a mast cell.","explanationZh":"应结合血管旁位置、颗粒和组胺功能判断；不能只凭有颗粒就认定所有细胞为肥大细胞。"},{"promptEn":"Identify the spindle-shaped cells producing new collagen and name the organelles expected to be well developed.","promptZh":"识别产生新胶原的梭形细胞，并写出预期发达的细胞器。","answerEn":"They are active fibroblasts, with abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum and a well-developed Golgi complex.","answerZh":"是活跃成纤维细胞，具有丰富粗面内质网和发达高尔基复合体。","explanationEn":"The required task is synthesis and secretion of ECM proteins, not antibody production.","explanationZh":"题述任务为合成、分泌ECM蛋白，不能误答浆细胞的抗体分泌。"},{"promptEn":"What mechanical property does the newly deposited collagen mainly provide, and how does this differ from elastic fibers?","promptZh":"新沉积胶原主要提供什么机械性能？与弹性纤维有何区别？","answerEn":"Collagen mainly provides tensile strength and supports the repaired tissue. Elastic fibers are specialized for stretching and recoil.","answerZh":"胶原主要提供抗拉强度、支持修复组织；弹性纤维主要适应伸展与回缩。","explanationEn":"Do not equate scar collagen with complete restoration of every original tissue component.","explanationZh":"不能把瘢痕胶原增多理解为原组织所有成分均已完全恢复。"}],"answerEn":"See the three model answers below.","answerZh":"见以下三个小问的标准答案。","explanationEn":"Connect the observed structure to the stated function; do not infer an unprovided clinical diagnosis.","explanationZh":"从题目已给结构推到功能及后果，不额外推定未提供证据的疾病诊断。","printedPages":[38,39,44,45,47]},{"id":"bone-mcq-01","chapter":"04","type":"single_choice","topic":"骨小管与营养通路","stemEn":"Which structure contains osteocyte processes and tissue fluid rather than a blood vessel?","stemZh":"哪一种结构内含骨细胞突起和组织液，而不是血管？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A central canal","zh":"中央管"},{"key":"B","en":"A bone canaliculus","zh":"骨小管"},{"key":"C","en":"A perforating canal","zh":"穿通管"},{"key":"D","en":"A marrow cavity","zh":"骨髓腔"}],"answerEn":"B. A bone canaliculus","answerZh":"B. 骨小管","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Central canals contain vessels, nerves and connective tissue.","zh":"中央管内有血管、神经和结缔组织。"},{"key":"B","en":"Canaliculi contain osteocyte processes and tissue fluid, linking lacunae for exchange.","zh":"骨小管含骨细胞突起和组织液，连接骨陷窝，参与物质交换。"},{"key":"C","en":"Perforating canals carry vessels between vascular channels and bone surfaces.","zh":"穿通管内有血管，沟通不同血管通道及骨表面。"},{"key":"D","en":"A marrow cavity contains marrow and vessels; it is not the minute channel for osteocyte processes.","zh":"骨髓腔内有骨髓和血管，不是容纳骨细胞突起的微细通道。"}],"explanationEn":"Canaliculi contain osteocyte processes and tissue fluid, linking lacunae for exchange.","explanationZh":"骨小管含骨细胞突起和组织液，连接骨陷窝，参与物质交换。","printedPages":[58,59,62]},{"id":"bone-mcq-02","chapter":"04","type":"single_choice","topic":"三类软骨比较","stemEn":"A specimen contains chondrocytes in lacunae arranged in rows between thick collagen bundles. Which tissue is most likely?","stemZh":"某标本中陷窝内的软骨细胞成行排列于粗胶原束之间，最可能是哪种组织？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Hyaline cartilage","zh":"透明软骨"},{"key":"B","en":"Elastic cartilage","zh":"弹性软骨"},{"key":"C","en":"Fibrocartilage","zh":"纤维软骨"},{"key":"D","en":"Dense regular connective tissue","zh":"致密规则结缔组织"}],"answerEn":"C. Fibrocartilage","answerZh":"C. 纤维软骨","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Hyaline cartilage has a relatively homogeneous matrix in routine light microscopy.","zh":"透明软骨在常规光镜下基质较均一，粗胶原束不突出。"},{"key":"B","en":"Elastic cartilage has a conspicuous elastic-fiber network rather than dominant thick collagen bundles.","zh":"弹性软骨突出的是弹性纤维网，不是以粗胶原束为主要背景。"},{"key":"C","en":"Rows of chondrocytes in lacunae between thick collagen bundles are characteristic of fibrocartilage.","zh":"粗胶原束之间成行排列的陷窝及软骨细胞，是纤维软骨的典型组合。"},{"key":"D","en":"Tendon has parallel collagen and fibroblast nuclei, but not typical chondrocytes in lacunae.","zh":"肌腱可有平行胶原和成纤维细胞核，但没有典型陷窝内软骨细胞这一组合。"}],"explanationEn":"Rows of chondrocytes in lacunae between thick collagen bundles are characteristic of fibrocartilage.","explanationZh":"粗胶原束之间成行排列的陷窝及软骨细胞，是纤维软骨的典型组合。","printedPages":[56,57]},{"id":"bone-mcq-03","chapter":"04","type":"single_choice","topic":"骨细胞位置与功能","stemEn":"Which bone cell is large, multinucleated and specialized for resorption at the bone surface?","stemZh":"哪种骨细胞体积大、多核，并在骨表面承担骨吸收？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"An osteoblast","zh":"成骨细胞"},{"key":"B","en":"An osteocyte","zh":"骨细胞"},{"key":"C","en":"An osteoprogenitor cell","zh":"骨祖细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"An osteoclast","zh":"破骨细胞"}],"answerEn":"D. An osteoclast","answerZh":"D. 破骨细胞","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Osteoblasts form osteoid and usually line the surface as smaller mononuclear cells.","zh":"成骨细胞形成类骨质，通常为沿表面排列的较小单核细胞。"},{"key":"B","en":"Osteocytes are embedded in lacunae and maintain surrounding matrix.","zh":"骨细胞包埋于骨陷窝内，维持周围骨基质。"},{"key":"C","en":"Osteoprogenitor cells differentiate into osteoblasts; they are not giant resorptive cells.","zh":"骨祖细胞能分化为成骨细胞，不是巨大的吸收性细胞。"},{"key":"D","en":"An osteoclast is a giant multinucleated cell whose resorptive surface includes a ruffled border.","zh":"破骨细胞是巨大多核细胞，吸收面具有皱褶缘，与骨吸收相适应。"}],"explanationEn":"An osteoclast is a giant multinucleated cell whose resorptive surface includes a ruffled border.","explanationZh":"破骨细胞是巨大多核细胞，吸收面具有皱褶缘，与骨吸收相适应。","printedPages":[60,61]},{"id":"bone-tf-01","chapter":"04","type":"true_false","topic":"类骨质与矿化","stemEn":"Osteoid is the newly deposited organic bone matrix before mineralization.","stemZh":"类骨质是新沉积、尚未矿化的有机骨基质。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"Osteoblasts first secrete osteoid; subsequent mineral deposition produces mineralized bone matrix.","explanationZh":"成骨细胞先分泌类骨质，随后矿物质沉积形成矿化骨基质；类骨质不是单指钙盐。","printedPages":[58,59]},{"id":"bone-tf-02","chapter":"04","type":"true_false","topic":"软骨营养与软骨膜","stemEn":"All cartilage is supplied by blood vessels that enter the cartilage lacunae.","stemZh":"所有软骨均由进入软骨陷窝的血管直接供养。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Cartilage is avascular. Nutrients diffuse through its hydrated matrix; vessels do not enter cartilage lacunae.","explanationZh":"软骨本身无血管，营养经富含水分的基质扩散到软骨细胞，而不是血管进入每个陷窝。","printedPages":[54]},{"id":"bone-def-01","chapter":"04","type":"definition","topic":"骨单位","stemEn":"Define an osteon (Haversian system).","stemZh":"解释骨单位（哈弗斯系统）。","answerEn":"An osteon is a cylindrical structural unit of mature compact bone, consisting of a central canal containing blood vessels and nerves, surrounded by concentric bone lamellae.","answerZh":"骨单位是成熟密质骨中的圆柱形结构单位，由含血管和神经的中央管及其周围同心圆排列的骨板组成。","explanationEn":"A complete definition identifies the tissue, the central canal and the concentric lamellae. An osteon is larger than a lacuna or a single lamella.","explanationZh":"得分要点是成熟密质骨、中央管、同心圆骨板三者的关系。骨单位大于单个骨陷窝，也不等于一层骨板。","printedPages":[62]},{"id":"bone-image-01","chapter":"04","type":"image_label","topic":"骨表面细胞与骨基质","stemEn":"Identify the five structures described by A-E in the original course image. A-E are textual locations, not labels added to the image.","stemZh":"根据A-E的文字定位识别原课件图中的五种结构。A-E为本题文字定位，不是原图新增箭头。","image":{"stem":"bone-image-01","targets":[{"key":"A","whereZh":"图上方、骨小梁表面橙色箭头指向的巨大细胞","whereEn":"The giant cell on the upper bone surface, indicated by the orange arrow","answerEn":"Osteoclast","answerZh":"破骨细胞","explanationEn":"Its large cell body and surface position support an osteoclast; this view does not resolve its ruffled border.","explanationZh":"巨大胞体及骨表面位置支持破骨细胞；本图不能据其外缘清楚分辨皱褶缘。"},{"key":"B","whereZh":"骨小梁下缘、黑色箭头所指的成排较小细胞","whereEn":"The row of smaller cells along the lower surface, indicated by black arrows","answerEn":"Osteoblasts","answerZh":"成骨细胞","explanationEn":"They line the bone surface and deposit organic bone matrix.","explanationZh":"这些细胞沿骨表面排列，合成并沉积有机骨基质。"},{"key":"C","whereZh":"图中偏左、蓝色箭头所指、已被粉红基质包围的细胞","whereEn":"The cell embedded in pink matrix near the left center, indicated by the blue arrow","answerEn":"Osteocyte","answerZh":"骨细胞","explanationEn":"Its embedded position distinguishes it from surface osteoblasts.","explanationZh":"已经包埋在基质内的位置，使它区别于表面排列的成骨细胞。"},{"key":"D","whereZh":"右下缘、绿色向下箭头所指的浅粉色表面薄层","whereEn":"The pale pink superficial layer at the lower right, indicated by the downward green arrow","answerEn":"Osteoid","answerZh":"类骨质","explanationEn":"This is the newly deposited unmineralized organic layer adjacent to osteoblasts.","explanationZh":"这是邻近成骨细胞的新生、尚未矿化的有机基质层。"},{"key":"E","whereZh":"中央绿色星号所在的大片粉红区域","whereEn":"The broad pink region marked by the central green star","answerEn":"Bone matrix","answerZh":"骨基质","explanationEn":"The matrix is extracellular material, not the cytoplasm of one giant cell.","explanationZh":"这是细胞外基质，不是某个巨大细胞的胞质。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Osteoclast; B: Osteoblasts; C: Osteocyte; D: Osteoid; E: Bone matrix.","answerZh":"A破骨细胞；B成骨细胞；C骨细胞；D类骨质；E骨基质。","explanationEn":"Read the bone surface first, then distinguish surface cells, embedded cells and extracellular matrix.","explanationZh":"先追踪骨表面，再区分表面细胞、包埋细胞和细胞外基质，避免只看颜色命名。","printedPages":[58,59,60]},{"id":"bone-case-01","chapter":"04","type":"case","topic":"骨折修复与结构功能","stemEn":"During fracture repair, a biopsy shows cuboidal basophilic cells lining newly formed bone, cells embedded in lacunae, and large multinucleated cells on other bone surfaces. Answer the following questions.","stemZh":"骨折修复时，活检显示新生骨表面有立方形嗜碱性细胞，陷窝内有包埋细胞，另一些骨表面有巨大多核细胞。回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Identify the surface-forming cells and the large multinucleated cells, and state their respective functions.","promptZh":"指出表面造骨细胞与巨大多核细胞，并分别说明功能。","answerEn":"The cuboidal basophilic cells are osteoblasts, which synthesize osteoid. The large multinucleated cells are osteoclasts, which resorb mineralized bone and its organic matrix.","answerZh":"立方形嗜碱性细胞是成骨细胞，合成类骨质；巨大多核细胞是破骨细胞，吸收骨矿物和有机基质。","explanationEn":"Location, nuclear number and matrix-forming versus resorptive activity distinguish these populations.","explanationZh":"结合表面位置、核数及形成/吸收基质的功能，区分两类细胞；成骨细胞不会直接转变为破骨细胞。"},{"promptEn":"Why do active osteoblasts have basophilic cytoplasm, and how does osteoid differ from mineralized bone?","promptZh":"活跃成骨细胞胞质为何嗜碱？类骨质与矿化骨有何不同？","answerEn":"Active osteoblasts have abundant ribosomes and rough endoplasmic reticulum for matrix-protein synthesis. Osteoid is unmineralized organic matrix; deposition of hydroxyapatite subsequently produces mineralized bone matrix.","answerZh":"活跃成骨细胞含丰富核糖体和粗面内质网，用于合成基质蛋白。类骨质是尚未矿化的有机基质，随后沉积羟基磷灰石形成矿化骨基质。","explanationEn":"Basophilia reflects protein-synthetic machinery, whereas mineralization is a later extracellular event.","explanationZh":"嗜碱性反映蛋白合成设备丰富；矿化则是随后发生的细胞外过程，不能把类骨质直接等同钙盐。"},{"promptEn":"How do the cells embedded in the mineralized matrix obtain nutrients and communicate?","promptZh":"包埋于矿化基质中的细胞怎样获得营养并相互联系？","answerEn":"These cells are osteocytes. Their cell bodies occupy lacunae and their processes extend through canaliculi containing tissue fluid. Nutrients reach this fluid network from nearby vessels in vascular canals, and gap junctions link adjacent osteocyte processes.","answerZh":"这些细胞是骨细胞，胞体位于骨陷窝，突起伸入含组织液的骨小管。营养从邻近血管通道内的血管到达这一组织液网络，相邻突起经缝隙连接联系。","explanationEn":"Blood vessels occupy larger vascular canals; individual canaliculi carry processes and fluid rather than capillaries.","explanationZh":"血管位于较大的血管通道，单根骨小管内是突起和组织液，并非各有毛细血管。"}],"answerEn":"Osteoblasts form osteoid, osteoclasts resorb bone, and osteocytes use a canalicular fluid network for exchange.","answerZh":"成骨细胞形成类骨质，破骨细胞吸收骨，骨细胞依靠骨小管组织液网络交换物质。","explanationEn":"Link each cell to its position, synthetic or resorptive apparatus, and contribution to coordinated bone remodeling.","explanationZh":"把细胞位置、合成或吸收设备、骨改建中的任务联系起来，而不是仅凭“修复”猜细胞名称。","printedPages":[58,59,60,61,67]},{"id":"muscle-mcq-01","chapter":"05","type":"single_choice","topic":"滑行学说与肌节条带","stemEn":"During shortening of a skeletal-muscle sarcomere, which region remains essentially unchanged in length?","stemZh":"骨骼肌肌节缩短时，哪一区域的长度基本保持不变？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"The I band","zh":"I带"},{"key":"B","en":"The H zone","zh":"H带"},{"key":"C","en":"The A band","zh":"A带"},{"key":"D","en":"The distance between two Z discs","zh":"两条Z线之间的距离"}],"answerEn":"C. The A band","answerZh":"C. A带","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"The I band narrows as thin filaments slide further into the A band.","zh":"细肌丝进一步滑入A带，I带变窄。"},{"key":"B","en":"The H zone narrows and may disappear as overlap increases.","zh":"肌丝重叠增多时H带变窄，甚至可消失。"},{"key":"C","en":"The A band corresponds to thick-filament length; the filaments slide rather than shorten.","zh":"A带对应粗肌丝全长；收缩时发生肌丝滑行，粗肌丝自身长度基本不变。"},{"key":"D","en":"The distance between adjacent Z discs is sarcomere length, which decreases during shortening.","zh":"相邻Z线之间就是肌节，收缩时这段距离缩短。"}],"explanationEn":"The A band corresponds to thick-filament length; the filaments slide rather than shorten.","explanationZh":"A带对应粗肌丝全长；收缩时发生肌丝滑行，粗肌丝自身长度基本不变。","printedPages":[87]},{"id":"muscle-mcq-02","chapter":"05","type":"single_choice","topic":"红白肌纤维与耐疲劳性","stemEn":"A skeletal-muscle fiber is rich in myoglobin, mitochondria and capillaries and is adapted for prolonged activity. Which type best fits this description?","stemZh":"某骨骼肌纤维肌红蛋白多、线粒体和毛细血管丰富，适于长时间活动，最符合哪一类型？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A slow oxidative fiber","zh":"慢氧化型纤维"},{"key":"B","en":"A fast glycolytic fiber","zh":"快糖酵解型纤维"},{"key":"C","en":"A smooth-muscle cell","zh":"平滑肌细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"A platelet","zh":"血小板"}],"answerEn":"A. A slow oxidative fiber","answerZh":"A. 慢氧化型纤维","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Myoglobin and oxidative machinery support sustained ATP supply and resistance to fatigue.","zh":"肌红蛋白与丰富的氧化代谢设备支持持续供ATP和耐疲劳，符合本书的红肌纤维／慢缩纤维描述。"},{"key":"B","en":"Fast glycolytic fibers favor rapid force generation and fatigue more readily; they are not the best fit for these combined features.","zh":"快糖酵解纤维偏向短时快速产力、较易疲劳，不符合这组持续供能特征。"},{"key":"C","en":"The stem explicitly describes a skeletal-muscle fiber type; smooth muscle is a different tissue class.","zh":"题干明确比较骨骼肌内部的纤维类型，平滑肌是另一类肌组织。"},{"key":"D","en":"A platelet is an anucleate blood-cell fragment, not a skeletal-muscle fiber.","zh":"血小板是无核血细胞胞质碎片，不属于骨骼肌纤维。"}],"explanationEn":"Myoglobin and oxidative machinery support sustained ATP supply and resistance to fatigue.","explanationZh":"肌红蛋白与丰富的氧化代谢设备支持持续供ATP和耐疲劳，符合本书的红肌纤维／慢缩纤维描述。","printedPages":[58,59,87,88]},{"id":"muscle-mcq-03","chapter":"05","type":"single_choice","topic":"三联体组成","stemEn":"Which combination forms a skeletal-muscle triad?","stemZh":"下列哪一组合构成骨骼肌三联体？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Three T-tubules","zh":"三条横小管"},{"key":"B","en":"One T-tubule and one terminal cisterna","zh":"一条横小管与一个终池"},{"key":"C","en":"Two T-tubules and one terminal cisterna","zh":"两条横小管与一个终池"},{"key":"D","en":"One T-tubule and two terminal cisternae","zh":"一条横小管与两个终池"}],"answerEn":"D. One T-tubule and two terminal cisternae","answerZh":"D. 一条横小管与两个终池","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"The three components are not three identical T-tubules.","zh":"三个组成部分并不是三条相同的横小管。"},{"key":"B","en":"This describes a diad, typically associated with cardiac muscle.","zh":"这描述的是二联体，典型见于心肌。"},{"key":"C","en":"A triad has one membrane invagination flanked by two SR cisternae, not two T-tubules.","zh":"三联体是一条肌膜内陷结构两侧各有一个肌质网终池，不是两条横管。"},{"key":"D","en":"A central T-tubule lies beside a terminal cisterna of the sarcoplasmic reticulum on each side.","zh":"中央是一条横小管，两侧各有一个肌质网终池，合计三个部分。"}],"explanationEn":"A central T-tubule lies beside a terminal cisterna of the sarcoplasmic reticulum on each side.","explanationZh":"中央是一条横小管，两侧各有一个肌质网终池，合计三个部分。","printedPages":[86,87]},{"id":"muscle-tf-01","chapter":"05","type":"true_false","topic":"闰盘的两类联系","stemEn":"Gap junctions in intercalated discs permit electrical coupling, whereas adherens junctions and desmosomes provide mechanical attachment.","stemZh":"闰盘中的缝隙连接允许电耦联，黏着连接和桥粒提供机械附着。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"Gap-junction channels allow ions to pass between adjacent cardiomyocytes. Adherens junctions and desmosomes link their contractile or cytoskeletal structures mechanically.","explanationZh":"缝隙连接通道允许离子在相邻心肌细胞间通过；黏着连接和桥粒则把收缩或骨架结构机械性地联系起来。","printedPages":[89,90]},{"id":"muscle-tf-02","chapter":"05","type":"true_false","topic":"平滑肌无横纹的原因","stemEn":"Smooth muscle lacks cross-striations because its cells contain neither actin nor myosin filaments.","stemZh":"平滑肌没有横纹，是因为其细胞既无肌动蛋白肌丝也无肌球蛋白肌丝。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Smooth muscle contains thick and thin filaments, but they are not organized into regularly repeating sarcomeres. Dense bodies and dense plaques anchor its contractile apparatus.","explanationZh":"平滑肌有粗、细肌丝，只是不形成规则重复的肌节。其收缩装置与密体、密斑等相连，所以无横纹不能推出无肌丝。","printedPages":[92]},{"id":"muscle-def-01","chapter":"05","type":"definition","topic":"肌节","stemEn":"Define a sarcomere.","stemZh":"解释肌节。","answerEn":"A sarcomere is the segment of a myofibril between two adjacent Z discs and is the basic structural and functional contractile unit of striated muscle.","answerZh":"肌节是相邻两条Z线之间的一段肌原纤维，是横纹肌收缩的基本结构和功能单位。","explanationEn":"The definition needs the Z-disc boundaries and the contractile-unit role. A sarcomere contains one A band and one half of an I band at each end.","explanationZh":"得分核心是相邻Z线之间的边界和收缩单位作用。组成可理解为半个I带、一个A带、半个I带。","printedPages":[84,86]},{"id":"muscle-image-01","chapter":"05","type":"image_label","topic":"肌节中粗细肌丝和条带","stemEn":"Identify structures A-E from the textual locations in the original sarcomere diagram. Do not use the unclear original M-line leader as an identification cue.","stemZh":"根据文字定位识别原肌节图中的A-E结构。原图M线引线不清，不将其作为本题识别依据。","image":{"stem":"muscle-image-01","targets":[{"key":"A","whereZh":"图最左端或最右端、黑色锯齿样边界","whereEn":"The black zigzag boundary at either end of the diagram","answerEn":"Z disc (Z line)","answerZh":"Z线","explanationEn":"Thin filaments attach at the Z discs, which bound a sarcomere.","explanationZh":"细肌丝附着在Z线上，两条相邻Z线界定一个肌节。"},{"key":"B","whereZh":"图中水平延伸的红色较粗长条","whereEn":"The thick red horizontal filaments","answerEn":"Thick filaments","answerZh":"粗肌丝","explanationEn":"The red filaments represent myosin-containing thick filaments spanning the A band.","explanationZh":"红色代表以肌球蛋白为主的粗肌丝，其全长对应A带。"},{"key":"C","whereZh":"从两端Z线向中央伸出的黑色细线","whereEn":"The thin black filaments extending inward from the Z discs","answerEn":"Thin filaments","answerZh":"细肌丝","explanationEn":"Thin filaments extend from the Z discs and overlap thick filaments toward the center.","explanationZh":"细肌丝自Z线伸向中央，并在A带外侧与粗肌丝重叠。"},{"key":"D","whereZh":"顶部黑色大括线所跨、对应红色粗肌丝全长的区域","whereEn":"The region spanned by the large upper bracket across the full thick-filament length","answerEn":"A band","answerZh":"A带","explanationEn":"The A band includes the entire thick-filament length, with overlap regions on either side of the H zone.","explanationZh":"A带包含粗肌丝全长，既有重叠区，也包括中央只有粗肌丝的H带。"},{"key":"E","whereZh":"顶部H band小括线所跨、中央没有黑色细肌丝的区域","whereEn":"The central region beneath the H-band bracket, where thin black filaments are absent","answerEn":"H zone (H band)","answerZh":"H带","explanationEn":"This central part of the A band contains thick but not thin filaments.","explanationZh":"H带是A带中央仅有粗肌丝、没有细肌丝的部分。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Z disc; B: Thick filaments; C: Thin filaments; D: A band; E: H zone.","answerZh":"A Z线；B粗肌丝；C细肌丝；D A带；E H带。","explanationEn":"Anchor the two Z discs first, then follow filament lengths to establish the bands rather than memorizing label positions.","explanationZh":"先定两端Z线，再顺着粗细肌丝的实际范围判断条带，避免照背文字和引线位置。","printedPages":[85,86]},{"id":"muscle-case-01","chapter":"05","type":"case","topic":"心肌连接损伤与同步收缩","stemEn":"After myocardial injury, tissue sections show branched striated cells with central nuclei. Examination of their junctions reveals damage to both mechanical attachments and intercellular communicating channels. Answer the following questions.","stemZh":"心肌损伤后，组织切片可见有分支、有横纹、中央核的细胞。检查发现其连接处的机械附着和细胞间通讯通道均受损。回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Identify the muscle tissue and the specialized junctional region between its cells. Give two supporting morphological features.","promptZh":"指出肌组织类型及细胞之间的特殊连接区域，并给出两条形态依据。","answerEn":"This is cardiac muscle. The specialized junctional region is the intercalated disc. Branching cells and centrally located nuclei, together with striations, support this identification.","answerZh":"这是心肌，细胞间特殊连接区域为闰盘。细胞分支、核位于中央，并有横纹，支持此判断。","explanationEn":"Striations alone also occur in skeletal muscle; combine them with branching and nuclear position.","explanationZh":"单凭横纹不能排除骨骼肌，必须结合分支和核的位置。"},{"promptEn":"Which junctions provide mechanical attachment, and what would their damage impair?","promptZh":"哪些连接提供机械附着？受损后会影响什么？","answerEn":"Fascia adherens and desmosomes provide mechanical attachment. Their damage weakens force transmission and the ability of adjacent cells to remain attached during repeated contraction.","answerZh":"黏着连接和桥粒提供机械附着；受损会削弱力的传递，以及细胞在反复收缩时保持连接的能力。","explanationEn":"Mechanical junctions link contractile or cytoskeletal structures, so their role differs from ion conduction.","explanationZh":"机械连接把收缩或骨架结构联系起来，作用不同于离子传导。"},{"promptEn":"Which junction allows electrical coupling, and why does its loss interfere with coordinated contraction?","promptZh":"哪种连接允许电耦联？其丧失为何影响协调收缩？","answerEn":"Gap junctions allow ions to pass directly between neighboring cardiomyocytes, spreading depolarization. Their loss disrupts electrical coupling and coordinated activation of the myocardium.","answerZh":"缝隙连接使离子直接通过相邻心肌细胞，传播去极化。丧失这些连接会破坏电耦联和心肌协调兴奋。","explanationEn":"The myocardium contains separate cells; coordinated activation relies partly on their communicating junctions.","explanationZh":"心肌由独立细胞组成，相邻细胞的通讯连接是协调兴奋的重要基础。"}],"answerEn":"Cardiac muscle uses intercalated discs for both mechanical attachment and gap-junction-mediated electrical coupling.","answerZh":"心肌通过闰盘实现机械附着和缝隙连接介导的电耦联。","explanationEn":"Separate the mechanical and electrical components, then relate each structural defect to the function it compromises.","explanationZh":"把机械与电联系拆开解释，再说明各自损伤如何影响功能，比只写“闰盘受损”更完整。","printedPages":[88,89,90]},{"id":"blood-mcq-01","chapter":"06","type":"single_choice","topic":"网织红细胞识别","stemEn":"A supravital stain shows a blue reticular pattern in an anucleate erythroid cell. What is the cell?","stemZh":"活体染色显示一枚无核红系细胞内有蓝色网状结构，该细胞是什么？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A mature erythrocyte","zh":"成熟红细胞"},{"key":"B","en":"A reticulocyte","zh":"网织红细胞"},{"key":"C","en":"A lymphocyte","zh":"淋巴细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"A megakaryocyte","zh":"巨核细胞"}],"answerEn":"B. A reticulocyte","answerZh":"B. 网织红细胞","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"A mature erythrocyte has lost the residual ribosomal RNA that produces the reticulum.","zh":"成熟红细胞已基本失去形成网状染色的残余核糖体RNA。"},{"key":"B","en":"A reticulocyte is an immature, already anucleate erythrocyte with residual ribosomal RNA.","zh":"网织红细胞是已经无核、仍保留少量核糖体RNA的幼稚红细胞。"},{"key":"C","en":"A lymphocyte has a nucleus; a dark nucleus is different from a supravital RNA reticulum.","zh":"淋巴细胞有核；深染细胞核不同于活体染色显示的RNA网。"},{"key":"D","en":"A megakaryocyte is a very large nucleated marrow cell that forms platelets.","zh":"巨核细胞是骨髓内巨大有核细胞，其胞质形成血小板。"}],"explanationEn":"A reticulocyte is an immature, already anucleate erythrocyte with residual ribosomal RNA.","explanationZh":"网织红细胞是已经无核、仍保留少量核糖体RNA的幼稚红细胞。","printedPages":[72,81]},{"id":"blood-mcq-02","chapter":"06","type":"single_choice","topic":"嗜酸性粒细胞形态功能","stemEn":"Which leukocyte typically has a bilobed nucleus and coarse orange-red granules and participates in defense against helminths?","stemZh":"哪种白细胞通常有双叶核、粗大橘红色颗粒，并参与抗蠕虫防御？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A neutrophil","zh":"中性粒细胞"},{"key":"B","en":"An eosinophil","zh":"嗜酸性粒细胞"},{"key":"C","en":"A basophil","zh":"嗜碱性粒细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"A monocyte","zh":"单核细胞"}],"answerEn":"B. An eosinophil","answerZh":"B. 嗜酸性粒细胞","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Neutrophils usually have segmented nuclei and finer, paler granules; they are prominent in acute bacterial inflammation.","zh":"中性粒细胞通常核分叶、颗粒较细淡，突出参与急性细菌性炎症。"},{"key":"B","en":"The combination of a typically bilobed nucleus, coarse eosinophilic granules and helminth defense identifies an eosinophil.","zh":"常见双叶核、粗嗜酸性颗粒、抗蠕虫功能三者共同指向嗜酸性粒细胞。"},{"key":"C","en":"Basophils have coarse blue-purple granules that may obscure the nucleus and release inflammatory mediators.","zh":"嗜碱性粒细胞颗粒粗大、蓝紫色，常遮核，并释放炎症介质。"},{"key":"D","en":"Monocytes have an indented or folded nucleus and abundant gray-blue cytoplasm, not dense orange-red specific granules.","zh":"单核细胞核凹陷或折叠、胞质灰蓝丰富，不以密集橘红特异性颗粒为特征。"}],"explanationEn":"The combination of a typically bilobed nucleus, coarse eosinophilic granules and helminth defense identifies an eosinophil.","explanationZh":"常见双叶核、粗嗜酸性颗粒、抗蠕虫功能三者共同指向嗜酸性粒细胞。","printedPages":[73]},{"id":"blood-mcq-03","chapter":"06","type":"single_choice","topic":"血小板来源","stemEn":"Platelets are produced as cytoplasmic fragments of which cell?","stemZh":"血小板是哪一种细胞的胞质碎片？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A reticulocyte","zh":"网织红细胞"},{"key":"B","en":"An osteoclast","zh":"破骨细胞"},{"key":"C","en":"A megakaryocyte","zh":"巨核细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"A plasma cell","zh":"浆细胞"}],"answerEn":"C. A megakaryocyte","answerZh":"C. 巨核细胞","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Reticulocytes mature into erythrocytes; they do not fragment into platelets.","zh":"网织红细胞成熟为红细胞，不形成血小板。"},{"key":"B","en":"Osteoclasts resorb bone and are not the source of platelets, despite being large and multinucleated.","zh":"破骨细胞吸收骨，虽大且多核，也不是血小板来源。"},{"key":"C","en":"Megakaryocytes in marrow release cytoplasmic fragments containing platelet granules and organelles.","zh":"骨髓巨核细胞释放含血小板颗粒和细胞器的胞质碎片，形成血小板。"},{"key":"D","en":"Plasma cells secrete antibodies and do not generate platelets.","zh":"浆细胞分泌抗体，不产生血小板。"}],"explanationEn":"Megakaryocytes in marrow release cytoplasmic fragments containing platelet granules and organelles.","explanationZh":"骨髓巨核细胞释放含血小板颗粒和细胞器的胞质碎片，形成血小板。","printedPages":[50,75,81,82]},{"id":"blood-tf-01","chapter":"06","type":"true_false","topic":"嗜碱性粒细胞与肥大细胞","stemEn":"A basophil is simply a mast cell circulating in the blood.","stemZh":"嗜碱性粒细胞就是在血液中循环的肥大细胞。","answerEn":"False","answerZh":"错误","explanationEn":"Basophils and mast cells share some mediators and allergic functions, but they are distinct cell types with different maturation and tissue-distribution patterns.","explanationZh":"两者可共享部分介质和过敏相关功能，但属于不同细胞类型，成熟方式和分布不同。旧课件的类比不应背成细胞身份等式。","printedPages":[50,73,74]},{"id":"blood-tf-02","chapter":"06","type":"true_false","topic":"淋巴细胞分型证据","stemEn":"Routine light microscopy of a blood smear cannot reliably distinguish T lymphocytes from B lymphocytes.","stemZh":"仅靠普通光镜血涂片不能可靠区分T淋巴细胞和B淋巴细胞。","answerEn":"True","answerZh":"正确","explanationEn":"T and B lymphocytes may have similar routine morphology. Their functional types require additional evidence such as specific immunophenotypic markers.","explanationZh":"T、B淋巴细胞常规形态可相似，功能分型需要特异性免疫表型标记等额外证据，不能只凭细胞大小或深核断定。","printedPages":[49,82]},{"id":"blood-def-01","chapter":"06","type":"definition","topic":"血细胞发生","stemEn":"Define hemopoiesis (hematopoiesis).","stemZh":"解释血细胞发生（造血）。","answerEn":"Hemopoiesis is the production and development of the formed elements of blood from hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells. In adults, it occurs mainly in red bone marrow.","answerZh":"血细胞发生是造血干细胞及祖细胞产生、分化发育为血液有形成分的过程，成年人主要在红骨髓进行。","explanationEn":"Include the production-and-development process, the stem/progenitor-cell origin and the main adult site. Platelet production is also part of hemopoiesis.","explanationZh":"定义应含产生与发育、干/祖细胞来源、成人主要场所；造血不仅包括红细胞，还包括白细胞和血小板形成。","printedPages":[47,48,49,76,77,78,79]},{"id":"blood-image-01","chapter":"06","type":"image_label","topic":"五类白细胞定位","stemEn":"Name the leukocyte in each of the five peripheral micrographs described by A-E. Use nuclear shape and cytoplasmic granules together.","stemZh":"根据A-E文字位置，命名周围五张显微照片中的白细胞，核形和胞质颗粒必须结合判断。","image":{"stem":"blood-image-01","targets":[{"key":"A","whereZh":"左上方真实涂片中，有相连分叶核和细淡颗粒的细胞","whereEn":"The cell with a segmented nucleus and fine pale granules in the upper-left micrograph","answerEn":"Neutrophil","answerZh":"中性粒细胞","explanationEn":"Connected nuclear lobes belong to one nucleus; fine pale granules distinguish it from the coarse-granule cells.","explanationZh":"相连核叶属于一个核，不能答多核细胞；颗粒细淡，与粗颗粒细胞不同。"},{"key":"B","whereZh":"上方中央真实涂片中，双叶核及粗大橘红颗粒的细胞","whereEn":"The bilobed cell with coarse orange-red granules in the upper-middle micrograph","answerEn":"Eosinophil","answerZh":"嗜酸性粒细胞","explanationEn":"The granule color and size complement the bilobed nuclear shape.","explanationZh":"粗大橘红颗粒与双叶核共同支持判断，不能单凭两叶核命名。"},{"key":"C","whereZh":"右上方真实涂片中，深蓝紫颗粒遮盖大部分核的细胞","whereEn":"The cell with coarse blue-purple granules obscuring its nucleus in the upper-right micrograph","answerEn":"Basophil","answerZh":"嗜碱性粒细胞","explanationEn":"A nucleus is present but partly obscured; the cell is not anucleate.","explanationZh":"核被颗粒遮盖不等于无核，蓝紫粗颗粒是重要线索。"},{"key":"D","whereZh":"左下方真实涂片中，大圆深染核占多数、胞质仅为窄边的细胞","whereEn":"The cell with a large dark round nucleus and a thin cytoplasmic rim in the lower-left micrograph","answerEn":"Small lymphocyte","answerZh":"小淋巴细胞","explanationEn":"A high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio is characteristic; routine appearance does not determine T or B lineage.","explanationZh":"核浆比大是典型表现，但普通形态不能进一步可靠分T、B细胞。"},{"key":"E","whereZh":"右下方真实涂片中，凹陷核、灰蓝胞质较多的细胞","whereEn":"The cell with an indented nucleus and abundant gray-blue cytoplasm in the lower-right micrograph","answerEn":"Monocyte","answerZh":"单核细胞","explanationEn":"Its indented nucleus and broader cytoplasm contrast with the small lymphocyte.","explanationZh":"凹陷核和较宽胞质共同支持单核细胞，与小淋巴细胞形成对照。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Neutrophil; B: Eosinophil; C: Basophil; D: Small lymphocyte; E: Monocyte.","answerZh":"A中性粒细胞；B嗜酸性粒细胞；C嗜碱性粒细胞；D小淋巴细胞；E单核细胞。","explanationEn":"Compare nucleus shape, granule appearance and cytoplasmic amount. Different panels need not share an identical scale or color balance.","explanationZh":"合看核形、颗粒和胞质量；不同小图不一定同倍率同色调，不按屏幕直径推算精确细胞大小。","printedPages":[71,73,74,75]},{"id":"blood-case-01","chapter":"06","type":"case","topic":"贫血与骨髓红系反应","stemEn":"A patient develops anemia after blood loss. Several days later, the reticulocyte count rises. Supravital staining shows anucleate red cells with blue reticular material. Answer the following questions about erythrocytes and marrow response.","stemZh":"某患者失血后出现贫血，数日后网织红细胞计数升高。活体染色显示部分无核红细胞内有蓝色网状物。根据红细胞结构和骨髓反应回答以下问题。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Why does a reduction in circulating erythrocytes and hemoglobin cause fatigue? Give two structural features of mature erythrocytes that support their normal function.","promptZh":"循环红细胞和血红蛋白减少为何引起乏力？列出成熟红细胞适应正常功能的两条结构特征。","answerEn":"Reduced hemoglobin lowers the oxygen-carrying capacity of blood and oxygen delivery to tissues. Mature erythrocytes contain abundant hemoglobin and have a flexible biconcave shape that provides a large exchange surface and allows passage through narrow capillaries.","answerZh":"血红蛋白减少会降低血液携氧能力及向组织输氧。成熟红细胞富含血红蛋白，并具有柔韧的双凹圆盘形，可提供较大交换表面并通过狭窄毛细血管。","explanationEn":"The functional link is hemoglobin and gas transport, not the presence of a nucleus.","explanationZh":"功能联系在于血红蛋白和气体运输，而不是“有没有细胞核”。"},{"promptEn":"Identify the cells showing the blue reticulum and explain what the reticulum represents. Are these cells nucleated?","promptZh":"蓝色网状物出现于哪种细胞？网状物代表什么？这些细胞是否有核？","answerEn":"They are reticulocytes, immature erythrocytes containing residual ribosomal RNA that forms a reticular pattern with supravital staining. They are already anucleate.","answerZh":"它们是网织红细胞，即含残余核糖体RNA的幼稚红细胞，活体染色时RNA形成网状图案；此时已经无核。","explanationEn":"The blue RNA reticulum is not a fragmented nucleus. Nuclear extrusion occurs before the reticulocyte stage.","explanationZh":"蓝色RNA网不是破碎的细胞核；排核发生在网织红细胞阶段之前。"},{"promptEn":"What does the reticulocyte rise suggest, and what are the main morphological changes during erythroid maturation?","promptZh":"网织红细胞升高提示什么？红系成熟主要发生哪些形态变化？","answerEn":"It suggests an increased erythropoietic response, mainly in adult red bone marrow. Erythroid cells generally become smaller, chromatin condenses, nucleoli disappear, and the nucleus is eventually extruded. Hemoglobin increases while cytoplasmic RNA decreases, shifting the cytoplasm from basophilic toward eosinophilic.","answerZh":"提示红细胞生成反应增强，成人主要发生于红骨髓。红系细胞一般逐渐变小，染色质凝集、核仁消失，最后排核；血红蛋白增多而胞质RNA减少，使胞质由嗜碱性逐渐转为嗜酸性。","explanationEn":"Interpret the count as evidence of marrow response in this case, not as a diagnosis of one specific disease. Megakaryocytes are an exception to the general decrease in cell size during blood-cell development.","explanationZh":"本例应解释为骨髓反应线索，不能凭网织计数单独确定一种疾病。巨核细胞是血细胞发育中体积变小这一总体趋势的例外。"}],"answerEn":"Anemia lowers oxygen transport; reticulocytes contain residual RNA without a nucleus, and their rise suggests increased erythropoiesis.","answerZh":"贫血降低输氧能力；网织红细胞已无核但保留RNA，增多提示红细胞生成反应增强。","explanationEn":"Connect the clinical symptom to hemoglobin, the stain to residual RNA, and the count change to marrow activity.","explanationZh":"把症状连到血红蛋白，把染色连到残余RNA，把数量变化连到骨髓生成活动，三条证据各有对应层级。","printedPages":[49,50,69,70,72,78,81]},{"id":"07_nerve-01","chapter":"07","type":"single_choice","topic":"尼氏体的结构基础","stemEn":"Which structures form the ultrastructural basis of Nissl bodies?","stemZh":"尼氏体的超微结构基础是哪组结构？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Rough endoplasmic reticulum and free ribosomes","zh":"粗面内质网和游离核糖体"},{"key":"B","en":"Smooth endoplasmic reticulum and Golgi cisternae","zh":"滑面内质网和高尔基扁囊"},{"key":"C","en":"Microtubules and neurofilaments","zh":"微管和神经丝"},{"key":"D","en":"Mitochondria and lysosomes","zh":"线粒体和溶酶体"}],"answerEn":"A. Rough endoplasmic reticulum and free ribosomes","answerZh":"A．粗面内质网和游离核糖体","explanationEn":"Nissl bodies represent aggregates of rough endoplasmic reticulum and free ribosomes. Ribosomal RNA contributes to their basophilia.","explanationZh":"尼氏体是粗面内质网和游离核糖体的聚集表现。核糖体RNA使其具有嗜碱性，联系神经元活跃的蛋白质合成。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Correct: both components contribute to protein synthesis and the basophilic aggregates.","zh":"正确：二者参与蛋白合成并构成嗜碱性聚集。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: smooth ER lacks the attached ribosomes characteristic of rough ER.","zh":"错误：滑面内质网缺少粗面内质网表面附着的核糖体。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: these are cytoskeletal components underlying neurofibrils, not Nissl bodies.","zh":"错误：这是神经原纤维相关骨架成分，不是尼氏体。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: these organelles have metabolic and degradative roles but do not form Nissl bodies.","zh":"错误：二者分别联系代谢及降解，不组成尼氏体。"}],"printedPages":[95,96]},{"id":"07_nerve-02","chapter":"07","type":"single_choice","topic":"中枢和周围成髓鞘细胞","stemEn":"Which statement correctly describes a myelinating Schwann cell?","stemZh":"关于形成髓鞘的施万细胞，哪项描述正确？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"It forms all myelin segments along an entire peripheral axon.","zh":"它形成一整条周围轴突的全部髓鞘节段。"},{"key":"B","en":"It forms one internodal myelin segment around one peripheral axon.","zh":"它围绕一根周围轴突形成一个节间段的髓鞘。"},{"key":"C","en":"It myelinates many axons in the central nervous system.","zh":"它在中枢神经系统为多条轴突形成髓鞘。"},{"key":"D","en":"It surrounds neuronal cell bodies in a ganglion as its main location.","zh":"它主要围绕神经节内神经元胞体分布。"}],"answerEn":"B. It forms one internodal myelin segment around one peripheral axon.","answerZh":"B．它围绕一根周围轴突形成一个节间段的髓鞘。","explanationEn":"A myelinating Schwann cell wraps one segment of one PNS axon. A long axon therefore requires many Schwann cells in sequence.","explanationZh":"一个成髓鞘的施万细胞负责一根周围轴突的一个节间段。长轴突沿途需要许多个施万细胞依次包裹。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: successive Schwann cells form successive internodes.","zh":"错误：一整条长轴突的不同节间段由不同施万细胞形成。"},{"key":"B","en":"Correct: both one axon and one internode define its myelinating territory.","zh":"正确：应同时限定一根轴突、一个节间段。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: oligodendrocytes form CNS myelin and may myelinate segments of multiple axons.","zh":"错误：中枢髓鞘由少突胶质细胞形成，一个细胞可联系多条轴突的节段。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: satellite cells surround neuronal somata in peripheral ganglia.","zh":"错误：围绕周围神经节胞体的是卫星细胞。"}],"printedPages":[104,105,106,108]},{"id":"07_nerve-03","chapter":"07","type":"single_choice","topic":"化学突触的释放机制","stemEn":"An action potential reaches a chemical synaptic terminal. Which event most directly triggers neurotransmitter exocytosis?","stemZh":"动作电位到达化学突触末梢后，哪一事件直接触发递质胞吐？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Synthesis of new Nissl bodies in the axon terminal","zh":"轴突末梢新合成尼氏体"},{"key":"B","en":"Formation of a gap junction across the synaptic cleft","zh":"突触间隙新形成缝隙连接"},{"key":"C","en":"Calcium entry through voltage-gated channels in the presynaptic membrane","zh":"钙离子经突触前膜电压门控通道内流"},{"key":"D","en":"Activation of receptors on the postsynaptic membrane before release","zh":"递质释放前先激活突触后膜受体"}],"answerEn":"C. Calcium entry through voltage-gated channels in the presynaptic membrane","answerZh":"C．钙离子经突触前膜电压门控通道内流","explanationEn":"Presynaptic calcium entry triggers fusion of synaptic vesicles with the presynaptic membrane. The released transmitter then binds postsynaptic receptors.","explanationZh":"前膜钙通道开放后，Ca²⁺内流触发突触小泡与前膜融合；递质先释放，随后才结合突触后膜受体。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: axon terminals do not contain conventional Nissl bodies, and release is not triggered by forming them.","zh":"错误：轴突末梢没有常规光镜尼氏体，释放也不由其新生触发。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: gap junctions are the structural basis of electrical synapses.","zh":"错误：缝隙连接是电突触的结构基础。"},{"key":"C","en":"Correct: calcium influx couples terminal depolarization to vesicle fusion.","zh":"正确：钙内流将末梢去极化与小泡融合连接起来。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: postsynaptic receptor activation follows transmitter release.","zh":"错误：后膜受体的激活位于递质释放之后。"}],"printedPages":[100,101]},{"id":"07_nerve-04","chapter":"07","type":"true_false","topic":"无髓轴突与施万细胞","stemEn":"Peripheral unmyelinated axons lack Schwann-cell association.","stemZh":"周围无髓轴突没有施万细胞伴随。","answerEn":"False. Peripheral unmyelinated axons can be embedded in Schwann-cell cytoplasm without a multilamellar myelin sheath.","answerZh":"错误。周围无髓轴突可嵌入施万细胞胞质，只是没有多层卷绕的髓鞘。","explanationEn":"Absence of myelin is different from absence of a Schwann cell. One nonmyelinating Schwann cell can accommodate several small axons.","explanationZh":"“无髓鞘”不等于“无施万细胞”。非成髓鞘施万细胞可包容多条细小轴突。","printedPages":[108,109]},{"id":"07_nerve-05","chapter":"07","type":"true_false","topic":"血脑屏障的关键封闭结构","stemEn":"Tight junctions between capillary endothelial cells are a key structural basis for restricting paracellular passage across the blood–brain barrier.","stemZh":"毛细血管内皮细胞之间的紧密连接是血脑屏障限制细胞旁通路的关键结构。","answerEn":"True. Endothelial tight junctions seal the paracellular route.","answerZh":"正确。内皮紧密连接封闭细胞之间的通路。","explanationEn":"The basal lamina and astrocyte end-feet support the barrier, but astrocyte end-feet do not replace the endothelial seal.","explanationZh":"基膜和星形胶质足突参与支持、诱导和维持屏障；足突不能替代内皮细胞间的封闭结构。","printedPages":[125]},{"id":"07_nerve-06","chapter":"07","type":"definition","topic":"突触名词解释","stemEn":"Define a synapse. For a chemical synapse, name its three main structural components.","stemZh":"解释突触；对于化学突触，列出三个主要结构成分。","answerEn":"A synapse is a specialized junction that transmits information between neurons or between a neuron and an effector cell. A chemical synapse consists of a presynaptic element, a synaptic cleft and a postsynaptic element.","answerZh":"突触是神经元之间或神经元与效应细胞之间传递信息的特化连接。化学突触包括突触前成分、突触间隙和突触后成分。","explanationEn":"A complete definition identifies the type of junction, the cells connected and its function. For chemical synapses, vesicles belong to the presynaptic element and receptors to the postsynaptic element.","explanationZh":"完整定义包括“是什么连接、连接谁、做什么”。化学突触中小泡属于突触前成分，相应受体属于突触后成分；不要把间隙误写成一种细胞。","printedPages":[99,100,101,102]},{"id":"07_nerve-07","chapter":"07","type":"image_label","topic":"血脑屏障五结构填图","stemEn":"Identify structures 1–5 in the supplied blood–brain barrier diagram. Use the original arrow numbers.","stemZh":"识别所给血脑屏障图的1—5号结构，按原图真实箭头编号作答。","image":{"stem":"07-nerve-07","targets":[{"key":"1","whereEn":"The thin cell directly bordering the central lumen, at arrow 1","whereZh":"1号箭头末端：直接衬中央白色管腔的薄细胞","answerEn":"Capillary endothelial cell","answerZh":"毛细血管内皮细胞","explanationEn":"The endothelial cell forms the innermost cellular lining of the blood vessel.","explanationZh":"直接构成血管腔内侧细胞衬里。"},{"key":"2","whereEn":"The focal junction between adjacent endothelial cells at the lower right","whereZh":"右下2号箭头末端：相邻内皮细胞接缝处","answerEn":"Tight junction","answerZh":"紧密连接","explanationEn":"The seal is at an intercellular junction, rather than in the extracellular basal lamina.","explanationZh":"落点在细胞间连接处，而非细胞外基膜。"},{"key":"3","whereEn":"The thin continuous extracellular layer external to the endothelium at the lower left","whereZh":"左下3号箭头末端：内皮外侧连续薄层","answerEn":"Basement membrane / basal lamina","answerZh":"基膜","explanationEn":"Follow the thin layer around the vessel; it is distinct from the much larger outer cellular processes.","explanationZh":"沿血管外侧薄层追踪，区分它与更外侧大片细胞突起。"},{"key":"4","whereEn":"The perivascular cell cytoplasm at arrow 4, next to its dark nucleus at the upper right","whereZh":"4号箭头末端：贴血管壁的周细胞胞质，右侧相邻可见其深染核","answerEn":"Pericyte","answerZh":"周细胞","explanationEn":"The pericyte lies outside the endothelial tube within the vascular basal-lamina compartment. The arrow does not point to the large surrounding astrocyte end-foot.","explanationZh":"周细胞位于内皮管外、血管基膜相关区域内；箭头指其胞质，不是大片星形胶质足突。"},{"key":"5","whereEn":"The broad surrounding cellular process at the upper left","whereZh":"左上5号箭头末端：包在血管外的大片细胞突起","answerEn":"Astrocyte end-foot","answerZh":"星形胶质细胞足突","explanationEn":"The broad outer process covers the external surface of the capillary rather than lining the lumen.","explanationZh":"大片足突覆盖毛细血管外表面，不直接衬管腔。"}]},"answerEn":"1: Capillary endothelial cell; 2: Tight junction; 3: Basement membrane / basal lamina; 4: Pericyte; 5: Astrocyte end-foot","answerZh":"1：毛细血管内皮细胞；2：紧密连接；3：基膜；4：周细胞；5：星形胶质细胞足突","explanationEn":"Read from lumen to endothelium, then basal lamina and surrounding end-feet. Arrow 4 points to pericyte cytoplasm, whereas arrow 3 points to the basal lamina. The numbers are the original labels in the supplied figure.","explanationZh":"从管腔向外读：内皮、基膜、外围足突。4指周细胞胞质，3指基膜，二者按落点区分。1—5均为用户原图已有编号，不是新造箭头。","printedPages":[125]},{"id":"07_nerve-08","chapter":"07","type":"case","topic":"周围脱髓鞘的结构功能分析","stemEn":"A patient has slowed conduction in a peripheral motor nerve. Electron microscopy shows loss of multilamellar myelin around otherwise continuous axons. The neuronal cell bodies are preserved. Answer the following questions without assigning a specific disease.","stemZh":"一名患者周围运动神经传导减慢。电镜显示轴突总体连续，但周围多层髓鞘减少；神经元胞体保存。请依据结构与功能回答，不必指定病名。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Which glial cell normally forms this myelin, and how much of an axon does one cell myelinate?","promptZh":"正常由哪种胶质细胞形成这种髓鞘？一个细胞负责多大范围？","answerEn":"A Schwann cell forms one internodal segment of myelin around one peripheral axon.","answerZh":"施万细胞围绕一根周围轴突形成一个节间段的髓鞘。","explanationEn":"Peripheral location distinguishes Schwann cells from CNS oligodendrocytes.","explanationZh":"“周围神经”先决定成髓鞘细胞为施万细胞，而非中枢少突胶质细胞。"},{"promptEn":"Explain why loss of myelin can slow conduction.","promptZh":"解释髓鞘丢失为何使传导减慢。","answerEn":"Myelin provides electrical insulation between nodes of Ranvier. Its loss impairs efficient saltatory conduction and may slow or block impulse propagation.","answerZh":"髓鞘使郎飞结之间的轴膜获得电绝缘。丢失后高效跳跃式传导受损，可使冲动传导减慢或阻滞。","explanationEn":"The mechanism connects the insulating internode with action-potential regeneration at nodes; preserved axonal continuity does not guarantee normal conduction.","explanationZh":"将节间段绝缘与结区动作电位再生连起来；轴突形态连续并不保证传导正常。"},{"promptEn":"Would an unmyelinated peripheral axon necessarily lack a Schwann cell? Explain.","promptZh":"周围无髓轴突是否一定没有施万细胞？说明理由。","answerEn":"No. Unmyelinated peripheral axons may be embedded in Schwann-cell cytoplasm, but the cell membrane is not wrapped into a thick multilamellar myelin sheath.","answerZh":"不一定。周围无髓轴突可嵌入施万细胞胞质，但细胞膜没有反复卷绕形成厚的多层髓鞘。","explanationEn":"Distinguish the presence of a supporting glial cell from the presence of compact myelin.","explanationZh":"区分“有胶质细胞支持”和“有致密多层髓鞘”这两个不同层次。"}],"answerEn":"1. A Schwann cell forms one internodal segment of myelin around one peripheral axon. 2. Myelin provides electrical insulation between nodes of Ranvier. Its loss impairs efficient saltatory conduction and may slow or block impulse propagation. 3. No. Unmyelinated peripheral axons may be embedded in Schwann-cell cytoplasm, but the cell membrane is not wrapped into a thick multilamellar myelin sheath.","answerZh":"1．施万细胞围绕一根周围轴突形成一个节间段的髓鞘。 2．髓鞘使郎飞结之间的轴膜获得电绝缘。丢失后高效跳跃式传导受损，可使冲动传导减慢或阻滞。 3．不一定。周围无髓轴突可嵌入施万细胞胞质，但细胞膜没有反复卷绕形成厚的多层髓鞘。","explanationEn":"Connect each observation to a histological structure and then to its function. Do not infer a specific disease from nonspecific findings alone.","explanationZh":"每小问按“病例线索—组织结构—功能后果”作答。病例用于解释结构与功能，不由单一非特异表现强行确诊某种疾病。","printedPages":[105,106,108,109]},{"id":"08_circulation-01","chapter":"08","type":"single_choice","topic":"弹性动脉的结构与功能","stemEn":"Which feature best explains how the aorta helps maintain blood flow during ventricular diastole?","stemZh":"哪项结构最能解释主动脉为何有助于在心室舒张期维持血流？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Numerous elastic lamellae in the tunica media","zh":"中膜含大量弹性板"},{"key":"B","en":"Valves projecting into the lumen","zh":"伸入管腔的瓣膜"},{"key":"C","en":"An endothelium with large intercellular gaps","zh":"内皮细胞间有大间隙"},{"key":"D","en":"A wall composed only of smooth muscle","zh":"管壁完全由平滑肌组成"}],"answerEn":"A. Numerous elastic lamellae in the tunica media","answerZh":"A．中膜含大量弹性板","explanationEn":"Elastic lamellae stretch during systole and recoil during diastole, helping maintain forward blood flow between ventricular ejections.","explanationZh":"弹性板在心室收缩时扩张储能，在舒张时回缩释能，有助于维持两次射血之间的连续血流。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Correct: elastic recoil supports continued flow during diastole.","zh":"正确：弹性回缩支持舒张期继续向前的血流。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: this is a feature of many veins, not the mechanism of aortic recoil.","zh":"错误：管腔瓣膜常见于相应静脉，不是主动脉回缩的机制。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: large endothelial gaps characterize some sinusoids rather than the aortic wall.","zh":"错误：大内皮间隙联系部分血窦，不是主动脉管壁的特征。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: the aortic media contains abundant elastic lamellae as well as smooth muscle.","zh":"错误：主动脉中膜除平滑肌外还有大量弹性板，并非全由平滑肌组成。"}],"printedPages":[131,133]},{"id":"08_circulation-02","chapter":"08","type":"single_choice","topic":"有孔毛细血管的内皮与基膜","stemEn":"Which combination characterizes a typical fenestrated capillary?","stemZh":"哪组特点符合典型有孔毛细血管？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Large intercellular gaps with an absent or discontinuous basal lamina","zh":"较大细胞间隙，基膜缺失或不连续"},{"key":"B","en":"Endothelial fenestrae with a necessarily discontinuous basal lamina","zh":"内皮有窗孔，且基膜必定不连续"},{"key":"C","en":"Endothelial fenestrae with a continuous basal lamina","zh":"内皮有窗孔，基膜连续"},{"key":"D","en":"No endothelial lining and a thick smooth-muscle wall","zh":"没有内皮衬里，管壁含厚层平滑肌"}],"answerEn":"C. Endothelial fenestrae with a continuous basal lamina","answerZh":"C．内皮有窗孔，基膜连续","explanationEn":"Fenestrae pass through endothelial cells, whereas the basal lamina remains continuous. Endothelial fenestrae and gaps between adjacent cells are different structures.","explanationZh":"窗孔穿过内皮细胞本身，有孔毛细血管的基膜仍连续。细胞内窗孔与相邻细胞之间的间隙不是一回事。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: this describes important features of a sinusoid.","zh":"错误：这是血窦的重要特征组合。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: endothelial pores do not imply that the basal lamina is interrupted.","zh":"错误：内皮有孔并不意味着基膜也断裂。"},{"key":"C","en":"Correct: endothelial fenestrae and a continuous basal lamina distinguish this type.","zh":"正确：有孔内皮加连续基膜是本型关键组合。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: capillaries are endothelial-lined vessels and lack a thick tunica media.","zh":"错误：毛细血管有内皮，也没有厚的中膜。"}],"printedPages":[134,135,136,137]},{"id":"08_circulation-03","chapter":"08","type":"single_choice","topic":"静脉瓣的组织来源","stemEn":"A thin leaflet projects into the lumen of a vein. Which part of the vessel wall forms the venous valve?","stemZh":"静脉腔内见薄叶状结构，静脉瓣由管壁哪部分形成？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"A fold of the tunica media alone","zh":"单独由中膜折叠形成"},{"key":"B","en":"A fold of the tunica adventitia","zh":"由外膜折叠形成"},{"key":"C","en":"A free sheet of elastic tissue without endothelial covering","zh":"没有内皮覆盖的游离弹性组织片"},{"key":"D","en":"A fold of the tunica intima with a connective-tissue core covered by endothelium","zh":"内膜折叠，结缔组织为核心，表面覆盖内皮"}],"answerEn":"D. A fold of the tunica intima with a connective-tissue core covered by endothelium","answerZh":"D．内膜折叠，结缔组织为核心，表面覆盖内皮","explanationEn":"Venous valves are intimal folds. Their connective-tissue core is covered by endothelium, and their orientation helps limit reverse blood flow.","explanationZh":"静脉瓣是内膜折叠，结缔组织为核心，两面有内皮覆盖；瓣的朝向有助于限制血液倒流。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: a venous valve is not an isolated fold of smooth-muscle-rich media.","zh":"错误：静脉瓣并非富平滑肌的中膜单独折入。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: the adventitia lies outside the vessel, not at the luminal surface.","zh":"错误：外膜位于血管外侧，不直接形成腔面瓣叶。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: the leaflet retains an endothelial surface.","zh":"错误：瓣叶表面有内皮，不能写成无内皮游离组织片。"},{"key":"D","en":"Correct: the intimal origin and endothelial covering explain its continuity with the luminal wall.","zh":"正确：内膜来源及内皮覆盖解释其与血管腔面连续。"}],"printedPages":[137,138]},{"id":"08_circulation-04","chapter":"08","type":"true_false","topic":"心脏浦肯野纤维的组织属性","stemEn":"Cardiac Purkinje fibers are bundles of neuronal axons located beneath the endocardium.","stemZh":"心脏浦肯野纤维是位于心内膜下的神经元轴突束。","answerEn":"False. They are specialized cardiac muscle cells of the cardiac conduction system.","answerZh":"错误。它们是心脏传导系统中的特化心肌细胞。","explanationEn":"Purkinje fibers have a cardiac-muscle origin. Their pale cytoplasm and conduction role do not make them nervous tissue; cerebellar Purkinje cells are a different structure.","explanationZh":"浦肯野纤维属于心肌。胞质浅染和传导功能不能把它改判成神经组织；小脑浦肯野细胞则是另一种结构。","printedPages":[140,141]},{"id":"08_circulation-05","chapter":"08","type":"true_false","topic":"周细胞的位置","stemEn":"A pericyte lies outside the endothelial layer of a capillary and is associated with its basal lamina.","stemZh":"周细胞位于毛细血管内皮层外侧，并与基膜相关。","answerEn":"True. Pericytes occupy a perivascular position outside the endothelial tube.","answerZh":"正确。周细胞位于内皮管外的血管周围位置。","explanationEn":"The inner luminal lining is endothelium. A pericyte does not replace that lining and is not an erythrocyte within the lumen.","explanationZh":"衬管腔的最内层是内皮。周细胞既不替代内皮，也不是管腔内的红细胞。","printedPages":[134,135]},{"id":"08_circulation-06","chapter":"08","type":"definition","topic":"毛细血管名词解释","stemEn":"Define a blood capillary and relate its wall structure to exchange.","stemZh":"解释血毛细血管，并联系其管壁结构说明交换功能。","answerEn":"A blood capillary is a small blood vessel whose wall consists mainly of a single endothelial layer and an associated basal lamina. Its thin wall provides a short diffusion distance for exchange between blood and surrounding tissues. Capillaries include continuous, fenestrated and sinusoidal types.","answerZh":"血毛细血管是主要由单层内皮及其相关基膜构成管壁的细小血管。薄的管壁缩短血液与周围组织之间的扩散距离，利于交换；按超微结构分连续型、有孔型和血窦型。","explanationEn":"Name the vessel, its thin endothelial wall and exchange function. Basal-lamina continuity differs by type; do not claim that all capillaries have a continuous basal lamina.","explanationZh":"定义要包含血管类别、薄的内皮性管壁及交换功能。不同类型的基膜连续性不同，不能把“基膜连续”当成所有毛细血管共同的绝对条件。","printedPages":[134,137]},{"id":"08_circulation-07","chapter":"08","type":"image_label","topic":"毛细血管三类型与两种超微结构","stemEn":"Use the five textual locations A–E to identify three capillary types and two wall structures. The letters are prompts, not new arrows on the original slide.","stemZh":"按A—E五处文字定位，识别三类毛细血管及两种管壁结构。字母是文字提示，不是原图新增箭头。","image":{"stem":"08-circulation-07","targets":[{"key":"A","whereEn":"The leftmost of the three colored vessel models along the lower left","whereZh":"左下方三个彩色血管模型中最左一个，内皮无大量穿孔","answerEn":"Continuous capillary","answerZh":"连续毛细血管","explanationEn":"The endothelial layer and outer basal lamina are continuous; the many small vesicles are not fenestrae.","explanationZh":"内皮层与外侧基膜连续；小泡不是窗孔。"},{"key":"B","whereEn":"The middle of the three colored vessel models along the lower left","whereZh":"左下方三个彩色模型中间一个，内皮布满小孔，外侧薄层连续","answerEn":"Fenestrated capillary","answerZh":"有孔毛细血管","explanationEn":"Pores perforate the endothelial cell, while the basal lamina remains continuous.","explanationZh":"孔穿过内皮细胞本身，而其外侧基膜保持连续。"},{"key":"C","whereEn":"The rightmost of the three colored vessel models along the lower left","whereZh":"左下方三个彩色模型中最右一个，管腔宽、不规则，壁有较大开口","answerEn":"Sinusoid / sinusoidal capillary","answerZh":"血窦／血窦型毛细血管","explanationEn":"Large openings and discontinuous basal lamina distinguish this model from the other two.","explanationZh":"较大开口和不连续基膜使它区别于前两型。"},{"key":"D","whereEn":"A small pore through the wall of the middle colored vessel model, beside the Fenestra label","whereZh":"中间彩色模型上Fenestra标记附近、穿过内皮细胞壁的小孔","answerEn":"Fenestra / endothelial pore","answerZh":"窗孔／内皮细胞孔","explanationEn":"The pore is within an endothelial cell, rather than the space between two cells.","explanationZh":"这是内皮细胞内的孔，不是两个内皮细胞之间的间隙。"},{"key":"E","whereEn":"The thin external layer indicated by Basement membrane above the middle colored vessel model","whereZh":"中间彩色模型上方Basement membrane引线所指的外侧连续薄层","answerEn":"Basement membrane / basal lamina","answerZh":"基膜","explanationEn":"Its continuity is assessed separately from the presence of endothelial fenestrae.","explanationZh":"基膜是否连续，需要与内皮是否有窗孔分别判断。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Continuous capillary; B: Fenestrated capillary; C: Sinusoid / sinusoidal capillary; D: Fenestra / endothelial pore; E: Basement membrane / basal lamina","answerZh":"A：连续毛细血管；B：有孔毛细血管；C：血窦／血窦型毛细血管；D：窗孔／内皮细胞孔；E：基膜","explanationEn":"Use the described locations A–E. These letters are textual prompts, not additional arrows drawn on the source figure.","explanationZh":"按文字定位A–E识别。字母属于本题的文字提示，不代表原图新增了A–E箭头；原课件现有标注保留，用作识图练习。","printedPages":[134,135,136,137]},{"id":"08_circulation-08","chapter":"08","type":"case","topic":"弹性回缩受损的结构功能分析","stemEn":"A section from a large artery near the heart shows numerous elastic lamellae in the tunica media. In another specimen from the same arterial region, many lamellae are fragmented and elastic recoil is reduced. Relate these findings to normal vessel function.","stemZh":"近心端大动脉切片的中膜含大量弹性板。来自相同动脉区域的另一标本中，许多弹性板碎裂，弹性回缩减弱。请联系正常血管功能分析。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Identify the artery type and give the key histological evidence.","promptZh":"判断动脉类型并给出关键组织学依据。","answerEn":"It is an elastic artery. The key feature is the numerous elastic lamellae distributed throughout the tunica media.","answerZh":"这是弹性动脉，关键依据是中膜内广泛分布的大量弹性板。","explanationEn":"Artery type is determined from medial composition, not simply from a large lumen or the presence of one elastic line.","explanationZh":"按中膜成分判断，不能只凭管腔大或看到一条弹性线。"},{"promptEn":"Explain how the normal wall contributes to blood flow during systole and diastole.","promptZh":"说明正常管壁在收缩期和舒张期怎样帮助血流。","answerEn":"The elastic wall expands during ventricular systole, storing part of the energy of ejection. During diastole it recoils, helping maintain forward blood flow between heartbeats. Reduced recoil weakens this buffering function.","answerZh":"弹性管壁在心室收缩时扩张，储存部分射血能量；在舒张时回缩，帮助维持两次心搏之间的前向血流。回缩减弱会削弱这种缓冲作用。","explanationEn":"Connect lamellar stretch and recoil to temporal smoothing of pulsatile flow; no specific diagnosis or treatment follows from the slide alone.","explanationZh":"将弹性板的扩张与回缩联系到脉动血流的平缓化，不凭单张切片指定临床病因或治疗。"},{"promptEn":"How does a muscular artery differ in its media and main functional emphasis?","promptZh":"肌性动脉的中膜成分和功能重点有什么不同？","answerEn":"A muscular artery has a media dominated by circumferential smooth muscle, with a prominent internal elastic lamina. Changes in muscle contraction help regulate distribution of blood to organs.","answerZh":"肌性动脉中膜以环行平滑肌为主，内弹性膜明显；通过平滑肌舒缩调节向器官分配的血流。","explanationEn":"Elastic arteries mainly buffer pulsatile output; muscular arteries emphasize active control of distribution, although both contain smooth muscle and elastic components.","explanationZh":"弹性动脉着重缓冲脉动射血，肌性动脉着重主动调节分配；两者都不是只有一种成分。"}],"answerEn":"1. It is an elastic artery. The key feature is the numerous elastic lamellae distributed throughout the tunica media. 2. The elastic wall expands during ventricular systole, storing part of the energy of ejection. During diastole it recoils, helping maintain forward blood flow between heartbeats. Reduced recoil weakens this buffering function. 3. A muscular artery has a media dominated by circumferential smooth muscle, with a prominent internal elastic lamina. Changes in muscle contraction help regulate distribution of blood to organs.","answerZh":"1．这是弹性动脉，关键依据是中膜内广泛分布的大量弹性板。 2．弹性管壁在心室收缩时扩张，储存部分射血能量；在舒张时回缩，帮助维持两次心搏之间的前向血流。回缩减弱会削弱这种缓冲作用。 3．肌性动脉中膜以环行平滑肌为主，内弹性膜明显；通过平滑肌舒缩调节向器官分配的血流。","explanationEn":"Connect each observation to a histological structure and then to its function. Do not infer a specific disease from nonspecific findings alone.","explanationZh":"每小问按“病例线索—组织结构—功能后果”作答。病例用于解释结构与功能，不由单一非特异表现强行确诊某种疾病。","printedPages":[131,133,134]},{"id":"09_immune-01","chapter":"09","type":"single_choice","topic":"淋巴结T细胞主区","stemEn":"Which region of a lymph node is predominantly populated by T lymphocytes?","stemZh":"淋巴结中哪个区域以T淋巴细胞为主？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Germinal center","zh":"生发中心"},{"key":"B","en":"Paracortex","zh":"副皮质区"},{"key":"C","en":"Medullary sinus","zh":"髓窦"},{"key":"D","en":"Capsule","zh":"被膜"}],"answerEn":"B. Paracortex","answerZh":"B．副皮质区","explanationEn":"The paracortex is the T-cell-rich region. B-cell follicles occupy the superficial cortex, while sinuses carry lymph.","explanationZh":"副皮质区是淋巴结的T细胞主区。浅皮质滤泡以B细胞相关区域为主；髓窦则是淋巴经过的通道。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: germinal centers are associated with activated B-cell responses.","zh":"错误：生发中心联系活化的B细胞反应。"},{"key":"B","en":"Correct: the paracortex is the thymus-dependent, T-cell-rich region.","zh":"正确：副皮质是胸腺依赖区，T细胞占优势。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: medullary sinuses are lymph channels rather than the principal T-cell compartment.","zh":"错误：髓窦是淋巴通道，不是主要T细胞区。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: the capsule is connective tissue surrounding the organ.","zh":"错误：被膜是包围器官的结缔组织。"}],"printedPages":[150]},{"id":"09_immune-02","chapter":"09","type":"single_choice","topic":"胸腺支持网架","stemEn":"Which cells form the principal supporting framework of the thymic parenchyma?","stemZh":"哪种细胞形成胸腺实质的主要支持网架？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Epithelial reticular cells","zh":"上皮网状细胞"},{"key":"B","en":"Schwann cells","zh":"施万细胞"},{"key":"C","en":"Plasma cells","zh":"浆细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"Erythrocytes","zh":"红细胞"}],"answerEn":"A. Epithelial reticular cells","answerZh":"A．上皮网状细胞","explanationEn":"Thymic epithelial reticular cells form an interconnected cellular framework and support the microenvironment for T-cell development.","explanationZh":"胸腺上皮网状细胞形成相互联系的细胞性支架，支持T细胞发育的局部微环境。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Correct: thymic stromal support is primarily epithelial reticular rather than the ordinary reticular-tissue pattern of lymph nodes and spleen.","zh":"正确：胸腺主要为上皮网状细胞支架，不能照搬淋巴结、脾的普通网状组织支架。"},{"key":"B","en":"Incorrect: Schwann cells support peripheral axons and form peripheral myelin.","zh":"错误：施万细胞联系周围轴突及周围髓鞘。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: plasma cells secrete antibodies rather than forming the thymic framework.","zh":"错误：浆细胞主要分泌抗体，不构成胸腺网架。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: erythrocytes carry respiratory gases within the blood.","zh":"错误：红细胞在血液中运输呼吸气体，不构成支持网架。"}],"printedPages":[147,148]},{"id":"09_immune-03","chapter":"09","type":"single_choice","topic":"脾白髓的B与T分区","stemEn":"Which pairing of a splenic compartment with its predominant lymphocyte population is correct?","stemZh":"脾的区域与占优势淋巴细胞的配对，哪项正确？","options":[{"key":"A","en":"Periarteriolar lymphoid sheath — predominantly B cells","zh":"动脉周围淋巴鞘——以B细胞为主"},{"key":"B","en":"Lymphoid follicles in white pulp — predominantly B cells","zh":"白髓淋巴滤泡——以B细胞为主"},{"key":"C","en":"The entire white pulp — B cells only","zh":"全部白髓——仅含B细胞"},{"key":"D","en":"Red pulp — T cells only","zh":"红髓——仅含T细胞"}],"answerEn":"B. Lymphoid follicles in white pulp — predominantly B cells","answerZh":"B．白髓淋巴滤泡——以B细胞为主","explanationEn":"White-pulp follicles are B-cell-rich, whereas the periarteriolar lymphoid sheath is T-cell-rich. Neither white nor red pulp contains only one immune-cell type.","explanationZh":"白髓滤泡以B细胞相关区域为主，PALS则以T细胞为主。白髓或红髓均不能概括成只含一种免疫细胞。","optionExplanations":[{"key":"A","en":"Incorrect: the PALS is the T-cell-rich compartment around a central arteriole.","zh":"错误：PALS是围绕中央小动脉的T细胞主区。"},{"key":"B","en":"Correct: splenic follicles are the B-cell-rich component of white pulp.","zh":"正确：脾滤泡是白髓中B细胞占优势的组成部分。"},{"key":"C","en":"Incorrect: white pulp also includes the T-cell-rich PALS.","zh":"错误：白髓还包含富T细胞的PALS。"},{"key":"D","en":"Incorrect: red pulp contains blood cells, macrophages and other immune cells, not exclusively T cells.","zh":"错误：红髓有血细胞、巨噬细胞等多种成分，并非只有T细胞。"}],"printedPages":[153,154]},{"id":"09_immune-04","chapter":"09","type":"true_false","topic":"初级滤泡与次级滤泡","stemEn":"Every primary lymphoid follicle contains a germinal center.","stemZh":"每个初级淋巴滤泡都有生发中心。","answerEn":"False. A germinal center is a feature of a secondary follicle formed during an antigen-driven response; a primary follicle lacks a germinal center.","answerZh":"错误。生发中心是抗原应答中形成的次级滤泡特征；初级滤泡没有生发中心。","explanationEn":"Differentiate an entire follicle from its germinal center. A secondary follicle includes both a germinal center and surrounding smaller lymphocytes.","explanationZh":"区分“整个滤泡”和“滤泡内部生发中心”。次级滤泡还包括生发中心外围的小淋巴细胞区。","printedPages":[146,147]},{"id":"09_immune-05","chapter":"09","type":"true_false","topic":"高内皮微静脉与淋巴细胞再循环","stemEn":"High endothelial venules provide a route for circulating lymphocytes to enter lymphoid tissue from the blood.","stemZh":"高内皮微静脉为循环淋巴细胞从血液进入淋巴组织提供通路。","answerEn":"True. Lymphocytes cross the specialized venular endothelium to enter lymphoid tissue.","answerZh":"正确。淋巴细胞穿过特化微静脉内皮进入淋巴组织。","explanationEn":"An HEV is a blood vessel, not an afferent lymphatic sinus. Its role in lymphocyte entry differs from lymph flow through node sinuses.","explanationZh":"HEV是血管，不是输入淋巴管或淋巴窦。它负责淋巴细胞从血液迁入，与淋巴沿结内窦道流动是两条不同路径。","printedPages":[146,150,152]},{"id":"09_immune-06","chapter":"09","type":"definition","topic":"血胸腺屏障的定义与组成","stemEn":"Define the blood–thymus barrier and list its components from the capillary lumen toward the thymic cortex.","stemZh":"解释血胸腺屏障，并按毛细血管腔向胸腺皮质的方向列出组成。","answerEn":"The blood–thymus barrier is a multilayered barrier around cortical capillaries that limits exposure of developing thymocytes to blood-borne macromolecular antigens. From the lumen outward it includes continuous capillary endothelium with tight junctions, the endothelial basal lamina, a perivascular space containing macrophages, the basal lamina of epithelial reticular cells, and an epithelial reticular cell layer.","answerZh":"血胸腺屏障是围绕胸腺皮质毛细血管的多层屏障，限制发育中胸腺细胞接触血源性大分子抗原。从腔向外依次为：具有紧密连接的连续毛细血管内皮、内皮基膜、含巨噬细胞的血管周围间隙、上皮网状细胞基膜及上皮网状细胞层。","explanationEn":"Location, protected cells, limiting function and ordered components are separate scoring points. Two basal laminae belong to different cellular layers; the barrier is selective rather than absolutely impermeable.","explanationZh":"位置、保护对象、限制作用和按序组成是不同得分点。两层基膜分别属于两种细胞层，不能合并漏写；屏障具有选择性，而非完全不允许任何物质通过。","printedPages":[149]},{"id":"09_immune-07","chapter":"09","type":"image_label","topic":"血胸腺屏障相关细胞与连接","stemEn":"Identify the five structures at the textual locations A–E in the blood–thymus barrier diagram. Do not interpret the schematic colors as H&E staining.","stemZh":"按A—E文字定位，识别血胸腺屏障图中的五个结构。图示颜色不能当作H&E染色颜色。","image":{"stem":"09-immune-07","targets":[{"key":"A","whereEn":"The thin yellow cell layer directly bordering the central white capillary lumen","whereZh":"中央白色毛细血管腔外、直接衬腔的薄黄色细胞层","answerEn":"Capillary endothelial cell","answerZh":"毛细血管内皮细胞","explanationEn":"Its luminal position distinguishes endothelium from the outer epithelial layer.","explanationZh":"直接衬管腔的位置将内皮与外侧上皮层区分。"},{"key":"B","whereEn":"The junction indicated by the original Tight junction label on the upper-right capillary wall","whereZh":"管壁右上方原Tight junction引线所指的内皮接缝","answerEn":"Tight junction","answerZh":"紧密连接","explanationEn":"It restricts passage between adjacent endothelial cells.","explanationZh":"它限制相邻内皮细胞之间的通路。"},{"key":"C","whereEn":"The large nucleated cell in the reddish perivascular region at the lower left, indicated by Macrophage","whereZh":"左下方红色血管周围区域内、原Macrophage引线所指的大细胞","answerEn":"Macrophage","answerZh":"巨噬细胞","explanationEn":"The cell lies outside the endothelium in the perivascular space and helps remove material.","explanationZh":"位于内皮外的血管周围间隙，参与清除物质。"},{"key":"D","whereEn":"The outer green branching process indicated by Process of epithelial cell","whereZh":"最外侧绿色分支状结构，原Process of epithelial cell引线所指","answerEn":"Epithelial reticular cell process","answerZh":"上皮网状细胞突起","explanationEn":"It belongs to the epithelial support surrounding the vascular compartment, not to the endothelial lining.","explanationZh":"属于包在血管周围的上皮性支持成分，不是内皮衬里。"},{"key":"E","whereEn":"A small round purple cell outside the outer green layer at the original Lymphocyte label","whereZh":"外侧绿色层以外、原Lymphocyte引线所指的小圆形紫色细胞","answerEn":"Thymocyte / developing T lymphocyte","answerZh":"胸腺细胞／发育中的T淋巴细胞","explanationEn":"Within this thymic cortical context, lymphocytes are developing thymocytes; an isolated purple nucleus alone would not establish T-cell identity.","explanationZh":"在胸腺皮质语境下这些为发育中的胸腺细胞；不能脱离位置，仅凭一个紫色核就证明T细胞身份。"}]},"answerEn":"A: Capillary endothelial cell; B: Tight junction; C: Macrophage; D: Epithelial reticular cell process; E: Thymocyte / developing T lymphocyte","answerZh":"A：毛细血管内皮细胞；B：紧密连接；C：巨噬细胞；D：上皮网状细胞突起；E：胸腺细胞／发育中的T淋巴细胞","explanationEn":"Use the described locations A–E. These letters are textual prompts, not additional arrows drawn on the source figure.","explanationZh":"按文字定位A–E识别。字母属于本题的文字提示，不代表原图新增了A–E箭头；原课件现有标注保留，用作识图练习。","printedPages":[149]},{"id":"09_immune-08","chapter":"09","type":"case","topic":"脾滤血、红细胞清除与感染防御","stemEn":"Practice case: A patient has anemia and splenomegaly. Examination shows increased uptake of poorly deformable erythrocytes by red-pulp macrophages. A clinician discusses the possible consequences of removing the spleen. Explain the following using splenic circulation and histology.","stemZh":"自编练习病例：一名患者贫血并有脾大。检查见红髓巨噬细胞对变形能力差的红细胞摄取增多。医生讨论切除脾后可能出现的后果。请从脾血液循环与组织结构解释。","subquestions":[{"promptEn":"Trace the open-circulation route from the splenic artery to the splenic vein and name the red-pulp compartments involved.","promptZh":"写出从脾动脉到脾静脉的开放循环路径，并指出涉及的红髓区域。","answerEn":"Splenic artery → trabecular arteries → central arterioles → penicillar arterioles and capillary endings → splenic cords → splenic sinusoids → trabecular veins → splenic vein. Splenic cords and sinusoids are the principal red-pulp compartments.","answerZh":"脾动脉→小梁动脉→中央小动脉→笔毛微动脉及毛细血管末端→脾索→脾血窦→小梁静脉→脾静脉。脾索与脾血窦是红髓的两个主要组成区域。","explanationEn":"In open circulation, blood leaves arterial endings for the splenic cords and re-enters sinusoids through endothelial slits. A minority of endings communicate directly with sinusoids, forming closed circulation. Some course diagrams also name pulp veins before trabecular veins; the fourth-edition text condenses this venous drainage.","explanationZh":"开放循环中血液先由动脉末端进入脾索，再经内皮狭缝回到脾血窦；少数末端直接与脾血窦相通，构成闭合循环。有些课程图在小梁静脉前另列髓静脉，本版正文将静脉回流概括书写，两者是详略差别。"},{"promptEn":"Explain why reduced erythrocyte deformability and increased macrophage activity may contribute to anemia.","promptZh":"说明红细胞变形能力下降及巨噬细胞活跃为何可能促成贫血。","answerEn":"Erythrocytes must deform to pass through narrow slits between sinusoidal endothelial cells. Poorly deformable cells are retained in the cords and phagocytosed. If erythrocyte destruction exceeds marrow replacement, extravascular hemolysis reduces erythrocyte numbers and hemoglobin, causing anemia.","answerZh":"红细胞需要变形，才能通过脾窦内皮细胞之间的狭缝。变形能力差的细胞滞留于脾索并被吞噬；若破坏超过骨髓补充，血管外溶血使红细胞数量及血红蛋白下降，导致贫血。","explanationEn":"Explain both the mechanical selection by the sinus wall and the cellular removal by macrophages. Do not state that every erythrocyte passing through the spleen is destroyed.","explanationZh":"应同时说明脾窦壁的机械筛选及巨噬细胞的吞噬清除，不能写成所有经过脾的红细胞都会被破坏。"},{"promptEn":"Why may removal of the spleen increase susceptibility to blood-borne infection?","promptZh":"切脾后为何可能更易发生血源性感染？","answerEn":"Splenectomy removes red-pulp macrophage clearance of circulating microbes and white-pulp/marginal-zone lymphocyte responses. It also removes an important site of B-cell-mediated antibody defense, so blood-borne microorganisms are cleared less effectively. As a clinical link, susceptibility is increased particularly for encapsulated bacteria such as Streptococcus pneumoniae.","answerZh":"切脾失去红髓巨噬细胞清除循环微生物，以及白髓和边缘区淋巴细胞应答的重要场所，同时削弱脾内B细胞相关抗体防御，因此血源性微生物更难被有效清除。临床联系：感染风险尤其涉及肺炎链球菌等有荚膜细菌。","explanationEn":"Mechanical trapping, macrophage phagocytosis and antigen-driven antibody responses provide complementary protection. The encapsulated-bacterium example is a clinical extension supported by CDC guidance; the fourth-edition spleen pages explain the underlying tissue functions.","explanationZh":"机械捕获、巨噬细胞吞噬和抗原驱动的抗体应答相互配合。有荚膜细菌的具体风险作为CDC支持的临床联系，教材脾章节提供基本组织功能依据。"}],"answerEn":"1. Splenic artery → trabecular arteries → central arterioles → penicillar arterioles and capillary endings → splenic cords → splenic sinusoids → trabecular veins → splenic vein. Splenic cords and sinusoids are the principal red-pulp compartments. 2. Erythrocytes must deform to pass through narrow slits between sinusoidal endothelial cells. Poorly deformable cells are retained in the cords and phagocytosed. If erythrocyte destruction exceeds marrow replacement, extravascular hemolysis reduces erythrocyte numbers and hemoglobin, causing anemia. 3. Splenectomy removes red-pulp macrophage clearance of circulating microbes and white-pulp/marginal-zone lymphocyte responses. It also removes an important site of B-cell-mediated antibody defense, so blood-borne microorganisms are cleared less effectively. As a clinical link, susceptibility is increased particularly for encapsulated bacteria such as Streptococcus pneumoniae.","answerZh":"1．脾动脉→小梁动脉→中央小动脉→笔毛微动脉及毛细血管末端→脾索→脾血窦→小梁静脉→脾静脉。脾索与脾血窦是红髓的两个主要组成区域。 2．红细胞需要变形，才能通过脾窦内皮细胞之间的狭缝。变形能力差的细胞滞留于脾索并被吞噬；若破坏超过骨髓补充，血管外溶血使红细胞数量及血红蛋白下降，导致贫血。 3．切脾失去红髓巨噬细胞清除循环微生物，以及白髓和边缘区淋巴细胞应答的重要场所，同时削弱脾内B细胞相关抗体防御，因此血源性微生物更难被有效清除。临床联系：感染风险尤其涉及肺炎链球菌等有荚膜细菌。","explanationEn":"Connect each observation to a histological structure and then to its function. Do not infer a specific disease from nonspecific findings alone.","explanationZh":"每小问按“病例线索—组织结构—功能后果”作答。病例用于解释结构与功能，不由单一非特异表现强行确诊某种疾病。","printedPages":[153,154,155]}],"textbook":[{"id":"textbook-methods-he-fundus","chapter":"01","page":6,"figure":"1-1","zh":"胃底黏膜的 H&E 染色","en":"H&E staining of the gastric fundus","promptZh":"图中偏蓝紫的区域和偏粉红的区域，各表现出什么染色性质？","promptEn":"What staining properties do the blue-purple and pink regions show?","answerZh":"蓝紫色为嗜碱性，粉红色为嗜酸性。","answerEn":"Blue-purple regions are basophilic, and pink regions are acidophilic (eosinophilic).","cueZh":"先区分蓝紫色核和周围胞质，再依据颜色描述。核酸丰富的区域常呈嗜碱性。","cueEn":"First distinguish the blue-purple nuclei from surrounding cytoplasm. Nucleic-acid-rich regions are typically basophilic.","image":"methods-he-fundus"},{"id":"textbook-methods-sem-respiratory","chapter":"01","page":11,"figure":"1-11","zh":"扫描电镜的呼吸道表面","en":"Respiratory surface on scanning electron microscopy","promptZh":"哪种显微镜显示了呼吸道表面凸起的立体形貌？","promptEn":"Which microscopy technique shows this three-dimensional relief of the respiratory surface?","answerZh":"扫描电镜（SEM）。","answerEn":"Scanning electron microscopy (SEM).","cueZh":"图中可沿表面追踪成簇的细长突起，明暗呈现表面起伏。","cueEn":"Trace clusters of fine projections across the surface. Their highlights and shadows show surface relief.","image":"methods-sem-respiratory"},{"id":"textbook-methods-tem-plasma","chapter":"01","page":11,"figure":"1-10","zh":"透射电镜的细胞内部","en":"Cell interior on transmission electron microscopy","promptZh":"这是透射电镜还是扫描电镜？图中深色区域反映什么性质？","promptEn":"Is this TEM or SEM? What property is represented by the dark regions?","answerZh":"透射电镜（TEM）；深色区域电子密度较高。","answerEn":"It is a transmission electron micrograph (TEM). Dark regions have higher electron density.","cueZh":"图中可见细胞内部截面及细胞器；灰阶来源于电子透过与散射形成的对比。","cueEn":"The section reveals internal cell structures and organelles. Its grayscale contrast reflects electron transmission and scattering.","image":"methods-tem-plasma"},{"id":"textbook-methods-pas-liver","chapter":"01","page":14,"figure":"1-15","zh":"肝细胞 PAS 反应","en":"PAS reaction in hepatocytes","promptZh":"这张教材图里，肝细胞内呈紫红色的颗粒是什么？","promptEn":"What are the magenta granules within the hepatocytes in this textbook image?","answerZh":"糖原颗粒，经 PAS 反应呈阳性。","answerEn":"They are glycogen granules, which are PAS-positive.","cueZh":"定位胞质中呈紫红色的颗粒，蓝紫色核来自苏木精复染。需要进一步确认糖原时，可结合淀粉酶消化对照。","cueEn":"Look for magenta cytoplasmic granules beside the hematoxylin-counterstained nuclei. A diastase digestion control can help confirm glycogen.","image":"methods-pas-liver"},{"id":"textbook-epithelia-renal-cuboidal","chapter":"02","page":25,"figure":"2-2 B","zh":"肾小管的单层立方上皮","en":"Simple cuboidal epithelium of renal tubules","promptZh":"沿一个清楚的肾小管管腔观察，衬里的上皮是哪一种？","promptEn":"What kind of epithelium lines a clearly visible renal tubule in this image?","answerZh":"单层立方上皮。","answerEn":"Simple cuboidal epithelium.","cueZh":"围绕同一管腔追踪一层细胞。细胞高度与宽度大致相当，核多为圆形。","cueEn":"Follow the single layer around one lumen. Cells are roughly as tall as they are wide and usually have round nuclei.","image":"epithelia-renal-cuboidal"},{"id":"textbook-epithelia-pseudostratified-cilia","chapter":"02","page":26,"figure":"2-4 B","zh":"假复层纤毛柱状上皮","en":"Pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium","promptZh":"上皮核分布在不同高度，游离面可见纤毛。应写出哪类上皮的全名？","promptEn":"What is the full name of the epithelium with nuclei at different heights and cilia on the free surface?","answerZh":"假复层纤毛柱状上皮。","answerEn":"Pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium.","cueZh":"先从有纤毛的一侧找到游离面，再观察核的高度。这个上皮的各类细胞都接触基膜，其中短细胞达不到腔面。","cueEn":"Use the ciliated edge to orient the free surface and inspect the staggered nuclei. All cells contact the basement membrane; shorter cells do not reach the lumen.","image":"epithelia-pseudostratified-cilia"},{"id":"textbook-epithelia-stratified-squamous","chapter":"02","page":27,"figure":"2-5 B","zh":"复层扁平上皮的表层","en":"Superficial layers of stratified squamous epithelium","promptZh":"为什么这层上皮命名为复层扁平上皮？图中是否见厚角化层？","promptEn":"How do the layers justify naming this stratified squamous epithelium? Is a thick keratin layer visible?","answerZh":"上皮有多层细胞，最表层细胞扁平并保留细胞核。图中未见厚角化层，属于非角化复层扁平上皮。","answerEn":"There are multiple cell layers, and the flattened superficial cells retain nuclei. No thick keratin layer is visible. This is nonkeratinized stratified squamous epithelium.","cueZh":"从基底侧向游离面追踪细胞形态。命名取决于表层形状，角化再看表面是否形成无核层。","cueEn":"Trace cell shape from the base to the free surface. The superficial shape gives the name, and a surface layer without nuclei helps identify keratinization.","image":"epithelia-stratified-squamous"},{"id":"textbook-epithelia-urothelium","chapter":"02","page":28,"figure":"2-6 B","zh":"膀胱变移上皮","en":"Urothelium of the bladder","promptZh":"游离面的一排大型穹隆状细胞叫什么？它们属于哪种上皮？","promptEn":"What are the large dome-shaped cells at the free surface, and which epithelium do they belong to?","answerZh":"伞细胞，位于变移上皮（尿路上皮）的表面。","answerEn":"They are umbrella cells on the surface of transitional epithelium, also called urothelium.","cueZh":"先找腔缘，再找宽大的表层细胞及下面的多层细胞。膀胱扩张时表层细胞可变扁。","cueEn":"Locate the luminal edge, then look for broad superficial cells over several layers. The superficial cells can flatten as the bladder distends.","image":"epithelia-urothelium"},{"id":"textbook-epithelia-intestinal-microvilli","chapter":"02","page":32,"figure":"2-14","zh":"小肠微绒毛与连接复合体","en":"Microvilli and junctional complex of the small intestine","promptZh":"顶端紧密并排的突起是什么？相邻上皮细胞的紧密连接位于何处？","promptEn":"Name the closely packed apical projections and locate the tight junction between neighboring epithelial cells.","answerZh":"突起是微绒毛；紧密连接位于相邻细胞侧面最靠近顶端的位置。","answerEn":"The projections are microvilli. The tight junction lies at the apical end of the lateral contact between adjacent cells.","cueZh":"先找游离面成排突起，再沿两个细胞之间的侧面接触向下看各连接层级。","cueEn":"First find the parallel projections at the free surface, then trace down the lateral contact between the two cells to compare the junctions.","image":"epithelia-intestinal-microvilli"},{"id":"textbook-connective-plasma-light","chapter":"03","page":41,"figure":"3-7 A","zh":"结缔组织里的浆细胞","en":"Plasma cells in connective tissue","promptZh":"箭头指的是什么细胞？写一个镜下辨认依据。","promptEn":"Identify the cells indicated by the arrows and give one visible clue.","answerZh":"浆细胞；可见偏心核，染色质沿核周呈粗块状分布。","answerEn":"Plasma cells. The eccentric nucleus has coarse blocks of peripheral chromatin.","cueZh":"在箭头附近先找偏心的圆形核，再看车轮状染色质及嗜碱性胞质，部分细胞可见核旁淡区。","cueEn":"Look near the arrows for an eccentric round nucleus, clock-face chromatin and basophilic cytoplasm. Some cells show a pale juxtanuclear area.","image":"connective-plasma-light"},{"id":"textbook-connective-mast-metachromasia","chapter":"03","page":44,"figure":"3-12","zh":"肥大细胞的异染颗粒","en":"Metachromatic granules of mast cells","promptZh":"图中胞质富含紫色颗粒的细胞是什么？颗粒体现什么染色现象？","promptEn":"Which cells have cytoplasm packed with purple granules, and what staining phenomenon do the granules demonstrate?","answerZh":"肥大细胞；甲苯胺蓝染色时颗粒呈异染性。","answerEn":"Mast cells. Their granules show metachromasia with toluidine blue.","cueZh":"关注胞质成群紫颗粒以及细胞位于结缔组织的背景。","cueEn":"Focus on the packed purple cytoplasmic granules and the connective-tissue setting.","image":"connective-mast-metachromasia"},{"id":"textbook-connective-collagen-elastic","chapter":"03","page":47,"figure":"3-17","zh":"胶原纤维与弹性纤维","en":"Collagen and elastic fibers","promptZh":"图中较粗的粉红波状纤维和较细分支的深色纤维分别是什么？","promptEn":"Identify the thicker pink wavy fibers and the thinner dark branching fibers.","answerZh":"较粗的粉红波状纤维为胶原纤维，较细分支的深色纤维为弹性纤维。","answerEn":"The thicker pink wavy fibers are collagen fibers. The thinner dark branching fibers are elastic fibers.","cueZh":"先比束的粗细及有无分支，再结合这张特殊染色提供的颜色差别。","cueEn":"Compare fiber thickness and branching first, then use the color contrast provided by this special stain.","image":"connective-collagen-elastic"},{"id":"textbook-connective-collagen-fibrils","chapter":"03","page":47,"figure":"3-18","zh":"胶原原纤维的周期横纹","en":"Periodic banding of collagen fibrils","promptZh":"电镜下呈规则周期横纹的是哪种结构？","promptEn":"Which structure shows the regularly spaced transverse bands in this electron micrograph?","answerZh":"胶原原纤维。教材本版所述的横纹周期约 67 nm。","answerEn":"Collagen fibrils. This textbook edition describes a banding repeat of approximately 67 nm.","cueZh":"沿一条细长原纤维的长轴，可见密度深浅交替的重复横带。","cueEn":"Follow the long axis of one fibril to see recurring alternating electron-dense and lighter bands.","image":"connective-collagen-fibrils"},{"id":"textbook-connective-reticular-silver","chapter":"03","page":48,"figure":"3-20","zh":"网状纤维的银染","en":"Silver-stained reticular fibers","promptZh":"细而深染、分支连成网的纤维是什么？主要胶原类型是什么？","promptEn":"Identify the fine dark branching fibers forming a network and name their principal collagen type.","answerZh":"网状纤维，主要由Ⅲ型胶原组成。","answerEn":"Reticular fibers, composed primarily of type III collagen.","cueZh":"在银染图里追踪细线的分支和网孔，网状纤维在这里呈深色。","cueEn":"Trace the branches and spaces in the mesh. Reticular fibers stain dark in this silver preparation.","image":"connective-reticular-silver"},{"id":"textbook-connective-tendon-cut-planes","chapter":"03","page":50,"figure":"3-23","zh":"肌腱的纵切与横切","en":"Longitudinal and transverse sections of tendon","promptZh":"两图属于哪种结缔组织？哪张是纵切？","promptEn":"What type of connective tissue is shown in both panels, and which panel is longitudinal?","answerZh":"致密规则结缔组织（肌腱）；左图 A 为纵切，右图 B 为横切。","answerEn":"Dense regular connective tissue (tendon). A on the left is longitudinal and B on the right is transverse.","cueZh":"左图胶原束呈长条、平行排列，细长核顺着纤维束排列；右图可见短小的纤维束横断面。","cueEn":"In A, long parallel collagen bundles are accompanied by elongated nuclei. In B, the bundles are cut across.","image":"connective-tendon-cut-planes"},{"id":"textbook-hyaline-cartilage-groups","chapter":"04","page":54,"figure":"4-1","zh":"透明软骨：软骨膜、陷窝和同源细胞群","en":"Hyaline cartilage: perichondrium, lacunae and isogenous groups","promptZh":"识别这类软骨。A 图表面标注 P 的薄层和 B 图标注 IG 的细胞群分别是什么？","promptEn":"Identify the cartilage. What are the surface layer marked P in panel A and the cell groups marked IG in panel B?","answerZh":"透明软骨。P 是软骨膜，IG 是同源细胞群。","answerEn":"Hyaline cartilage. P is the perichondrium and IG marks isogenous groups of chondrocytes.","cueZh":"先看浅染、均质的基质，再看陷窝中的软骨细胞。浅层细胞较扁，深部可见几个相邻细胞聚成一群。软骨膜在基质外侧。","cueEn":"Start with the pale, relatively homogeneous matrix and identify chondrocytes in lacunae. The superficial cells are flatter, and deeper cells occur in clusters. The perichondrium lies at the outer surface.","image":"hyaline-cartilage-groups"},{"id":"textbook-osteoclast-bone-surface","chapter":"04","page":60,"figure":"4-11","zh":"骨表面的破骨细胞","en":"Osteoclasts on bone surfaces","promptZh":"黑箭头所指是什么细胞？描述位置和细胞核特征，说明判断依据。","promptEn":"Identify the cells indicated by the black arrows. Give one positional and one nuclear clue.","answerZh":"破骨细胞。它们位于骨表面，可见胞体大，同一胞质内有多个细胞核。","answerEn":"Osteoclasts. They lie against bone surfaces and are large cells with multiple nuclei in a shared cytoplasm.","cueZh":"先沿骨小梁边缘寻找贴在表面的细胞，再观察胞体范围。多个核应当落在同一个大细胞内；附近拥挤的骨髓细胞各有自己的胞体。","cueEn":"Follow the trabecular surface before tracing the boundary of the large cell. The nuclei must share a single cytoplasm. Crowded marrow cells nearby have separate cell bodies.","image":"osteoclast-bone-surface"},{"id":"textbook-osteon-ground-section","chapter":"04","page":63,"figure":"4-15","zh":"骨单位：脱钙切片与骨磨片","en":"Osteon: decalcified bone and ground section","promptZh":"两幅图中的 C 是同一个什么结构？B 图中 BL 指的小腔与 BC 指的细线分别是什么？","promptEn":"What structure is marked C in both panels? Identify the small spaces marked BL and the fine lines marked BC in panel B.","answerZh":"C 是中央管（哈弗斯管），BL 是骨陷窝，BC 是骨小管。","answerEn":"C is the central (Haversian) canal, BL marks bone lacunae, and BC marks bone canaliculi.","cueZh":"以同心骨板为参照找中央管。骨陷窝是骨板间的小腔，细小的骨小管从陷窝向外放射并与邻近陷窝相通。中央管和整个骨单位是两个不同层级。","cueEn":"Find the central canal by tracing the concentric lamellae. Lacunae are small spaces between lamellae, and canaliculi radiate from them. The canal forms only the centre of the osteon.","image":"osteon-ground-section"},{"id":"textbook-epiphyseal-growth-plate","chapter":"04","page":66,"figure":"4-19","zh":"骺板五区：从软骨细胞排列到成骨","en":"Growth plate: five histological zones","promptZh":"从图上方到下方写出骺板的五区。小软骨细胞排成长列和细胞明显肥大分别对应哪一区？","promptEn":"Name the five growth-plate zones from top to bottom. Which zones contain columns of small chondrocytes and markedly enlarged chondrocytes, respectively?","answerZh":"软骨贮备区、软骨增生区、软骨成熟区（肥大区）、软骨钙化区、成骨区。小细胞纵列见于增生区，肥大的细胞见于成熟区。","answerEn":"Resting, proliferating, maturing (hypertrophic), calcifying, and ossifying zones. Columns of small cells characterize the proliferating zone; enlarged cells characterize the maturing zone.","cueZh":"沿图从上往下依次找散在的小细胞、纵向细胞柱、扩大的陷窝、钙化软骨残留和靠近骨髓的骨小梁。单个结构不清楚时，用相邻带的位置来判断。","cueEn":"Follow scattered small cells, longitudinal columns, enlarged lacunae, calcified cartilage remnants, and trabeculae near marrow. Use neighbouring zones to orient uncertain boundaries.","image":"epiphyseal-growth-plate"},{"id":"textbook-skeletal-muscle-two-planes","chapter":"05","page":84,"figure":"6-2","zh":"骨骼肌：纵切与横切对照","en":"Skeletal muscle: longitudinal and transverse sections","promptZh":"A 和 B 各是什么切面？从横纹、纤维轮廓和核的位置中选两个线索，说明两图属于同一种肌组织。","promptEn":"Which section plane is shown in A and B? Use any two clues from striation, fibre outline, and nuclear position to identify the muscle type.","answerZh":"两图均为骨骼肌。A 是纵切，见平行的长肌纤维和横纹。B 是横切，见多边形肌纤维轮廓，核可位于纤维边缘。","answerEn":"Both show skeletal muscle. A is longitudinal and shows long parallel, striated fibres. B is transverse and shows polygonal profiles with nuclei at the fibre periphery when present.","cueZh":"纵切时核可在长纤维的边缘看到，视野内也可能有纤维之间的结缔组织核。横切时尽量选一根轮廓完整的纤维，先定轮廓再判断核的位置。","cueEn":"In the longitudinal section, distinguish peripheral muscle nuclei from connective-tissue nuclei between fibres. In cross-section, trace a complete fibre outline before deciding whether a nucleus is peripheral.","image":"skeletal-muscle-two-planes"},{"id":"textbook-skeletal-sarcomere-tem","chapter":"05","page":85,"figure":"6-3","zh":"骨骼肌电镜：Z 线、M 线与肌节","en":"Skeletal muscle TEM: Z lines, M lines and sarcomeres","promptZh":"一个肌节的两端是什么线？本图的白色三角标记所指的线和白色长箭头所指的肌丝分别是什么？","promptEn":"Which lines bound a sarcomere? What do the white arrowheads and the white arrows indicate, respectively?","answerZh":"相邻两条 Z 线之间为一个肌节。白色三角标记指 M 线，白色长箭头指粗肌丝。","answerEn":"A sarcomere extends between two adjacent Z lines. White arrowheads indicate M lines; white arrows indicate thick myofilaments.","cueZh":"先沿同一排肌原纤维找相邻两个深色 Z 线，再认居中的 M 线。A 带覆盖粗肌丝长度，I 带只有细肌丝，H 带只有粗肌丝。","cueEn":"Locate two Z lines along the same myofibril before finding the central M line. The A band spans the thick filaments, the I band has thin filaments only, and the H zone has thick filaments only.","image":"skeletal-sarcomere-tem"},{"id":"textbook-cardiac-muscle-two-planes","chapter":"05","page":89,"figure":"6-7","zh":"心肌：从两种切面定位中央核","en":"Cardiac muscle: central nuclei in two planes","promptZh":"这是什么肌组织？在 A 图找肌细胞核，说明为什么 B 图有些横切轮廓见不到核。","promptEn":"Identify this muscle type. Locate the myocyte nuclei in panel A and explain why some profiles in panel B lack a visible nucleus.","answerZh":"心肌。A 图的心肌细胞核位于细胞中央。B 图有些切面未经过细胞核所在高度，因此可见无核的肌纤维轮廓。","answerEn":"Cardiac muscle. Myocyte nuclei are centrally located in panel A. Some profiles in panel B miss the level of the cell nucleus.","cueZh":"在纵切中沿粉红色肌细胞找位于细胞内的卵圆核，再用横纹和不规则、可分支的形态辅助判断。间隙中的小深染核可来自间质细胞。","cueEn":"In the longitudinal section, look for an oval nucleus within a pink myocyte, then check for striations and irregular or branching fibre profiles. Small nuclei in the spaces between myocytes may belong to interstitial cells.","image":"cardiac-muscle-two-planes"},{"id":"textbook-smooth-muscle-two-planes","chapter":"05","page":91,"figure":"6-11","zh":"平滑肌：纵切长核与横切大小不等","en":"Smooth muscle: elongated nuclei and variable cross-sectional profiles","promptZh":"两图属于什么肌组织？为什么 B 图细胞横切面大小不等，有些可见核而有些看不到？","promptEn":"Identify the muscle in both panels. Why do profiles in panel B differ in size, and why do only some contain visible nuclei?","answerZh":"平滑肌。梭形细胞中段宽、两端窄，横切不同位置可见不同大小的轮廓；只有切到中部核所在位置才能看到核。","answerEn":"Smooth muscle. Spindle-shaped cells are wider in the middle than at the ends, so different section levels give profiles of different sizes. A nucleus is visible only when the section passes through it.","cueZh":"先用 A 图辨认长形中央核及没有规则横纹的肌束，再用梭形细胞三维形状解释 B 图的大小变化。横切偶尔见不到核只是切面效应。","cueEn":"In panel A, look for elongated central nuclei and bundles without regular cross-striations. Use the three-dimensional spindle shape to interpret the variable profiles in panel B.","image":"smooth-muscle-two-planes"},{"id":"textbook-peripheral-blood-smear-cells","chapter":"06","page":71,"figure":"5-5","zh":"血涂片：五类白细胞与红细胞、血小板","en":"Blood smear: five leukocyte types, erythrocytes and platelets","promptZh":"分别写出图中 1–7 所示血细胞或血小板的英文。2 的两个细胞核形不同，为什么仍是同一类？","promptEn":"Identify the formed elements numbered 1–7. Why do the two profiles numbered 2 belong to the same cell type despite their different nuclear shapes?","answerZh":"1 红细胞，2 中性粒细胞，3 嗜酸性粒细胞，4 嗜碱性粒细胞，5 单核细胞，6 淋巴细胞，7 血小板。2 分别表示杆状核和分叶核的中性粒细胞。","answerEn":"1 erythrocyte; 2 neutrophil; 3 eosinophil; 4 basophil; 5 monocyte; 6 lymphocyte; 7 platelet. The two neutrophils show band-shaped and segmented nuclei.","cueZh":"先用红细胞作大小参照，再对比核形与颗粒。嗜酸性粒细胞常见双叶核和粗红颗粒，嗜碱性粒细胞深色颗粒可遮住核。单核细胞核有凹陷，淋巴细胞核圆且胞质较少。","cueEn":"Use erythrocytes as a size reference, then compare nuclear shape and granules. Eosinophils often have bilobed nuclei and coarse red granules. Dark basophil granules can obscure the nucleus. Monocytes have indented nuclei; lymphocytes typically have round nuclei and scant cytoplasm.","image":"peripheral-blood-smear-cells"},{"id":"textbook-reticulocyte-smear","chapter":"06","page":72,"figure":"5-6","zh":"网织红细胞：活体染色显示残余 RNA","en":"Reticulocytes: residual RNA in supravital stain","promptZh":"箭头所指是什么细胞？细胞内深色的网状物由什么成分形成？","promptEn":"What cells do the arrows indicate? What forms the dark reticulum inside them?","answerZh":"网织红细胞。胞质中的残余核糖体 RNA 经活体染色呈深色网状或颗粒状。","answerEn":"Reticulocytes. Residual ribosomal RNA in the cytoplasm forms a dark reticular or granular pattern after supravital staining.","cueZh":"把箭头所指细胞与周围大小相近的红细胞作对照。深色成分呈不规则网状或成簇颗粒，无单独成形的细胞核。","cueEn":"Compare the arrowed cells with the similarly sized erythrocytes around them. The dark material forms an irregular network or clusters of granules rather than a discrete nucleus.","image":"reticulocyte-smear"},{"id":"textbook-granulocyte-ultrastructure","chapter":"06","page":74,"figure":"5-7","zh":"粒细胞电镜：颗粒与结晶样核心","en":"Granulocyte TEM: granules and crystalloid cores","promptZh":"A、B、C 各是哪种粒细胞？带结晶样核心的颗粒在哪一图？","promptEn":"Identify the granulocytes in A, B and C. Which panel shows granules with crystalloid cores?","answerZh":"A 为中性粒细胞，B 为嗜酸性粒细胞，C 为嗜碱性粒细胞。结晶样核心在 B 的嗜酸性特殊颗粒内。","answerEn":"A is a neutrophil, B an eosinophil, and C a basophil. The crystalloid cores are in the specific granules of the eosinophil in B.","cueZh":"A 图区分分叶的核和两类胞质颗粒；B 图看大颗粒内的深色结晶样核心；C 图看粗大的电子致密颗粒。这里的深浅表示电子密度。","cueEn":"In A, distinguish nuclear lobes from the cytoplasmic granules. In B, look for a dense crystalloid core within a large granule. In C, look for coarse electron-dense granules. Contrast here reflects electron density.","image":"granulocyte-ultrastructure"},{"id":"textbook-red-marrow-megakaryocyte","chapter":"06","page":77,"figure":"5-10","zh":"红骨髓：巨核细胞与幼红细胞岛","en":"Red marrow: megakaryocytes and erythroblastic islets","promptZh":"图中右上方的大细胞和右下方成团分布的结构各是什么？哪一个与血小板形成有关？","promptEn":"Identify the large cell toward the top right and the cell cluster marked below it. Which is associated with platelet formation?","answerZh":"右上方是巨核细胞，右下方所标的是幼红细胞岛。巨核细胞的胞质形成血小板。","answerEn":"The large cell is a megakaryocyte and the cluster below it is an erythroblastic islet. Platelets arise from megakaryocyte cytoplasm.","cueZh":"巨核细胞从周围密集的小造血细胞中凸显：胞体很大、核分叶。幼红细胞岛中的幼红细胞聚集分布。区别单个大细胞与细胞群。","cueEn":"The megakaryocyte stands out from small neighbouring hematopoietic cells by its large body and lobulated nucleus. An erythroblastic islet appears as a cluster of erythroid precursors.","image":"red-marrow-megakaryocyte"},{"id":"textbook-motor-neuron-nissl","chapter":"07","page":95,"figure":"7-3","zh":"运动神经元与尼氏体","en":"Motor neuron and Nissl bodies","promptZh":"白箭所指的嗜碱性团块叫什么？发出轴突的轴丘有没有同类团块？","promptEn":"Name the basophilic clumps indicated by white arrows. Are these clumps present in the axon hillock?","answerZh":"尼氏体，结构基础为粗面内质网与游离核糖体。轴丘缺乏可见的尼氏体。","answerEn":"Nissl bodies, composed of rough endoplasmic reticulum and free ribosomes. The axon hillock lacks visible Nissl bodies.","cueZh":"找有明显细胞核的大胞体，再看核外紫蓝色胞质团块。轴丘在胞体逐渐收窄、发出轴突的一侧，通常浅染。","cueEn":"Find the large soma, then locate the purple-blue clumps outside its nucleus. The axon hillock is the pale taper from which the axon emerges.","image":"motor-neuron-nissl"},{"id":"textbook-chemical-synapse-vesicles","chapter":"07","page":101,"figure":"7-11","zh":"化学突触的透射电镜像","en":"Chemical synapses on TEM","promptZh":"密集的小圆囊称为什么？由此判断它们在哪一侧。","promptEn":"What are the clustered round profiles, and which side of the synapse contains them?","answerZh":"突触小泡，集中在突触前末梢。两侧之间可见窄的突触间隙。","answerEn":"Synaptic vesicles clustered in the presynaptic terminal. A narrow synaptic cleft separates it from the postsynaptic element.","cueZh":"先找贴着细胞膜的一簇小泡，再沿膜找突触间隙，并与对侧贴膜的突触后致密物对照。","cueEn":"Find the cluster of vesicles adjacent to the membrane, follow the narrow cleft, and compare the dense specialization on the opposite membrane.","image":"chemical-synapse-vesicles"},{"id":"textbook-myelinated-axon-node","chapter":"07","page":107,"figure":"7-19","zh":"髓鞘横切与郎飞结纵切","en":"Myelin cross-section and node of Ranvier","promptZh":"左图包绕轴突的深色厚环是什么？右图两段深色结构之间的中断叫什么？","promptEn":"Name the dark ring around the axon at left and the interruption between the two myelin segments at right.","answerZh":"左为髓鞘，右为郎飞结。","answerEn":"Myelin sheath at left and a node of Ranvier at right.","cueZh":"左图先找中央浅色的轴突（Ax），外侧深环是层叠的髓鞘。右图追踪纵行轴突，可见髓鞘在节点处终止又重新出现。","cueEn":"At left the pale axoplasm marked Ax is enclosed by lamellar myelin. At right follow the longitudinal axon where the sheath ends and begins again.","image":"myelinated-axon-node"},{"id":"textbook-cutaneous-corpuscle-pair","chapter":"07","page":112,"figure":"7-25","zh":"触觉小体与环层小体","en":"Tactile and lamellar corpuscles","promptZh":"比较A、B两图，哪一个位于真皮乳头，哪一个形成洋葱样板层？","promptEn":"Compare panels A and B. Which corpuscle lies in a dermal papilla, and which has onion-like lamellae?","answerZh":"A 是触觉小体（Meissner 小体），B 是环层小体（Pacinian 小体）。","answerEn":"A is a tactile (Meissner) corpuscle. B is a lamellar (Pacinian) corpuscle.","cueZh":"A 靠近表皮，体积小而呈卵圆形；B 的中央有轴心，外面是反复包绕的同心板层。","cueEn":"A is small and ovoid near the epidermis. B has a central core surrounded by repeated concentric lamellae.","image":"cutaneous-corpuscle-pair"},{"id":"textbook-muscular-artery-wall","chapter":"08","page":130,"figure":"9-3","zh":"中动脉壁的三层","en":"Three layers of a muscular artery","promptZh":"靠腔的一条明显深染波浪线是什么？它把哪两层分开？","promptEn":"What is the prominent dark wavy line near the lumen, and which two layers does it separate?","answerZh":"内弹性膜，位于内膜与中膜交界。","answerEn":"The internal elastic lamina, at the boundary between the tunica intima and tunica media.","cueZh":"从管腔向外追踪内皮与内皮下层，遇到波浪状弹性膜后是以平滑肌为主的厚中膜。再往外才是结缔组织较多的外膜。","cueEn":"Trace outward from the endothelium and subendothelial layer. Beyond the wavy elastic lamina lies a thick smooth-muscle media, followed by the connective-tissue adventitia.","image":"muscular-artery-wall"},{"id":"textbook-elastic-artery-lamellae","chapter":"08","page":131,"figure":"9-4","zh":"大动脉中膜的弹性板层","en":"Elastic lamellae in a large artery","promptZh":"C 图特殊染色显示中膜内一层又一层的波纹是什么？它支持判定哪类动脉？","promptEn":"What are the repeated wavy layers in the specially stained tunica media in C, and which class of artery do they identify?","answerZh":"多层弹性膜，提示大动脉，即弹性动脉。","answerEn":"Numerous elastic lamellae, characteristic of a large elastic artery.","cueZh":"观察波浪线在中膜厚度内反复出现。中动脉更容易见到一条突出的内弹性膜，中膜以平滑肌为主。","cueEn":"The wavy layers repeat through the thickness of the media. A muscular artery has a smooth-muscle-dominant media and often a conspicuous internal elastic lamina.","image":"elastic-artery-lamellae"},{"id":"textbook-capillary-ultrastructure","chapter":"08","page":136,"figure":"9-14","zh":"三类毛细血管的电镜辨认","en":"Ultrastructure of three capillary types","promptZh":"A、B各是什么类型的毛细血管？D 图的 Sp 标记是什么？","promptEn":"Identify the capillary types in A and B. What does Sp label in panel D?","answerZh":"A 为连续毛细血管，B 为有孔毛细血管。D 示脾血窦，Sp 为内皮细胞之间的间隙。","answerEn":"A is a continuous capillary, and B is a fenestrated capillary. D shows a splenic sinusoid; Sp marks an interendothelial space.","cueZh":"沿 A、B 的管腔追踪变薄的内皮：B 的三角形标有孔处。D 看的是相邻内皮细胞之间的间隙，不能把细胞间隙当作单个细胞上的窗孔。","cueEn":"Trace the attenuated endothelium around the lumina of A and B. The triangle in B marks a fenestra. D shows spaces between adjacent endothelial cells, a different scale of opening.","image":"capillary-ultrastructure"},{"id":"textbook-microcirculation-routes","chapter":"08","page":139,"figure":"9-18","zh":"微循环的三条通路","en":"Three microcirculatory routes","promptZh":"从左侧微动脉到右侧微静脉，主要进行物质交换的通路经过什么结构？最下方绕开毛细血管网的红蓝连线是什么？","promptEn":"Which vessels carry the major exchange route from arteriole to venule? What is the direct lower connection that bypasses the capillary bed?","answerZh":"交换通路经过真毛细血管网。最下方为动静脉吻合。","answerEn":"The exchange route passes through the true capillary bed. The direct lower route is an arteriovenous anastomosis.","cueZh":"先按红到蓝定血流方向，再区分分支丰富的网、近直行的通血毛细血管与下方独立的吻合。","cueEn":"Orient from red to blue. Distinguish the branching network, the more direct thoroughfare channel, and the separate lower anastomosis.","image":"microcirculation-routes"},{"id":"textbook-heart-wall-purkinje","chapter":"08","page":140,"figure":"9-20","zh":"心壁与浦肯野纤维","en":"Heart wall and Purkinje fibers","promptZh":"A 图 P 指向什么，位于心壁哪一侧？B 图的脂肪细胞帮助定位哪一层？","promptEn":"What does P indicate in A, and on which side of the heart wall is it found? Which layer is suggested by the fat cells in B?","answerZh":"P 为浦肯野纤维，位于靠腔面的心内膜下层。B 图脂肪位于外侧的心外膜结缔组织内。","answerEn":"P marks Purkinje fibers in the subendocardial region on the luminal side. The fat cells in B are in connective tissue of the epicardium.","cueZh":"浦肯野纤维比邻近工作心肌细胞显得浅而宽。外侧的脂肪位于心肌之外，结合表面间皮定位。","cueEn":"Purkinje fibers appear wider and paler than working myocardium. The fat is external to the myocardium; the surface mesothelium helps locate the epicardium.","image":"heart-wall-purkinje"},{"id":"textbook-thymus-lobules-corpuscles","chapter":"09","page":148,"figure":"10-3","zh":"胸腺小叶与胸腺小体","en":"Thymic lobules and Hassall corpuscles","promptZh":"A 图的小叶如何分出皮质与髓质？B 图的同心圆样结构是什么？","promptEn":"How do you distinguish cortex from medulla in A? What is the concentrically arranged structure in B?","answerZh":"胸腺小叶外周为深染皮质，中央为浅染髓质。B 示髓质内的胸腺小体。","answerEn":"Each lobule has a darker peripheral cortex and a paler central medulla. B shows a thymic (Hassall) corpuscle in the medulla.","cueZh":"先沿结缔组织间隔找到相邻小叶，再看每叶的外深内浅。遇到层层同心排列的上皮性结构时定位在髓质。","cueEn":"Use connective-tissue septa to locate adjacent lobules. The peripheral cortex is dark, and the concentric epithelial whorl is in the lighter medulla.","image":"thymus-lobules-corpuscles"},{"id":"textbook-blood-thymus-barrier","chapter":"09","page":149,"figure":"10-5","zh":"血胸腺屏障的层次","en":"Layers of the blood–thymus barrier","promptZh":"从毛细血管腔向胸腺皮质淋巴细胞，由内向外说出组成屏障的五层。","promptEn":"List the five layers of the barrier from the capillary lumen toward lymphocytes in the thymic cortex.","answerZh":"有紧密连接的连续毛细血管内皮、内皮基膜、含巨噬细胞的血管周隙、上皮基膜、有紧密连接的上皮网状细胞鞘。","answerEn":"Continuous capillary endothelium with tight junctions, endothelial basal lamina, perivascular space containing macrophages, epithelial basal lamina, and a sheath of epithelial reticular cells with tight junctions.","cueZh":"先从白色管腔向外读图。分别找血管侧与上皮侧的两层基膜，中间的血管周隙可见巨噬细胞。","cueEn":"Start in the pale lumen and trace outward. Identify both basal laminae and the macrophage-containing compartment between them.","image":"blood-thymus-barrier"},{"id":"textbook-lymph-node-low-power","chapter":"09","page":150,"figure":"10-6","zh":"低倍定位淋巴结","en":"Lymph node at low power","promptZh":"这是什么器官？找出外周的淋巴小结和凹陷的门部。","promptEn":"Identify this organ. Locate the peripheral lymphoid nodules and its indented hilum.","answerZh":"淋巴结；淋巴小结在被膜下的浅层皮质，右侧箭头示淋巴结门。","answerEn":"A lymph node. Lymphoid nodules occupy the superficial cortex beneath the capsule. The arrow on the right indicates the hilum.","cueZh":"沿边缘找被膜与浅层皮质的圆形小结，再从边缘向内追踪较浅、分支样的髓质；图右缘凹陷形成门。","cueEn":"Find the capsule and round cortical nodules at the periphery, then follow the paler branching medulla inward. The indentation on the right is the hilum.","image":"lymph-node-low-power"},{"id":"textbook-lymph-node-hev","chapter":"09","page":151,"figure":"10-7","zh":"淋巴结副皮质和高内皮微静脉","en":"Paracortex and high endothelial venule","promptZh":"B/C所示的毛细血管后微静脉是哪种特化血管？它帮助哪类细胞从血液进入淋巴结？","promptEn":"What specialized postcapillary venule is shown in B/C, and which cells use it to enter the lymph node from blood?","answerZh":"高内皮微静脉（HEV），是循环淋巴细胞从血液进入淋巴结实质的入口。","answerEn":"A high endothelial venule (HEV), through which circulating lymphocytes enter the lymph node parenchyma from blood.","cueZh":"先定位富含T细胞的副皮质，再看血管管腔一圈饱满的内皮，和一般薄扁平的内皮区别。","cueEn":"Locate the T-cell-rich paracortex first. The plump endothelial cells lining the venule contrast with the thin flattened endothelium typical of ordinary vessels.","image":"lymph-node-hev"},{"id":"textbook-lymph-node-medullary-pattern","chapter":"09","page":151,"figure":"10-8","zh":"淋巴结髓索与髓窦","en":"Medullary cords and sinuses","promptZh":"三角与星号各指哪一结构？哪一个是淋巴流动的通道？","promptEn":"What do the triangles and asterisks indicate, respectively? Which is a channel for lymph flow?","answerZh":"三角示髓索，星号示髓窦。髓窦是淋巴流过的通道。","answerEn":"Triangles mark medullary cords, and asterisks mark medullary sinuses. Lymph flows through the sinuses.","cueZh":"细胞密集、深染的条带是索；它们之间较浅、细胞较少的间隙是窦。","cueEn":"The cords are dark, cell-rich bands. The sinuses are the paler, less densely cellular spaces between them.","image":"lymph-node-medullary-pattern"},{"id":"textbook-spleen-white-red-pulp","chapter":"09","page":153,"figure":"10-12","zh":"脾白髓与红髓","en":"White and red pulp of the spleen","promptZh":"A 图 CA 周围的深染淋巴组织叫什么？B 图 SC 与 SS 分别是什么？","promptEn":"What is the dark lymphoid tissue around CA in A? Identify SC and SS in B.","answerZh":"A 图是中央动脉周围淋巴鞘。B 图 SC 为脾索，SS 为脾血窦。","answerEn":"A shows the periarteriolar lymphoid sheath (also called the periarterial lymphatic sheath, PALS) around the central arteriole. SC is a splenic cord, and SS is a splenic sinusoid.","cueZh":"白髓先找中央动脉，再看紧贴血管的淋巴鞘和偏在一旁的淋巴小结；红髓先分开细胞密集的脾索与相邻窦腔。","cueEn":"In white pulp, follow the central arteriole and distinguish its sheath from the adjacent lymphoid nodule. In red pulp, separate the cell-rich cord from the adjoining sinusoidal lumen.","image":"spleen-white-red-pulp"},{"id":"textbook-palatine-tonsil-crypt","chapter":"09","page":155,"figure":"10-14","zh":"腭扁桃体的隐窝","en":"Crypt of the palatine tonsil","promptZh":"箭头所指的上皮内陷叫什么？与周围哪些结构合起来支持判断为腭扁桃体？","promptEn":"Name the epithelial invagination indicated by the arrow. Which nearby structures support identification as a palatine tonsil?","answerZh":"扁桃体隐窝。表面及隐窝的复层扁平上皮，加上邻近的淋巴小结，是腭扁桃体的特征组合。","answerEn":"A tonsillar crypt. Stratified squamous epithelium lining the surface and crypt, together with nearby lymphoid nodules, supports identification of the palatine tonsil.","cueZh":"从图右侧表面沿上皮追入空隙，确认它与表面连续；再找上皮下成团的淋巴小结。","cueEn":"Follow the epithelium from the surface on the right into the space to confirm continuity, then locate the underlying lymphoid nodules.","image":"palatine-tonsil-crypt"}]};
